(47,'ilan-47','tablo','yayinda','Fran Larsen ''The Village Path'' Watercolour, Hand Carved Polychrome Frame, 1996','FRAN LARSEN ''The Village Path'', 1996. Watercolour on Strathmore Crescent board, glazed with acrylic gloss medium and varnish, in a hand carved and painted polychrome frame. Titled and catalogued F 9701-006 on the label to the reverse. Framed size 21.5 by 26 inches.','Fran Larsen','The Village Path','1996','Watercolor in hand carved and painted polychrome frame','','F 9701-006','','','','','','IMG_7744',21.5,26,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Gold", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(48,'ilan-48','tablo','yayinda','Salvador Dalí ''Piccarda Donati'' Signed Print with Certificate of Authenticity','SALVADOR DALI (Spanish, 1904-1989) ''Piccarda Donati''. Print in colours, pencil signed lower right with edition notation lower left. Certificate of authenticity affixed to the reverse. Presented with a burgundy fillet mat in a gilt rope-twist frame under glass.','Salvador Dalí','Piccarda Donati','','','','','','','','','Certificate of Authenticity','IMG_7752',22.25,26.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": [], "medium": ["print"], "style": ["surrealist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["White", "Brown", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(49,'ilan-49','tablo','yayinda','Sunflower Still Life Oil on Canvas Signed Legas, Carved Gold Frame','LEGAS (Hungarian). Still life of yellow sunflowers in a vase, oil on canvas, signed lower right. Stretcher label ''Section No. 907-C-7, Finish Ref. 20" x 24", Made in Belgium''. Handwritten note to the reverse. Presented in a carved baroque gold frame.','Legas','','','','','','','','','Hungarian artist','','IMG_7756, IMG_7759, IMG_7760',28.25,33.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "", "color": ["Brown", "Gold", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(50,'ilan-50','tablo','yayinda','Impasto Night Road with Cypress and Star, Signed, Unframed','A thickly loaded impasto canvas after Van Gogh''s road with cypress: a dark green cypress twists up the centre of the picture, flanked by a huge swirling white and yellow star at the upper left and a small crescent moon at the upper right. Golden wheat fields press in from both sides in slabs of orange, chrome yellow and green, and a pale road sweeps down to the foreground where two small figures in blue and ochre walk towards the viewer. The paint is applied in ridges several millimetres proud of the surface, catching the light along every stroke. The canvas is gallery-wrapped with the image continued over the edges and is unframed. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas. Condition: Paint surface intact with pronounced impasto ridges; no cracking, flaking or losses visible. Canvas edges clean.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A001; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8382, IMG_8384, IMG_8385; The dark cursive signature at the lower right is not legible in this listing''s photographs; a clearer detail appears as IMG_8383 in listing A002, where it reads approximately ''C. S. Snead''. This is a copy or homage after Van Gogh''s ''Road with Cypress and Star'', not an original composition. Listing A002 contains no separate artwork and appears to be further photographs of this same canvas. Merged with former listing A002 (same work).','No certificate photographed.','IMG_8381',20.0,24.2,'canvas',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Yellow", "Orange", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(51,'ilan-51','tablo','yayinda','Sunlit Courtyard with Flowering Vines, Unframed','A warm, palette-knife landscape of a stone cottage whose facade is smothered in scarlet and gold climbing blossom, a blue-shuttered door and window at its centre. A small round table with two chairs sits in the dappled shade at the foot of the wall, while a broad path of cream and yellow strokes leads the eye past banks of red, white and yellow flowers to a pale distant house and misty hills. The paint is applied in short, loaded strokes with visible knife ridges, giving the whole surface a glittering broken texture. The canvas is gallery-wrapped and unframed. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: Thick knife-applied paint intact with no cracking or losses; canvas edges clean and painted over. No visible damage.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A003; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8388, IMG_8389; No signature could be found along the lower edge in either the full view or the angled detail; a signature may lie under the tape or on the reverse, which was not photographed. No title, label or stamp appears anywhere in the set.','No certificate photographed.','IMG_8386',30.0,30.0,'canvas',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture", "still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Gold", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(52,'ilan-52','tablo','yayinda','Molten Orange Abstract Harbour Landscape, Signed, Framed','A square canvas saturated in molten yellow and orange, worked with an extremely heavy granular impasto that catches light across the whole surface. A horizon band of crimson and maroon runs across the upper third, broken by quick dark-green and black calligraphic strokes suggesting distant boats, masts or trees. In the lower half two blunt oxblood-red vertical forms - a bollard and a pillar - anchor the composition, their shadows dragged forward into the orange ground. Handling is thick, dry and heavily loaded, applied with knife and stiff brush rather than blended. Medium: oil on canvas, heavy impasto. Signed lower right, on the orange ground beside the red pillar. Condition: no visible damage; impasto crests intact, no craquelure or losses seen. Some photographic glare off the raised paint.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, heavy impasto','','','','','','katalog A004; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8393, IMG_8394, IMG_8395; The signature at lower right is a fast dark cursive flourish and is not legible at 900px; no name is offered. Subject reading (harbour/landscape) is an interpretation of an essentially abstract image.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8391',38.0,38.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "seascape", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Orange", "Gold", "Red", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(53,'ilan-53','tablo','yayinda','Tuscan Pines Above Blossoming Fields, Framed','A square canvas built up in exceptionally thick impasto, so heavy that the surface reads almost as relief. Three tall umbrella pines with dark green canopies rise on slender trunks against a pale blue sky; a hilltop village with a small tower sits on the green ridge at the right. Below, the ground breaks into bands of cadmium yellow, orange and vermilion stubble with two mounds of white blossom worked in stiff ridges of pure white paint. Colour is applied wet-in-wet with a knife, unblended, so that every stroke stands proud of the canvas. Medium: oil on canvas, very heavy palette-knife impasto. Condition: no visible issues; impasto ridges intact, no flaking or craquelure observed.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, very heavy palette-knife impasto','','','','','','katalog A005; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8397, IMG_8398, IMG_8399, IMG_8400; No signature was found in any of the five frames; the lower edge of the canvas is partly hidden by the frame in every shot, so a signature could exist under the rebate.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8396',39.0,38.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Yellow", "Orange", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(54,'ilan-54','tablo','yayinda','Tall Vessels With Blossom On Gold, Framed','A square, warmly lit still life on a gold-ochre ground that shades from lemon at the top to burnt orange below. Five attenuated vessels - a tall oxblood bottle, a cobalt blue cylinder, a scarlet column and two smaller pots - stand in a shallow row, their reflections dragged downward into a dark pool of maroon and black. A bare branch carrying white five-petalled blossoms and a hanging cluster of rust-red berries springs from the tallest bottle. The paint is applied in a dense, sandy, granular impasto that speckles the entire background. Medium: oil on canvas, heavy textured impasto. Condition: no visible issues; thick paint intact.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, heavy textured impasto','','','','','','katalog A006; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8403, IMG_8404, IMG_8405; No signature located in any frame. Frame IMG_8402 was flagged as a possible document but is only a close-up of the painted surface.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8401',39.0,38.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gold", "Yellow", "Red", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(55,'ilan-55','tablo','yayinda','Provencal Fields With Yellow Farmhouse, Signed, Framed','A square canvas divided into broad, flat colour planes edged with dark contour lines, in the manner of a stained-glass window. Blue-violet mountains close off the horizon under a scumbled pale sky; below, the land opens into interlocking wedges of chrome yellow, lavender, cobalt and coral, crossed by salmon-pink roads that sweep in from the left. A tiny yellow farmhouse with a red roof and a dark cypress mark the middle distance; two round bushes and a lilac field with white furrow marks fill the foreground. Handling is smooth and matte with a fine linen-textured surface, quite different from the heavy impasto pieces around it. Medium: oil (or acrylic) on canvas. Signed lower right, on the yellow field. Condition: no visible damage; a fine craquelure-like crazing appears in the thicker white and coral passages, consistent with a heavily bodied ground rather than age.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil (or acrylic) on canvas','','','','','','katalog A007; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8407, IMG_8408, IMG_8409, IMG_8410; Signature is a long black flourish read at full resolution but not decipherable; no name recorded. Oil versus acrylic cannot be settled from photographs - the surface is matte and only lightly built.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8406',39.0,39.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["folk", "contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Blue", "Yellow", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(56,'ilan-56','tablo','yayinda','Apples And Banana In A Window Grid, Signed, Framed','A square composition organised like a leaded window: a grid of dark teal-blue bars divides the canvas into yellow, mauve and turquoise panes, each corner pane holding a single flat red apple. In the centre a lemon-yellow bowl heaped with scarlet apples sits beside a pale yellow jug and a long banana, against a turquoise pane. The yellow fields are worked in a dense granular impasto scattered with looping ochre scrollwork, so the surface glitters; the apples are laid in with thick vermilion and orange crusts. Medium: oil on canvas, heavy textured impasto. Signed centre right, across the yellow pane beside the large red apple. Condition: no visible issues; impasto sound.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, heavy textured impasto','','','','','','katalog A008; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8412, IMG_8413, IMG_8414, IMG_8415; The signature was enlarged and sharpened but remains an illegible cursive; several readings are possible and none is recorded.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8411',38.5,38.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["folk", "contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Yellow", "Red", "Blue", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(57,'ilan-57','tablo','yayinda','Snowbound Farmstead In Winter Woods, Signed, Framed','A landscape-format canvas in a muted winter palette of cream, grey-brown, olive and soft ochre. A large bare tree with frost-laden branches dominates the left; behind it a small outbuilding, and to the right a timber cabin with a deep snow-laden roof and a lean-to shed, its dark doorway the darkest accent in the picture. A rutted track catches a low warm light and leads into the middle distance past a broken fence and clumps of dry grass. The paint is worked wet-in-wet with a loaded brush and knife, the snow scumbled in thick creamy strokes over a warm underlayer. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas. Condition: the linen liner is lightly soiled and shows scattered grey marks, worst along the lower edge; the gilt frame has rubbing and small losses on the carved crests. Paint film appears sound with no visible tears or flaking.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A009; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8421, IMG_8422; The signature at lower right was enlarged and contrast-boosted; it appears to begin ''I. Cap'' or ''L. Cap'' followed by three or four more letters, but the ending is not legible and no name is recorded. The reverse of the canvas was never photographed, so any stretcher stamps or gallery labels are unknown.','no certificate or label photographed; the reverse was not photographed','IMG_8417',43.0,31.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Gray", "Green", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(58,'ilan-58','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Composition With Green Leaves, Signed, Framed','A square canvas of interlocking angular planes in blocked red, ochre-yellow, black and sage green, laid over a mottled turquoise and olive ground. A large dark-green leaf shape flecked with acid yellow sweeps across the lower centre; above it, scratched white lines fan out like rigging or a radio mast over a yellow field incised with a grid. The paint is thickly loaded and stippled, with dry-brushed veils and sgraffito lines scored back through the crust. Medium: oil on canvas, heavy impasto with sgraffito. Signed on the dark green leaf form, lower centre. Condition: no visible issues; heavy paint intact.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, heavy impasto with sgraffito','','','','','','katalog A010; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8426, IMG_8427; The signature runs over the raised green impasto and is not legible even at full resolution. Height and width readings differ by about an inch; the angled camera position may account for it.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8423',38.5,37.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Green", "Red", "Gold", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(59,'ilan-59','tablo','yayinda','Hand-Painted Copy After Van Gogh Sunflowers, Signed, Framed','A portrait-format canvas reproducing Van Gogh''s Sunflowers: a two-tone vase, pale above and ochre below with a dark dividing line, holds a dozen sunflowers in every stage from full ray-flowered bloom to bare seed-head. The background is a pale duck-egg blue-green laid in short blocky strokes; the table is a slab of chrome yellow and orange. Painted entirely in thick directional brushwork, with the petals dragged outward in loaded strokes and the seed centres built up in knotted brown and umber. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed on the body of the vase, lower centre, in blue paint, reading "Vincent". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Vincent. Condition: no visible issues; paint surface clean and intact, frame gilding unrubbed.','','','late 20th - early 21st century reproduction','oil on canvas','','','','Vincent','','katalog A011; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8429, IMG_8430, IMG_8431, IMG_8432; The word ''Vincent'' on the vase is part of the composition being copied and is not evidence of authorship - this is a modern hand-painted copy after Van Gogh, not an original. No copyist''s signature or studio label was found in any frame.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8428',26.75,31.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Yellow", "Gold", "Blue", "Brown"]}'::jsonb),
(60,'ilan-60','tablo','yayinda','Autumn Meadow With Flowering Slope, Signed, Framed','A square canvas in which a broad slope of flowering meadow fills the lower two thirds, stippled in thousands of separate touches of orange, chrome yellow, olive and pale blue so that the field seems to shimmer. Behind it a screen of trees in russet and gold flanks a pale opening of light, and blue-grey hills dissolve into a high scumbled sky. The paint is dragged and dotted with the knife, leaving crusted ridges and small paint pearls across the entire surface. Medium: oil on canvas, palette-knife impasto. Signed lower centre right, across the yellow meadow. Condition: no visible issues; impasto intact.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, palette-knife impasto','','','','','','katalog A012; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8434, IMG_8436, IMG_8437; Signature is a compact black flourish over heavy impasto; not legible and no name recorded.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8433',38.5,39.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Orange", "Yellow", "Green", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(61,'ilan-61','tablo','yayinda','Yellow Doorway In A Red Alley, Signed, Framed','A square canvas of strong flat planes: a vermilion wall on the left, a slate-blue house on the right with a small yellow window, and between them a chrome-yellow doorway thrown wide, spilling a wedge of yellow light across the orange ground. Blue-grey steps and a rounded blue form occupy the lower left corner. The surface is worked in a coarse, sandy impasto that breaks each colour into speckled grain, with the divisions between planes cut in dark green and black. Medium: oil on canvas, heavy textured impasto. Signed lower right, on the orange ground. Condition: no visible issues; paint crust intact.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','oil on canvas, heavy textured impasto','','','','','','katalog A013; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8440, IMG_8441, IMG_8442; Signature is a bold black cursive over rough impasto; enlarged but not decipherable, so no name is recorded.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8438',37.25,38.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Yellow", "Gray", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(62,'ilan-62','tablo','yayinda','Art Deco Woman In A Pleated Kimono, Numbered Edition, Framed','A tall, elegant Art Deco composition: a woman with a white marcelled coiffure and gold hair ornament stands with arms outstretched so that her ivory pleated robe opens into a great winged silhouette. The robe is finely ruled in vertical pleats and decorated with embossed-looking blossom clusters and pale mint bands; a turquoise and gold collar and a slim striped underdress run down the centre. She is flanked by two panels of dense black-and-white hairline stripes hung with pink iris stems, and a scrolling white smoke motif curls at her shoulder, all set against a matte black ground. Colour is flat and evenly laid with crisp line work, typical of a hand-pulled screenprint. Medium: serigraph (screenprint) on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in white pencil on the dark border. Edition: 83/300, hand-numbered in white pencil at lower left; hand-signed in white pencil at lower right. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 83/300. Condition: heavy reflections and dust on the glazing in every shot; the sheet itself appears clean with no foxing or tears visible through the glass.','','','late 20th century','serigraph (screenprint) on paper','83/300, hand-numbered in white pencil at lower left; hand-signed in white pencil at lower right','','','83/300','','katalog A014; olcu kareleri galeride degil: yok; The white pencil signature was enlarged and contrast-boosted; it reads as a short flowing cursive that could be ''S. Kao'' or ''S. Hao'' but is not certain, so no name is recorded. A small orange lozenge chop or seal appears at the upper left of the sheet but is too small to read. Medium is judged from the flat even colour and hand-numbered edition; lithograph cannot be ruled out without seeing the sheet edge. Frame IMG_8447 shows a different framed print (the Art Deco figure with two attendants catalogued as A015), not this work - it appears to have been grouped with A014 in error.','no certificate photographed; edition number and signature appear on the sheet itself','IMG_8443',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Black", "Blue", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(63,'ilan-63','tablo','yayinda','Art Deco Goddess With Two Attendants, Numbered Edition, Framed','A tall symmetrical Art Deco composition. A central figure with a jewelled cap stands before a gilded halo and an arch of pale jade, her long gown falling to a beaded train; she holds out two great swags of gold and copper drapery that loop down to either side. Two kneeling attendants in blush-pink gowns and close caps receive the drapery, one at each corner. Vertical hairline-striped panels rise behind her, hung with small fan and pearl ornaments, and the floor is a gold band of stylised lotus panels. Colour is flat, cool and precisely registered - pale jade, blush, ivory and metallic gold on a matte black ground. Medium: serigraph (screenprint) on paper, with metallic gold ink. Signed lower right of the sheet, in white pencil on the dark border. Edition: 168/275, hand-numbered in white pencil at lower left; hand-signed in white pencil at lower right. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 168/275. Condition: strong reflections and room reflections across the glazing in every shot; the sheet appears clean, with no foxing, cockling or tears visible through the glass.','','','late 20th century','serigraph (screenprint) on paper, with metallic gold ink','168/275, hand-numbered in white pencil at lower left; hand-signed in white pencil at lower right','','','168/275','','katalog A015; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8452, IMG_8453; The white pencil signature is a flowing cursive that could not be read even after enlargement and contrast enhancement, so no artist name is recorded; it is stylistically the same hand as the signature on A014. Serigraph is inferred from the flat, evenly laid colour, the metallic ink and the hand-numbered edition, not from an inspected sheet edge.','no certificate photographed; edition number and signature appear on the sheet itself','IMG_8448',33.75,41.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "ink", "paper"], "style": ["art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Gold", "Green", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(64,'ilan-64','tablo','yayinda','Old Master Style Floral Still Life, Framed','A portrait-format canvas in the old-master manner: an abundant bouquet of roses, peonies, tulips, cornflowers and marigolds cascades from a burnished copper-gold urn standing on a shadowed ledge. The flowers are picked out in pink, cream, coral, blue and lemon against a deep olive and umber background that lightens to a soft yellow-green glow behind the blooms. Petals are painted wet-in-wet with soft loaded strokes and lit from the left, with the darkest passages sunk almost to black at the lower left. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: the frame is deliberately distressed with rubbing to the gilt and visible red bole; the canvas shows a warm surface haze and some grime in the dark passages but no tears, flaking or obvious craquelure.','','','mid to late 20th century, in 18th-century taste','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A016; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8456, IMG_8457; No signature found in the four frames; the lower right of the canvas is dark and partly in shadow, so a signature could be present but unreadable. The reverse was not photographed, so stretcher stamps and labels are unknown. Age is a judgement from the frame and surface, not from any documentation.','no certificate or label photographed; the reverse was not photographed','IMG_8454',33.0,44.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "landscape", "still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Black", "Beige", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(65,'ilan-65','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Geometric Composition With Dark Orb, Signed, Framed','A square abstract in warm earth and jewel tones: a gold-leaf-like ochre panel at the left, a deep cobalt disc segment, a scarlet wedge and a pale sage horizontal band that cuts across the centre. A large dark aubergine orb sits low right of centre, weighted against a yellow ground scratched with fine incised lines. The surface reads as scumbled and abraded, with pencil and charcoal linework, faded grid marks and drips left visible - a worked, layered, almost frescoed appearance rather than a smooth one. Medium: mixed media or fine-art giclee print on paper, hand-signed in pencil. Signed lower right, in graphite on the image surface, reading "Rachel Warnick". Condition: glazing shows strong ceiling-light reflections in all shots; no damage visible through the glass.','','','late 20th - early 21st century','mixed media or fine-art giclee print on paper, hand-signed in pencil','','','','','','katalog A017; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8461, IMG_8462; The pencil signature is the only text; enlarged and sharpened it most plausibly reads ''Rachel Warnick'', but the surname could equally be ''Wardnick'' or ''Warnicl'' and the confidence is low - artist_read is left null deliberately. Medium is the weakest judgement in this record: the work is behind glass and matted, and no plate mark, deckle, dot screen or brush relief could be confirmed, so an original mixed-media work on paper and a signed giclee are both consistent with what is visible.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8458',40.5,40.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gold", "Blue", "Red", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(66,'ilan-66','tablo','yayinda','Nude Looking Over Her Shoulder, Signed, Framed','A tall portrait-format work on a near-black ground. A standing woman is seen from behind, her body turned so that the light rakes down her back, hip and thigh in soft rose and warm flesh tones while the shadowed side dissolves into the dark. She looks back over her right shoulder with long dark hair falling forward, her face modelled crisply against the void. The handling is soft and blended with no visible brush relief - the tonal transitions are rubbed and airbrush-smooth, and the background is a flat velvety black. Medium: pastel or airbrushed painting on board. Signed lower left of the image. Condition: the glazing is dusty and covered in fine scratches and swirl marks, with several bright scuff streaks across the upper left; a scattering of pale specks and small circular marks shows across the dark ground. It is not possible to tell from the photographs whether those marks are on the glass or on the work itself.','','','1970s','pastel or airbrushed painting on board','','','','','','katalog A018; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8465, IMG_8466; Medium is uncertain. The work is behind glass, which rules out an unvarnished oil on canvas presentation but the smooth blended tonality is equally consistent with soft pastel, airbrushed acrylic, or a printed reproduction; no dot screen, plate mark or paper deckle could be seen, and no brush relief is visible. The small dark signature at lower left was cropped and contrast-boosted but is illegible.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8463',27.5,40.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["charcoal", "panel"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Pink", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(67,'ilan-67','tablo','yayinda','Large Abstract Composition in Ochre and Blue, Signed, Framed','A square abstract built from stacked rectangular fields in burnt orange, ochre, cream and deep indigo, cut through by a broad pale arc that sweeps from the lower left to the upper right. The surface imitates weathered plaster or fresco, with scratched calligraphic marks, small circles and ruled lines drifting across the blocks. Warm earth tones dominate, with a cool violet-blue wedge and a slate-blue band at the right giving the composition its counterweight. Presented with a very wide white mat inside a broad brushed champagne-silver frame under glass. Medium: giclee or offset reproduction on textured paper. Signed lower left of the image, in yellow. Condition: No damage visible; heavy overhead-light glare on the glass in every shot, so the surface could not be fully inspected.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','giclee or offset reproduction on textured paper','','','','','','katalog A019; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8471, IMG_8472; The signature (IMG_8468) is a looping yellow cursive over textured ground and is not legible. The close-up also shows an even dot/grain pattern in the dark passages, which reads as a photomechanical or inkjet reproduction rather than an original painting, but the glass glare prevents certainty.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8467',40.25,40.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Orange", "Gold", "Beige", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(68,'ilan-68','tablo','yayinda','Sunflowers in a Vase After Van Gogh, B. Kenna, Signed, Framed','B. Kenna. A full-scale painted copy of Van Gogh''s Sunflowers, worked in very heavy impasto with a loaded brush and palette knife so the petals stand off the canvas in ridges. Chrome yellow, orange and russet flowers, some in full face and some spent and drooping, rise from a two-tone cream vase set on a broad orange table against a pale blue-green wall built from short choppy strokes. The colour is high-keyed and the handling frankly gestural, with visible ridges catching the light across the whole surface. Housed in a heavy ornate gilt-composition frame with fluted and acanthus-leaf ornament. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark red, reading "B. Kenna". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: B. Kenna. Condition: No tears or losses visible; some rubbing and small chips to the gilt frame ornament. Paint surface appears sound.','B. Kenna','','late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','B. Kenna','','katalog A020; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8479, IMG_8480; The signature is clear but the surname could be read as Kenna, Kerma or Kenno; there is a trailing flourish after the final letter. This is an unsigned-by-Van-Gogh copy, not an original.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8473',38.5,48.9,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Orange", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(69,'ilan-69','tablo','yayinda','Seated Woman Collage, Montevideo, P. KORZENIAK, Signed, Framed, 1999','P. KORZENIAK. A large mixed-media panel in which a hieratic, faceless seated woman fills the centre, her robe and the architecture around her collaged from real Spanish-language newspaper classified pages. Washes of dusty rose, mauve, slate blue and ochre float over the printed sheets, with a small scarlet heart at the figure''s breast and stepped city blocks and windows drawn behind her. Textured lace and doily papers are embedded in the drapery, and thin ink lines describe a necklace and the edges of the buildings. The palette is muted and chalky throughout, with the newsprint reading as warm tan. Medium: mixed media, newspaper collage with paint and wash on canvas. Signed upper area of the composition, in blue, reading "P. KORZENIAK  MVD 11/99". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: P. KORZENIAK; MVD 11/99; OPORTUNIDAD; SUPERMERCADO. Condition: Collaged newsprint is toned and shows fine surface crazing and small creases where the paper was laid down; frame gilding is rubbed with the red bole exposed in places. No tears or lifting seen.','P. KORZENIAK','','1999','mixed media, newspaper collage with paint and wash on canvas','','','','P. KORZENIAK; MVD 11/99; OPORTUNIDAD','','katalog A021; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8490, IMG_8491; The second signature line reads MVD followed by 11/99; MVD is the usual abbreviation for Montevideo and the newspaper ads name Uruguayan suburbs, but the date could be 11/90 or 11/00. The artist name is transcribed as printed and has not been researched.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8481',44.75,39.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["canvas", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Pink", "Purple", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(70,'ilan-70','tablo','yayinda','European Village by a Millstream, F. Wagner, Signed, Framed','F. Wagner. A quiet landscape of cream stuccoed cottages with steep red-brown tiled roofs and balconies clustered at the water''s edge, reached by a low stone arch that is doubled by its reflection. Slender autumn trees flecked with gold and white impasto lean over the buildings and a church spire rises in the misty distance. The water is painted smooth and silvery, in deliberate contrast to the thickly loaded, granular handling of the foliage and roofs. The palette is soft: greys, creams, ochres and olive, warmed by touches of rust. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right, in pale grey-white paint, reading "F. Wagner". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: F. Wagner. Condition: Paint film looks sound with no craquelure visible at this resolution; the frame has scattered chips and abrasion along the outer edges, most noticeably at the corners.','F. Wagner','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','F. Wagner','','katalog A022; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8496, IMG_8497; The signature is clearly F. Wagner but the name is a common studio signature on decorative European landscapes; no further attribution evidence was photographed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8492',37.75,32.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Gray", "Green", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(71,'ilan-71','tablo','yayinda','Parisian Suite Lithograph by Huchet, Numbered Edition, Framed','HUCHET. A light, calligraphic colour lithograph in which two seated women, one in cobalt and cerulean blue and the other in soft lilac with a wide brimmed hat, lean together over a small green-topped table. Loose contour lines describe the chairs and skirts while the colour is applied in transparent washes and stippled granular passages that sit slightly off the drawing. A two-armed chandelier with yellow flames hangs above them against the bare cream sheet. The image is deckle-free and floated behind a black-lined mat over a dusty rose mount. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil, reading "Huchet". Edition: 35/175, hand signed. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity for PARISIAN SUITE by/after HUCHET, colour lithograph, edition 35/175, hand signed, with an authorised signature. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 35/175; Huchet; Patrician Galleries Inc.; Certificate of Authenticity. Condition: Sheet appears clean and bright; light diagonal reflections on the glass. No foxing or toning visible.','HUCHET','PARISIAN SUITE','late 20th century','colour lithograph on paper','35/175, hand signed','','Patrician Galleries Inc.','35/175; Huchet; Patrician Galleries Inc.','','katalog A023; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8502, IMG_8503; IMG_8498 is a stamp on raw canvas reading THIS IS AN ORIGINAL OIL PAINTING / 41977 / UNLAWFUL TO COPY / Paul Robinson Fine Arts / Atlanta, Georgia. It cannot belong to this work, which is a lithograph on paper, and appears to have been shot in with the wrong lot. The certificate is photographed inside a sealed bag, so its title and edition lines are read through plastic.','Certificate of Authenticity for PARISIAN SUITE by/after HUCHET, colour lithograph, edition 35/175, hand signed, with an authorised signature.','IMG_8499',11.6,13.9,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Yellow", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(72,'ilan-72','tablo','yayinda','Paris Londres Geneve, Woman Reading a Newspaper, Gutting, Numbered Edition, Framed','Gutting. A bold black and white graphic image of a woman in a sleeveless black dress and an oversized black picture hat, seen in profile as she holds an open newspaper. Behind her the Eiffel Tower rises through fine hatched lines and a row of trees fills the right side, all rendered in dense pen-like strokes against the bare white sheet. A small espresso cup sits at the lower left and a scrolled iron cafe chair at the right; the only relief from the black and white is a touch of green in the foliage. A black rectangular gallery tab reading DLG is fixed to the mat below the image. Medium: lithograph or screenprint on paper, hand coloured in part. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil, reading "Gutting". Edition: 67/150. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: PARIS - LONDRES - GENEVE; 67/150; DLG. Condition: Sheet clean and bright with no visible foxing; some reflection on the glass at the upper right.','Gutting','PARIS - LONDRES - GENEVE','late 20th century','lithograph or screenprint on paper, hand coloured in part','67/150','','DLG (label on the mat)','PARIS - LONDRES - GENEVE; 67/150; DLG','','katalog A024; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8506, IMG_8507; The pencil signature reads as a cursive Gutting or Guttinger with an umlaut over the u; it is transcribed as written and not confidently resolved. A boxed monogram appears in the lower right of the image itself. The printing process could not be confirmed through glass - the flat solid blacks suggest a screenprint or lithograph rather than a relief cut.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8504',14.0,18.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "White", "Beige", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(73,'ilan-73','tablo','yayinda','Caribbean Market Women with Baskets, Fritz Plock, Signed, Framed','Fritz Plock. A vivid folk-modernist market scene in which three elongated figures with sharply faceted faces stand close together, balancing woven baskets of green fruit, magenta berries and yellow grain. The whole design is drawn in heavy black outline and filled with flat, high-chroma colour - tangerine, lemon, purple, emerald and turquoise - over a bare tan ground that is left showing as the earth. Sprays of orange leaves fan across the lower left corner and the sky is a clean gradient of turquoise blue. The handling is smooth and poster-like, with no visible impasto. Medium: acrylic on canvas. Signed lower left of the canvas, in black, reading "Fritz Plock". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Fritz Plock. Condition: Paint surface clean and unbroken; the frame has light rubbing at the corners.','Fritz Plock','','late 20th century','acrylic on canvas','','','','Fritz Plock','','katalog A025; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8509, IMG_8510, IMG_8511; The black brush signature is only partly legible; Fritz Plock is the closest reading and could equally be Fritz Block or a similar name. Whether the paint is acrylic or thinly worked oil cannot be told from the photographs, and the tan ground may be an unprimed canvas or a painted field.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8508',16.4,21.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["folk", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Yellow", "Blue", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(74,'ilan-74','tablo','yayinda','Adobe Cottage with Flame Tree, Signed, Framed, 1993','A small plein-air style landscape of a long adobe cottage with a weathered terracotta pantile roof, its shuttered windows and plank door facing a low dry-stone wall. A slender tree bursts into scarlet and orange bloom over the roofline, and soft blue-grey hills close the distance behind olive and sage foliage. The paint is applied in short, loose, unblended strokes with the canvas weave reading through the thin passages, and the palette stays warm and dusty - cream, terracotta, olive and mauve. Presented floated under a cream mat. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark paint, reading "C.M. 93". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: C.M. 93. Condition: Canvas appears sound with no visible losses; the frame is rubbed and the gilding worn along the edges.','','','1993 if the date reading is correct','oil on canvas','','','','C.M. 93','','katalog A026; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8515, IMG_8516; Only a monogram is present. The initials read as C M and the two digits as 93, but they could as easily be 43 or 45; no full name is given anywhere on the piece.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8513',21.25,17.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Orange", "Red", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(75,'ilan-75','tablo','yayinda','Naive Winter Scene with Buggy and Geese, Framed','A small naive painting set at dusk, with a graded blue sky that pales to warm cream at the horizon behind a bare, spidery tree. At the left a dark horse pulls a black-hooded buggy carrying two figures in broad white hats, while at the centre a woman in a long dark dress and white bonnet holds a small child and another child stoops beside a fence rail. A file of chalk-white geese waddles away to the right. Everything is simplified into flat silhouettes with fine brush detail, and the palette is restricted to slate blue, cream, black and a little rust. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: A short reddish scuff or paint mark runs along the top rail of the frame; the painting itself shows no visible damage.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A027; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8518, IMG_8519; No signature was found in any frame, and the back of the work was not photographed. Canvas weave is visible under the paint, but the support could be a canvas board rather than a stretched canvas.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8517',13.85,12.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Beige", "Black", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(76,'ilan-76','tablo','yayinda','Comic Fox Hunt Scene After Thelwell, Signed, Framed','Thelwell. A humorous hunting scene drawn in fine pen line and washed with transparent colour. Riders in scarlet coats and black caps stream out of a bare winter copse behind a pack of hounds, while in the foreground a small child in black clings to a fat, wide-eyed piebald pony that is charging off in the wrong direction. Autumn foliage in burnt orange marks the centre of the composition against a pale grey sky, and the ground is worked in soft ochre and olive. The image is a small sheet floated on a cream mat inside a plain gilt frame. Medium: colour offset lithograph on paper. Signed lower right within the image, in white, reading "Thelwell". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Thelwell. Condition: Scattered brown foxing spots across the cream mat, heaviest near the upper left and lower centre; the printed sheet itself looks clean. Frame gilding is rubbed at the corners.','Thelwell','','mid to late 20th century','colour offset lithograph on paper','','','','Thelwell','','katalog A028; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8522, IMG_8523; The signature in the image is small and white on a dark ground; it reads as Thelwell, which matches the subject matter, but the reading is not certain. There is no plate mark, no edition number and no publisher line, so this is treated as a published reproduction rather than an original watercolour, though the glass glare leaves some doubt.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8520',15.75,12.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Orange", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(77,'ilan-77','tablo','yayinda','El Anillo de Compromiso, Girl Admiring Her Ring, Signed, Framed','A half-length portrait of a dark-haired young woman turned in profile, her head wrapped in a red and multicoloured floral scarf and a loose white blouse slipping from one shoulder. She holds her hands before her and looks down at a ring with a small smile. The background is a loose, feathery green woodland worked wet-in-wet, which throws her warm flesh tones and the crisp white drapery forward. Brushwork is fluid and confident, with thick creamy strokes in the blouse and scumbled greens behind. Medium: oil on board or panel. Signed upper left of the picture, in dark paint, reading "Dapres Parisi". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Dapres Parisi; EL ANILLO DE COMPROMISO. Condition: Surface is dusty with fine scratches and speckling visible in the raking light of IMG_8525; the black frame is scuffed along the outer edges. No losses or tears seen.','','EL ANILLO DE COMPROMISO','20th century','oil on board or panel','','','','Dapres Parisi; EL ANILLO DE COMPROMISO','','katalog A029; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8527, IMG_8528; Dapres Parisi is written as an inscription meaning after Parisi, so the painter is a copyist, not Parisi. A second line below it, apparently the copyist''s own signature, is illegible. The support looks like a rigid panel rather than canvas but this could not be confirmed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8524',19.0,23.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "panel"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Beige", "Black", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(78,'ilan-78','tablo','yayinda','Lighthouse and Palms Coastal Scene, Framed','A soft, faded coastal view dominated by a tall pale lighthouse with a red-tiled cap and a railed gallery, set among low tile-roofed cottages. Two palms lean in from the left and right, gulls scatter across a hazy sky, and a grey clinker rowboat with wooden mooring posts rests on the sand in the foreground. The whole image is deliberately muted and antiqued, in bleached sand, chalky blue-green and dull terracotta, with a mottled crackle texture over the surface. It is set behind a wide marbled parchment mat with a gold beaded fillet. Medium: textured decorative reproduction print on board. Condition: No damage visible; several bright reflections from ceiling lights on the glass. Frame is clean with light dust.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','textured decorative reproduction print on board','','','','','','katalog A030; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8533, IMG_8534; No signature, edition or publisher mark appears anywhere. The overall crackle texture and the muted, uniformly aged palette read as a mass-produced decorative reproduction rather than a hand-painted original, but the glass and glare prevent a firm judgement.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8531',18.25,22.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape"], "medium": ["print", "panel"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Beige", "Blue", "Orange", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(79,'ilan-79','tablo','yayinda','Pair of Large Wolverine Charcoal Drawings, Signed, Framed, 2001','A matched pair of large, dramatically shaded charcoal and graphite drawings of a clawed comic-book hero, each caught mid-lunge with the body coiled and the muscles heavily modelled. Broad smudged tones sweep out behind the figure as motion and smoke, and the claws are drawn as long, hard-edged blades that cut across the sheet. The palette is entirely greyscale, from near-black rubbed passages to the untouched white of the paper, with the figure''s mask and snarling face picked out by sharp highlights. Both sheets are dated in the lower right and framed identically. Medium: charcoal and graphite on paper. Signed lower right of each sheet, in pen. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 09.30.01. Condition: Sheets appear clean with no tears; some charcoal has migrated onto the paper as light grey haze, which is normal for the medium. Strong ceiling-light reflections on the glass.','','','dated 2001','charcoal and graphite on paper','','','','09.30.01','','katalog A031; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8540, IMG_8541; This listing contains two separate framed drawings, not one. The signature on both is a single looping flourish struck through with a long horizontal and cannot be read; only the date 09.30.01 is legible. These are hand-drawn interpretations of a copyrighted Marvel character, not licensed prints.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8536',18.25,24.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["charcoal", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gray", "Black", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(80,'ilan-80','tablo','yayinda','Shoulao, Star God of Longevity, with Deer, Signed, Framed','A hanging-scroll style painting on silk of a bearded elder in layered robes of pale gold, sage and dull rose, a hooded grey mantle over his head and a tall knotted staff in his right hand. A gentle spotted deer presses against his hip and gazes out at the viewer. The drawing is precise and linear in the gongbi manner, with fine ink contours filled by flat mineral washes, and the ground silk has toned to a warm dove grey. A four-character ink inscription and a small red seal are placed in the upper right. Medium: ink and colour on silk. Signed upper right, four characters in ink with a red seal below, reading "庚子初春". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 庚子初春. Condition: The silk is toned overall and shows faint tide lines and scattered specks; the frame is heavily rubbed with the gesso and red bole exposed along the edges. Reflections on the glass in every shot.','','','20th century; inscription appears to name a gengzi year','ink and colour on silk','','','','庚子初春','','katalog A032; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8545, IMG_8546; The four ink characters are read as gengzi early spring, a cyclical year date rather than a name; the second character could also be read as xu. The red seal is not legible, so no artist can be given. Whether the sheet is silk or a fine woven paper cannot be settled from the photographs, though the weave visible in IMG_8543 looks like silk.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8542',17.0,25.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["ink", "textile"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Gold", "Green", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(81,'ilan-81','tablo','yayinda','Sampans at Sunset on a Wide River, Signed, Framed','A palette-knife river scene at sunset, with three arched-roof sampans moored in a row, their dark violet-brown hulls and reflections cutting across a broad expanse of water that glows lemon and cream where the low sun strikes it. A single black boat lies on the pale sandbank in the foreground and a low, distant treeline runs along the horizon under a sky of thick sage and yellow strokes. The paint is laid on in flat, deliberate slabs, leaving a strongly ridged surface, and small figures in conical hats are indicated with a few dabs of white and ochre. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower left of the canvas, in black. Condition: Impasto is intact with no flaking seen; the painted frame is chipped and marked along the outer edges and there is a small paler patch on the lower rail.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A033; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8549, IMG_8550; The signature is a compressed black scrawl at the lower left and cannot be read. No head or background-removed frame was supplied for this listing, so IMG_8547 is used as the cover.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8547',19.5,15.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["asian", "impressionist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Green", "Brown", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(82,'ilan-82','tablo','yayinda','Lady Reading Under a Vine Pergola, Framed','A Victorian garden idyll: a woman in a long white lace-trimmed dress leans back in a bentwood rocker with a small blue book in her lap, a folding chair and a white cloth-covered table with a decanter, glass and books beside her. Overhead a whitewashed timber pergola carries a screen of vines that filters the light onto a dusty mauve-brown floor. The handling is loose and painterly, with visible directional brushwork in the beams and ground and softly blended pastel flesh and drapery. The palette is muted - cream, dusty rose, pale sage and violet-grey - and the picture is surrounded, unusually, by a woven floral tapestry mat instead of paper. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: A pale diagonal line runs across the lower left of the picture in IMG_8552 and IMG_8554 - possibly a scratch, crease or old repair in the surface. Heavy glass glare in most frames. The tapestry mat looks intact but is dusty in places.','','','late 19th to 20th century (image style late 19th century)','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A034; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8555, IMG_8556; The surface shows directional brush texture with no dot screen, so it reads as hand-painted, but a textured giclee on canvas cannot be ruled out from photographs. No signature was found in any frame. The tapestry surround may be part of an original decorative scheme or a later reframing.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8551',28.0,35.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Pink", "Green", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(83,'ilan-83','tablo','yayinda','Jane Avril Jardin de Paris Poster, HLautrec, Signed, Framed, 1893','HLautrec. The famous Montmartre cabaret design: Jane Avril in a yellow-gold skirt and black stockings raises one leg on a raked stage, her figure outlined in a single sinuous black contour. The whole composition is enclosed by the scrolling brown-grey neck of a double bass and the player''s spread hand, which forms a repoussoir arch at the right. Lettering in black brush script reads ''Jane Avril'' across the top with ''Jardin de Paris'' beneath. Flat yellow, warm cream, black and a soft stippled grey (crachis spatter) carry the whole image, printed on a white sheet. Medium: colour lithograph poster (later printing or reproduction). Signed lower centre, printed within the design, reading "HLautrec 93". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Jane Avril; Jardin de Paris; HLautrec 93; Depot Chez Kleinmann. Condition: Reflections and a photographer reflection on the glass obscure parts of the sheet. No tears, foxing or losses visible from these images.','HLautrec','Jane Avril / Jardin de Paris','design 1893; this impression later 20th century','colour lithograph poster (later printing or reproduction)','','','','Jane Avril; Jardin de Paris; HLautrec 93','','katalog A035; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8560, IMG_8561; At roughly 17 x 22 in framed this is far smaller than the original 1893 poster (about 51 x 37 in), so it is almost certainly a later printing or reproduction rather than a period affiche - but nothing in the photographs states an edition or publisher of this impression. The small ''AFFICHAGE'' billposting plaque inside the design has two further lines that are too blurred to transcribe.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8557',17.0,22.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist", "art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Gold", "Black", "Beige", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(84,'ilan-84','tablo','yayinda','Moulin Rouge La Goulue Poster, HLautrec, Signed, Framed, 1891','HLautrec. La Goulue kicks up a white froth of petticoats at the centre, her red-spotted bodice and blonde topknot bright against a frieze of flat black silhouetted spectators. In the foreground the grey-mauve rubbery profile of her partner Valentin looms, hands raised, while three yellow globe lamps float behind. The lettering block at the top repeats ''MOULIN ROUGE'' three times in red over ''LA GOULUE'', with ''CONCERT / BAL / TOUS LES SOIRS'' at the right. Flat poster colour - red, yellow, black and cream - with no modelling. Medium: colour lithograph poster (later printing or reproduction). Signed lower left, printed within the design, reading "HLautrec". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: MOULIN ROUGE MOULIN ROUGE MOULIN ROUGE; CONCERT; BAL; TOUS LES SOIRS. Condition: Strong room reflections in the glass. No visible tears or foxing.','HLautrec','Moulin Rouge / La Goulue','design 1891; this impression later 20th century','colour lithograph poster (later printing or reproduction)','','','','MOULIN ROUGE MOULIN ROUGE MOULIN ROUGE; CONCERT; BAL','','katalog A036; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8564, IMG_8565; Size again indicates a later printing rather than an 1891 original affiche. There is a small printed imprint line at the lower right of the design that is too small to read in any supplied frame.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8562',16.25,21.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist", "art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Red", "Yellow", "Black", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(85,'ilan-85','tablo','yayinda','Ambassadeurs Aristide Bruant Poster, HLautrec, Signed, Framed, 1892','HLautrec. Bruant stands three-quarter length in a wide-brimmed black hat and black cape, his long red scarf swinging across the body as the single note of colour. Behind him an orange panel carries the word ''AMBASSADEURS'' in heavy outlined capitals with three dots, and a shadowy black silhouette of a second figure crosses the deep navy ground at the left. Below, brush-lettered text reads ''aristide BRUANT dans son cabaret''. The design is built from broad flat areas of navy, orange, black and red with a bold contour line throughout. Medium: colour lithograph poster (later printing or reproduction). Signed lower left, printed within the design, in gold on the dark ground, reading "HLautrec". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: AMBASSADEURS; aristide BRUANT; dans son cabaret; HLautrec. Condition: Heavy reflection across the glass including the photographer; the dark ground makes surface condition hard to judge. No visible tears.','HLautrec','Ambassadeurs / aristide BRUANT dans son cabaret','design 1892; this impression later 20th century','colour lithograph poster (later printing or reproduction)','','','','AMBASSADEURS; aristide BRUANT; dans son cabaret','','katalog A037; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8569, IMG_8570; IMG_8571 does NOT belong with this poster - it shows an entirely different painting (Don Quixote charging the windmills, with Sancho Panza and greyhounds, oil on canvas, landscape format). It has been filed under this listing and is recorded here as a document frame; it most likely belongs to another lot. Frame IMG_8566 is missing from the sequence. Size again suggests a later printing rather than an original 1892 affiche.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8567',16.25,21.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist", "art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Blue", "Orange", "Red", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(86,'ilan-86','tablo','yayinda','Don Quixote Charging the Windmills, Framed','A landscape-format painting of Don Quixote at the charge, lance lowered towards a row of windmills on the ridge, with Sancho Panza on his donkey and a pair of greyhounds running alongside. Warm earth tones with a pale sky. Medium: oil or acrylic on canvas. Condition: only one photograph available.','','','','oil or acrylic on canvas','','','','','','katalog A037B; olcu kareleri galeride degil: yok; Photographed once only, inside another listing''s sequence. Needs its own photographs, measurements and a closer look.','','IMG_8571',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "animal"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "", "color": ["Brown", "Gold", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(87,'ilan-87','tablo','yayinda','Colourful Abstract Head in Gilt Frame, J. Clayton, Signed, Framed','J. Clayton. A dense central cluster of biomorphic shapes - a teal dome with yellow zig-zags, a pink and yellow crescent, a red disc, a cobalt wedge and a small spiral eye - floats on a scraped white and grey ground. Loose black ink lines whip across the whole surface in loops, spirals and calligraphic squiggles, and a border of deep aubergine-black scumbling frames the composition on all four sides with touches of gold leaf. The paint is thin and dragged in places and thickly worked in others, and the canvas weave shows through. The result is bright, playful and deliberately childlike. Medium: acrylic and ink on canvas. Signed lower right of the composition, in dark red, reading "J. Clayton". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: J. Clayton. Condition: No visible damage; paint surface intact with intentional scraping and drips. Frame shows minor rubbing on the gilt highlights.','J. Clayton','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic and ink on canvas','','','','J. Clayton','','katalog A038; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8575, IMG_8576; The signature is a fluent red script that could equally read ''J. Claydon'' or ''J. Davydov''; the middle letters are not certain. Whether the medium is acrylic or oil cannot be determined from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8572',27.75,32.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "figurative"], "medium": ["ink", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["White", "Blue", "Yellow", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(88,'ilan-88','obje','yayinda','R.C. Gorman Cast Paper Relief ''Yoko'', Numbered Edition, Framed, 1988','R.C. GORMAN. An entirely white cast-paper relief: a kneeling figure swathed in a deeply folded blanket, her head turned to show a serene profile and a long braid of hair. The whole image is modelled in raised and recessed paper - no pigment at all - so it reads purely through light and shadow across the ridged drapery folds. The sheet has a soft irregular deckled edge on all four sides and is floated on a cream linen-covered mat. Signed, dated and numbered in pencil along the lower edge. Medium: cast paper relief (handmade paper casting). Signed lower left of the sheet, in pencil, reading "R.C.Gorman 1988". Edition: 64/200, signed and numbered in pencil. Accompanied by a certificate: Typed certificate no. 110 dated 01/25/94 certifying the paper casting ''Yoko'' by R.C. Gorman as signed and numbered, authenticated by Cornell Gabos. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: R.C.Gorman 1988; 64/200; Certificate of Authenticity; 110. Condition: Sheet appears clean and undamaged with crisp deckled edges; light glass glare only. Certificate is creased and taped inside a plastic sleeve.','R.C. GORMAN','YOKO','1988','cast paper relief (handmade paper casting)','64/200, signed and numbered in pencil','','Renaissance Fine Arts, 2184 Warrensville Road, University Hts., Ohio 44118','R.C.Gorman 1988; 64/200; Certificate of Authenticity','','katalog A039; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8581, IMG_8582; The authenticator''s surname on the certificate prints as ''GABOS'' but the typeface is worn and could be ''GABDS''. The relief itself carries no title.','Typed certificate no. 110 dated 01/25/94 certifying the paper casting ''Yoko'' by R.C. Gorman as signed and numbered, authenticated by Cornell Gabos.','IMG_8577',26.0,30.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["White", "Beige", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(89,'ilan-89','tablo','yayinda','Two Ladies with Parasols and Flowers, Gerard Bernhard, Signed, Framed','Gerard Bernhard. Two stylised women stand close together at the centre: one in a wide white plumed hat and mustard-yellow coat holding a basket of blossom, the other in a scarlet jacket and dark hat, both under open parasols. Behind them the boulevard dissolves into slashing strokes of crimson, plum, ochre and near-black with scattered red and white lights - the background is nearly abstract while the faces are drawn with fine dark lines and porcelain-pale skin. The paint is applied in long dragged strokes over an open canvas weave, giving a smoky, theatrical effect. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower left of the canvas, in black, reading "Gerard Bernhard". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Gerard Bernhard. Condition: Paint surface appears sound. The gilt frame has rubbing and small losses on the raised ornament, and the linen liner is lightly soiled.','Gerard Bernhard','','third quarter of the 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','Gerard Bernhard','','katalog A040; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8587, IMG_8588; The signature''s surname is written in a cramped hand and could be ''Bernhardt'' or ''Bernhardi''. Note that IMG_8589, filed under A041, is a verso label reading ''Certificate of Authenticity - Collier Art Corporation / ARTIST Bernhard / MEDIA Original Oil / TITLE Elegance'' plus a Taiwanese stretcher-maker''s label - that label matches THIS painting''s signature and subject far better than A041''s, and may have been photographed out of order.','no certificate photographed with this listing - but see uncertainty','IMG_8584',29.25,26.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Red", "Gold", "Purple", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(90,'ilan-90','tablo','yayinda','Arc de Triomphe Paris Street Scene, J. GASTON, Signed, Framed','J. GASTON. A grey-silver Paris nocturne: the Arc de Triomphe rises through mist at the centre-right while horse-drawn carriages and a knot of small dark figures move across a rain-slicked foreground that mirrors the lamplight in long vertical smears. A bare tree and a lit street lantern anchor the left edge, with dabs of ochre and gold foliage. The paint is applied wet-into-wet with a palette knife and stiff brush in silver-grey, charcoal, cream and rust, and the figures are indicated with quick single-stroke touches of red and white. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark grey block capitals, reading "J. GASTON". Accompanied by a certificate: Small printed verso label headed ''Certificate of Authenticity - Collier Art Corporation'', filled in by hand: artist Bernhard, media Original Oil, title Elegance, size 19530-170, with an authorized signature. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: J. GASTON; Certificate of Authenticity - Collier Art Corporation; ARTIST  Bernhard; MEDIA  Original Oil. Condition: Painting appears sound with good impasto. The gilt frame has scattered rubbing and small chips to the raised ornament. The verso labels are torn, foxed and partly lifted.','J. GASTON','','third quarter of the 20th century','oil on canvas','','','Collier Art Corporation (on the verso label)','J. GASTON; Certificate of Authenticity - Collier Art Corporation; ARTIST  Bernhard','','katalog A041; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8593, IMG_8595; IMG_8589 (the verso with the Collier Art certificate label and the SINRICO Taiwan stretcher label) is filed with this listing but the label names the artist as ''Bernhard'' and the title as ''Elegance'', which matches A040''s signature and subject, not this canvas signed J. GASTON. The two backs may have been photographed out of order - the label should be re-checked against the actual verso before it is used in a listing. The handwritten size on the SINRICO label is illegible.','Small printed verso label headed ''Certificate of Authenticity - Collier Art Corporation'', filled in by hand: artist Bernhard, media Original Oil, title Elegance, size 19530-170, with an authorized signature.','IMG_8590',28.0,32.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Beige", "Gold", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(91,'ilan-91','tablo','yayinda','Autumn Woodland Path in Gilt Frame, Framed','A tonal woodland interior: slender bare trunks rise the full height of the canvas while a pale sandy path curves from the lower left into a luminous grey-gold clearing at the centre. Copper and rust foliage clusters on the right-hand trees, and a dark bank of scrub and boulders masses along the path''s edge. The whole picture is worked in a narrow range of browns, ochres and warm greys with a single soft light source in the mist, and the varnish has darkened so that the shadows are now almost opaque. Small birds are flicked into the sky in dark specks. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: The varnish is noticeably discoloured and the darks have sunk, which is typical of age; some surface grime. The gilt frame has rubbing and small losses to the high points of the ornament. No tears or obvious repairs visible.','','','late 19th to early 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A042; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8598, IMG_8599; No signature could be found in the supplied frames - both lower corners were examined at high magnification. The apparent age is judged from the darkened varnish and frame style only; there is no date or label.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8596',35.25,28.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture", "animal"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Gold", "Orange", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(92,'ilan-92','tablo','yayinda','P. Buckley Moss ''Berlin'' Signed Print, Signed, Framed, 1986','Moss. A stylised winter street scene: a tall dark-coated organ grinder stands behind a red-wheeled barrel organ while four elongated children in coats and hats gather around and a brown dachshund trots past on the snow. Behind them the broken spire and lower stump of the Kaiser Wilhelm Memorial Church rise in warm sandy brown against a pale blue-grey sky, flanked by bare trees and grey modern blocks. The figures are drawn with the artist''s characteristic tall, narrow, almost faceless silhouettes, and the palette is restrained - dove blue, sand, black and one note of pink. Medium: offset lithograph / poster print on paper, pencil signed. Signed lower right of the image, in pencil, reading "P Buckley Moss 1986". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Moss; Berlin; 1986. Condition: Sheet appears clean; glass carries strong reflections. The red frame shows minor edge scuffing.','Moss','Berlin','1986','offset lithograph / poster print on paper, pencil signed','','','','Moss; Berlin; 1986','','katalog A043; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8602, IMG_8603; The pencil signature is faint and read as ''P Buckley Moss 1986''; only the date and the surname''s shape are firm, but the word ''Moss'' printed in pink on the mat supports the reading. No edition number is visible, so this may be a poster rather than a limited edition print.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8600',16.5,25.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["folk", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Black", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(93,'ilan-93','tablo','yayinda','Woman in Blue Gown Klimt-Style Portrait, Q.SUN, Signed, Framed','Q.SUN. A three-quarter portrait of a woman with heavy chestnut hair, downcast blue-shadowed lids and a jewelled choker, wearing an off-shoulder gown patterned in peacock blue, turquoise and violet swirls. The background dissolves into a mosaic of small rectangles and totemic ornament in copper, magenta, cobalt and jade, and the lower third becomes a grid of soft olive, pink and gold squares like a tiled table. The medium is chalky and matt with the paper tooth showing through, and the drawing is built up in layered strokes rather than flat washes. Medium: pastel and mixed media on paper. Signed lower left of the sheet, in dark paint, reading "Q.SUN". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Q.SUN. Condition: Sheet appears clean and evenly toned; strong glass glare across the upper half in every frame. Frame ornament shows light rubbing.','Q.SUN','','late 20th century','pastel and mixed media on paper','','','','Q.SUN','','katalog A044; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8607, IMG_8608; The signature''s first character is obscured by glare - it reads as ''Q'' but could be ''X'', ''R'' or ''G''; only ''SUN'' is firm. Medium is judged from the chalky matt surface and visible paper tooth; it could be gouache or a mixed pastel/acrylic technique rather than pure pastel.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8604',45.25,37.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["charcoal", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Orange", "Pink", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(94,'ilan-94','tablo','yayinda','Scholar with a Bust Old Master Copy, Framed','A large dark-ground half-length: a bearded man in a broad black hat and black doublet stands at the right, one hand on his hip and the other laid on the head of a pale gold portrait bust of an older bearded man at the left. His billowing sleeves are painted in thick creamy gold-white impasto and a heavy chain loops across his chest, catching the light. Everything else - the background wall, a suggestion of a table and shelved books at the left - sinks into warm blacks and umbers, with the light falling from the upper left in true chiaroscuro. The composition closely follows Rembrandt''s ''Aristotle with a Bust of Homer''. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: Coarse canvas weave shows plainly through the thin dark passages, which is normal for the technique. Surface glare in the photographs makes fine condition hard to judge; no tears, punctures or flaking are visible.','','','20th century copy after a 17th century composition','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A045; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8612, IMG_8613; No signature, date, label or verso photograph is available, so both the painter and the date are unknown; the identification of the composition as after Rembrandt''s ''Aristotle with a Bust of Homer'' is my inference from the imagery, not from any inscription.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8609',40.75,45.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Brown", "Gold", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(95,'ilan-95','tablo','yayinda','Large Faceted Abstract Landscape 1947, L.HASE, Signed, Framed, 1947','L.HASE. A panoramic composition split into flat interlocking planes - pale butter yellow, cream and ivory dominate the centre and sky, while wedges of plum, aubergine, teal-green and olive anchor the corners and lower edge. Thin drawn lines in cobalt and violet arc across the facets like contour marks, and a few small pale blue rectangles float at the lower left. The paint is matt and evenly brushed with soft directional strokes and no impasto, so the picture reads as a designed, almost architectural surface. The mood is bright, cool and mid-century modern. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed right of centre within the composition, in dark blue-black, reading "L.HASE 47". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: L.HASE 47. Condition: Paint film appears stable and matt with no craquelure visible. The black frame has a few small scuffs along the lower edge.','L.HASE','','dated 47 - probably 1947','oil on canvas','','','','L.HASE 47','','katalog A046; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8616, IMG_8617; The signature is painted over a dark green passage and is only partly legible - ''L.HASE 47'' is my best reading but it could be ''LEHASE'', ''L.HASSE'' or similar; the date could also be a stock number rather than a year. The support is taken to be canvas from the brush texture, but a rigid board cannot be excluded from these photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8614',51.5,28.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Beige", "Purple", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(96,'ilan-96','tablo','yayinda','Cafe Terrace Ladies Serigraph Artist Proof, Numbered Edition, Framed','A bright cafe interior seen across a chequerboard floor of pink, cream, slate and teal diamonds. In the foreground a woman in a black top rests her chin on her hand at a lime-green cloth table set with a blue teapot and cups, while a companion in a red patterned jacket leans in beside her. Behind them a yellow awning, a scarlet-clothed table and a tall window open onto blue foliage, a coral parasol and a pale balustrade. The figures are drawn with long necks, sharp bobbed hair and blank ovoid faces; the colour is laid in flat, softly grained fields typical of screenprinting on textured paper. Medium: serigraph (screenprint) on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil. Edition: A.P. 35/45 (artist''s proof, pencil). Inscribed on the reverse or mount: A.P. 35/45. Condition: Sheet looks clean and bright with no foxing or waviness visible; heavy reflections on the glass. Frame in good order.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','serigraph (screenprint) on paper','A.P. 35/45 (artist''s proof, pencil)','','','A.P. 35/45','','katalog A047; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8622, IMG_8623; The pencil signature is a clear capital ''T'' followed by a single flowing illegible line, so no name can be transcribed with confidence - it is stylistically consistent with Itzchak Tarkay but nothing in the photographs states the artist. The medium is judged serigraph from the flat grained colour fields; it could be a giclee with hand-worked passages.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8618',52.25,40.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Green", "Blue", "Yellow", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(97,'ilan-97','tablo','yayinda','Row of Poplars Over Red Fields, Signed, Framed','A wide decorative landscape reduced to bands: a glowing gold and amber sky fills the upper half, a row of eight rounded dark-green poplars marches along a thin cream horizon line, and below them broad sweeping fields of scarlet, crimson and burnt orange curve to the lower edge. There is no detail beyond the trees - the whole effect is of light and colour rather than place. The paint is applied in a heavy granular texture that catches the light like sandstone, with flecks of gold and cream scumbled over the red. Medium: acrylic with textured medium on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in black over the red field. Condition: Textured surface is intact with no flaking visible. The frame''s speckled finish shows minor rubbing at the corners.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic with textured medium on canvas','','','','','','katalog A048; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8628, IMG_8629; The signature is a fast looping script over heavy texture and is not legible at all in the supplied frames, so no name can be given. Whether the medium is acrylic or oil, and whether the texture is applied paste or gel, cannot be settled from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8624',43.0,31.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Gold", "Orange", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(98,'ilan-98','tablo','yayinda','Belle Epoque Garden Party Print, Tapestry Mount, Signed, Framed, 1900','A colour reproduction of a Belle Epoque banquet scene: dozens of women in white lace gowns and wide hats seated at cloth-laid tables beneath strings of glowing lanterns, with a dark brick facade and heavy foliage behind. The palette is smoky and warm - deep browns and blacks for the setting against cream, rose and pale green dresses, with pink and red flowers heaped on the tablecloths. The image is float-mounted with a white border onto a large floral tapestry-effect fabric panel, so the picture appears as a small bright window inside a field of woven roses and leaves. Medium: colour reproduction print on paper. Signed lower right within the printed image. Condition: Heavy glass glare in all views; tapestry mount slightly toned; no tears, losses or foxing visible.','','','late 20th century reproduction of a c.1900 painting','colour reproduction print on paper','','','','','','katalog A049; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8635, IMG_8636; The printed signature in the lower right of the image is too small to read, so the original painter is unidentified. No publisher or edition information is visible anywhere in the photographs.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8630',34.5,29.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist", "old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Green", "Black", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(99,'ilan-99','tablo','yayinda','Big Sur Land Trust Vintage Conservation Poster, Signed, Framed','A vertical poster reproducing a painting in an almost monochrome blue key: a blue-painted ladder-back chair and small round table with a bowl stand on a plank deck, looking out to layered ridges, a cloud-filled sky and a sliver of ocean where the coastline meets the sea. The handling is flat and stylised, with simplified mountain planes and soft scumbled clouds. Below the image a cream band carries the heavy blue serif lettering THE BIG SUR LAND TRUST with an address line beside it. Medium: offset lithograph poster on paper. Signed lower right of the image area, on the table top. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: THE BIG SUR LAND TRUST; BOX 1645   CARMEL, CALIFORNIA 93921. Condition: Poster paper appears slightly wavy/rippled behind the glass and lightly toned overall; heavy reflection across the upper half; no tears visible.','','THE BIG SUR LAND TRUST','1970s-1980s','offset lithograph poster on paper','','','','THE BIG SUR LAND TRUST; BOX 1645   CARMEL, CALIFORNIA 93921','','katalog A050; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8638, IMG_8639; The small painted signature at lower right cannot be read, so the poster artist is unknown. The PO box digits (read as 1645) are very small and could be misread; the zip 93921 is legible.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8637',24.25,36.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Gray", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(100,'ilan-100','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Floral Watercolour Signed Valen, Signed, Framed','Valen. A large loose watercolour in which a winged, petal-like central form spreads across the sheet in bands of cerulean, teal and coral, surrounded by drifting curtains of mauve, plum and sage wash. The paint is applied wet-into-wet with visible granulation, bloom edges and dry-brush striations, and the composition reads equally as a flower opening or a bird in flight. The palette is soft and atmospheric, with no hard outlines anywhere. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in black brush or pen, reading "Valen". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Valen. Condition: Cream mat lightly toned; strong reflections and a lamp reflection across the glass; no tears, cockling or foxing visible.','Valen','','late 20th century','watercolour on paper','','','','Valen','','katalog A051; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8643, IMG_8644; The signature clearly begins ''Valen'' but ends in a long flourish, so the full surname may be longer (e.g. Valenti, Valentine, Valera). No date, title or edition anywhere.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8640',24.25,30.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "still-life", "animal"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Pink", "Green", "Blue", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(101,'ilan-101','tablo','yayinda','John Powell Conservatory Florals, Signed 194/300, Numbered Edition, Framed','John Powell. A large decorative print of a garden room: white and yellow orchids, irises, daffodils and daisies fill blue-and-white chinoiserie jars and terracotta pots ranged on wicker and lattice staging, with a mullioned window at the centre opening to distant hills and trees. The drawing is crisp and illustrative, the colour cool and high-key - lavender, buttercup yellow, sage and cobalt against cream. Pencil inscriptions in the lower margin give the edition number at left and the artist''s signature at right. Medium: colour serigraph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "John Powell". Edition: 194/300. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: John Powell; 194/300. Condition: No visible damage; some glass glare and one small dark speck on the mat above the edition number.','John Powell','','late 20th century','colour serigraph on paper','194/300','','','John Powell; 194/300','','katalog A052; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8650, IMG_8651; Cannot tell from photographs whether this is a serigraph or an offset lithograph; no plate mark or dot screen could be resolved. No title or publisher is inscribed in the visible margins.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8646',43.0,34.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "still-life"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Purple", "Yellow", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(102,'ilan-102','tablo','yayinda','Autumn River Landscape Oil Signed Fincke, Signed, Framed','Fincke. A warm-toned oil landscape: a narrow river runs from the middle distance to the lower left, mirroring a pale gold and grey-blue sunset sky, flanked by rust and ochre deciduous trees and one tall dark conifer at right. Foreground banks are worked in dry, scrubby strokes of umber and straw, with scattered boulders at the water''s edge. The paint is thinly brushed over a visible canvas weave with lighter impasto in the clouds and the sunlit foliage. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower left of the canvas, in dark blue paint with an underline, reading "Fincke". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Fincke. Condition: Surface glare and a slightly dull, possibly dirty varnish; no tears, punctures or flaking visible; frame ornament shows minor rubbing.','Fincke','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','Fincke','','katalog A053; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8657, IMG_8658; Signature is clearly ''Fincke'' but the artist is not otherwise identified; no date, title or verso information was photographed.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8653',36.5,29.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Brown", "Beige", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(103,'ilan-103','tablo','yayinda','Robed Figures with Birdcage, Modernist Print, Framed','A mid-century figurative composition on a heavily mottled cream and buff ground: tall, mask-faced women with dark curling hair stand in loose robes of indigo blue, ochre and olive, one holding a lute, another a spray of blue reeds, with an ornate birdcage and a low table between them. Everything is drawn in nervous black line over broad flat colour, and the background is worked in a dense stippled texture that reads like weathered plaster or fresco. The palette is restricted to indigo, rust-orange, olive and charcoal on cream. Medium: colour lithograph on textured paper. Condition: Linen mat is toned and shows brownish staining along the upper and left margins; the sheet itself is toned; glass glare throughout.','','','mid to late 20th century','colour lithograph on textured paper','','','','','','katalog A054; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8662, IMG_8663; No signature, title, edition or publisher is visible in any frame, and the margins are hidden by the mat. The medium is a judgement from the flat colour and stippled ground - it could equally be a serigraph, a lithograph or a gouache on textured paper.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8659',39.75,31.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Gold", "Beige", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(104,'ilan-104','tablo','yayinda','Mike Eruzione 1984 Olympic Art Collection Print, Signed, Framed, 1984','Mike Eruzione. A near-white field is slashed with blue skate-blade strokes and spatter, a broad crimson smear at the upper left, and one thick black sweep curving down the centre like a stick blade in motion. The marks are gestural and violent, in the manner of action painting, with dozens of thin scored lines crossing the surface. Below the marks, painted in heavy black, is the printed inscription M. ERUZIONE 80, and above it a personal dedication has been added in black marker. Medium: offset lithograph print on paper. Signed upper right of the image; printed name at right and a hand-written marker dedication above it, reading "M. ERUZIONE 80". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Ken S[illegible] / All my Best / M. Eruzione (hand-written in marker); M. ERUZIONE 80; 1984 OLYMPIC GAMES ART COLLECTION; Budweiser - Proud Sponsor of the U.S. Olympic Games. Condition: The paper label on the back is creased and wrinkled; the sheet itself shows no tears; heavy glare and reflections through the glass.','Mike Eruzione','','1984','offset lithograph print on paper','','','','Ken S[illegible] / All my Best / M. Eruzione (hand-written in marker); M. ERUZIONE 80; 1984 OLYMPIC GAMES ART COLLECTION','','katalog A055; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8667, IMG_8668; The hand-written dedication''s first line (a first name plus surname beginning with S) cannot be read with confidence. Whether this sheet is a printed edition or the original worked surface cannot be settled from photographs; no edition number appears anywhere.','A printed descriptive label from the 1984 Olympic Games Art Collection is taped to the backing board; it is biographical, not a certificate of authenticity','IMG_8664',24.25,33.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Red", "Blue", "Black", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(105,'ilan-105','tablo','yayinda','Beryl Cook ''Taxi'' Signed Limited Edition Print, Numbered Edition, Framed','Beryl Cook. Beryl Cook''s characteristic rotund figures crowd the picture: a woman in a scarlet dress, black tights and magenta stilettos is heaved into the open door of a black cab by a man in a pale green suit, while two grinning passengers already inside lean out to help. The street is a chalky mint green with pale paving slabs and a yellow kerb line, and a wintry townscape of shuttered buildings and a crane fills the background. The handling is smooth and flat with soft airbrushed modelling and strong dark outlines. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Beryl Cook". Edition: 51/300. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Taxi; Beryl Cook; 51/300. Condition: No visible damage, foxing or cockling; some glass glare and a reflection of the room across the lower half.','Beryl Cook','Taxi','late 20th century','colour lithograph on paper','51/300','','','Taxi; Beryl Cook; 51/300','','katalog A056; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8673, IMG_8674; The print process (lithograph vs serigraph) cannot be confirmed from photographs, and no publisher or blindstamp is visible in the shown margins.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8670',36.25,31.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Red", "Black", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(106,'ilan-106','tablo','yayinda','Kent R. Wallis Blossoming Mountain Valley Oil, Signed, Framed','Kent R. Wallis. A high-key impressionist landscape: a pale dirt lane curves in from the lower right past banks of rose-pink and magenta blossom and dark blue-green trees toward a cluster of small white-roofed houses, with hazy violet mountains and a brilliant blue sky of piled white cumulus above. The paint is laid on thickly with a loaded brush and palette knife, so the blossom and clouds stand in visible ridges of impasto. Colour is cool and saturated - cobalt, lavender, white and hot pink. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower centre-left of the canvas, in dark paint, reading "Kent R. Wallis". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Kent R. Wallis. Condition: No visible damage; impasto intact; some specular glare off the paint surface in the raking views.','Kent R. Wallis','','late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','Kent R. Wallis','','katalog A057; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8680, IMG_8681; No date, title or verso information was photographed.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8676',37.0,29.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "White", "Black", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(107,'ilan-107','tablo','yayinda','Charcoal Reclining Figure Study on Toned Paper, Framed, 1974','A gestural charcoal study on warm terracotta-toned paper: a heavily hatched horizontal bar with turned legs runs across the upper half like a table or bed frame, while below and around it long sweeping contour lines describe a reclining body, a raised knee and a dropped arm. The drawing is deliberately unfinished, with smudged shadow in the hatching and large areas of bare toned paper left as light. Only greys and blacks appear against the salmon ground. Medium: charcoal and graphite on toned paper. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 9/12/74. Condition: Sheet is uniformly warm-toned (probably as made); no tears or foxing visible; a small illegible pencil note sits on the mat at lower left; heavy glass reflections.','','','dated 1974','charcoal and graphite on toned paper','','','','9/12/74','','katalog A058; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8685, IMG_8686; The drawing is dated 9/12/74 in ink at lower right but carries no legible signature, so the artist is unknown. The subject is ambiguous - it reads as a reclining nude with a table or bed, but the forms are abstracted enough that another reading is possible. There is an illegible pencil inscription on the mat at lower left.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8682',33.5,27.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "nude", "figurative"], "medium": ["charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Gray", "Beige", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(108,'ilan-108','tablo','yayinda','Orca Pod Watercolour on Deckle-Edged Handmade Paper, Signed, Framed','A wide panoramic image in the softest of palettes: tall black dorsal fins and glossy grey-black backs break a mirror-flat sea, with pale reflections dropping beneath them, while behind rise layer upon layer of blue-grey conifer ridges and a snowy summit dissolving into mist. Everything is built from delicate graded washes with almost no hard edge - the far mountains are barely more than a tint. The sheet has ragged deckled edges on all four sides and is float-mounted on a grey mat so the deckle shows. Medium: watercolour on handmade paper. Signed on the grey mat below the sheet, right of centre, in pencil. Condition: Two small white spots/losses on the grey mat just below the sheet; sheet itself clean with intact deckle edges; strong glass reflections in every view.','','','late 20th century','watercolour on handmade paper','','','','','','katalog A059; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8693, IMG_8694; The pencil signature under the sheet is a flourish that cannot be read, and no title or edition number could be found - so it is unclear whether this is an original watercolour or an airbrushed/embossed print on handmade paper.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8689',40.75,20.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Green", "White", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(109,'ilan-109','tablo','yayinda','Antique Alpine Landscape Oil in Gilt Frame, Framed','A darkly atmospheric alpine view: a bare-branched birch rises at the centre left against a wall of plum-brown crags, while a brilliant white snow peak catches the light in the gap between them and a small chalet with a red roof sits on a green shoulder at the right. The foreground is a broad sweep of dry ochre grass with scattered rocks and rust-red scrub. The paint is thin, blended and heavily toned by an old varnish, so the whole picture reads in browns, olives and slate blue with the snow as its single bright note. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: Varnish is darkened and the surface looks dusty; the frame''s gesso ornament shows rubbing and small losses at the corners; no tears or obvious flaking seen in these views.','','','late 19th to early 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A060; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8705, IMG_8706; No signature could be found in any corner and the back was not photographed, so both artist and date are unknown; the age estimate is from the frame type and the darkened varnish only.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8695',42.4,28.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Green", "Gray", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(110,'ilan-110','tablo','yayinda','Alpine Farmhouse and Lake Oil Painting, Framed','A broad valley scene painted with a loaded brush: a weathered chalet with a shingled roof, red-shuttered windows and a small water wheel sits on a grassy bank at left under an autumnal tree, with a rail fence running down the slope. Beyond, a green-blue lake curves away toward jagged snow mountains under towering cream and white cumulus. Colour is bright and decorative - sky blue, olive, russet and cream - and the sky carries a dense network of fine craquelure. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: Fine overall craquelure is clearly visible across the sky and clouds; frame gilding rubbed at the corners; no tears or losses seen.','','','mid 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A061; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8710, IMG_8711; No signature is legible in any corner and the back was not photographed, so the artist and date are unknown.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8707',32.5,24.6,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Green", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(111,'ilan-111','tablo','yayinda','Italian Market Scene Oil Signed Forelli, Signed, Framed','Forelli. A genre scene set in a shadowy arcade: at the centre a barefoot woman in a green bodice and dark skirt carries an armful of oranges and flowers past a heap of dark green watermelons stacked on straw, while a crowd of townspeople in hats, shawls and long coats stands beneath a tall stone arch behind. The tonality is subdued and earthy - olive, umber and grey with accents of orange, rose and teal in the clothing - and the paint is brushed loosely with soft edges throughout. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark paint, reading "Forelli-". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Forelli-. Condition: Frame has noticeable losses and abrasion to the carved gesso with red bole exposed at several points; painting surface has a dull, slightly grimy varnish; no tears visible.','Forelli','','early to mid 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','Forelli-','','katalog A062; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8716, IMG_8717; The signature''s first letter is ambiguous - it may read ''Torelli'' rather than ''Forelli''. No date, title or verso information was photographed, and canvas vs board could not be confirmed.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8712',32.0,27.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Orange", "Beige", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(112,'ilan-112','tablo','yayinda','Parisian Shopfronts Painting Signed Thomas 1979, Signed, Framed, 1979','Thomas. A wide, flat-perspective view along a Paris pavement, painted in a crisp hard-edge style: from the left a grey-green cafe front lettered AUX BONS ENFANTS, then a cream facade with arched windows, clipped bay trees and the HOTEL de PARIS doorway, a blue-and-white striped awning over CAFE TABAC BAR, and finally a violet ANTIQUITES shop with a picture and candlesticks in its window against a peach stucco wall. Colour is cool and graphic - violet-blue, cobalt, dove grey and cream, with pink stucco and mottled weathered patches - and the empty grey pavement runs unbroken across the foreground. No figures appear anywhere. Medium: acrylic on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in black, reading "THOMAS 79". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: THOMAS 79; AUX BONS ENFANTS; CAFE  THE  VINS; HOTEL de PARIS. Condition: No visible damage to the painted surface; the black frame shows light scuffing along the top edge.','Thomas','','dated 1979','acrylic on canvas','','','','THOMAS 79; AUX BONS ENFANTS; CAFE  THE  VINS','','katalog A063; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8722, IMG_8723; Only the surname ''Thomas'' is given, so the artist cannot be pinned down. Acrylic vs oil cannot be settled from photographs, and canvas vs board is inferred from the stretcher-like edge.','no certificate or label photographed; the back was not shown','IMG_8718',39.25,25.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative", "document"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Gray", "Black", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(113,'ilan-113','tablo','yayinda','Asemic Calligraphy on Handmade Petal Paper, Uzilevsky, Signed, Framed','Uzilevsky. Four ruled staves carry rows of sweeping black brush characters that read like writing but spell nothing, looping and doubling back across a soft blush-pink sheet. The paper itself is the second subject: handmade, deckled and thickly flecked with pressed petals, blue and violet flower heads and a whole fern frond caught in the pulp. Small accents of rust-red, ochre and slate blue flicker inside the black strokes, and a faint gold rectangle is drawn at the lower centre. Deep taupe mat with black-and-cream core lines, in a carved champagne-silver moulding under glass. Medium: serigraph on handmade paper with pressed botanical inclusions. Signed lower right of the image, in pencil, reading "Uzilevsky ... ''82". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Uzilevsky ... ''82 (pencil, within the image at lower right; a looped mark or paraph sits between the name and the date). Condition: No damage visible through the glass. Heavy reflections of a window and the photographer across the glazing; the pressed botanical inclusions are original to the sheet, not foxing.','Uzilevsky','','dated ''82 - early 1980s','serigraph on handmade paper with pressed botanical inclusions','','','','Uzilevsky ... ''82 (pencil, within the image at lower right; a looped mark or paraph sits between the name and the date)','','katalog A064; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8728, IMG_8729; Medium is the main open question: the ruled lines and the flat, even black of the strokes point to a screenprint, but the varied stroke weight and the transparent colour inside the marks would also fit an original ink-and-watercolour drawing. No edition fraction is visible anywhere. The pencil mark between ''Uzilevsky'' and "''82" could be a numeral or just a flourish; I could not resolve it.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8724',36.5,30.1,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Gray", "Gold", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(114,'ilan-114','tablo','yayinda','Woman in White with Basket of Flowers, Frosall, Signed, Framed','Frosall. A young woman stands three-quarter turned in a garden, her long copper hair blown back and a loose white dress falling in heavy folds to her feet. On her hip she balances a wicker basket crammed with red and white daisies and carnations, echoed by a bank of red flowers at her knees. The background is worked in broad palette-knife slabs of powder blue, lavender and pale grey, so the figure reads as the only solid form in a shimmering, weather-like field. Thick buttery impasto throughout, especially in the dress and the flowers. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed left of centre, painted into the blue-grey background beside the dress, reading "Frosall". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Frosall (painted signature, background left of the figure). Condition: No visible damage, tears or losses; surface is glossy and the impasto is intact. Some flash glare on the varnish in the detail shots.','Frosall','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','Frosall (painted signature, background left of the figure)','','katalog A065; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8738, IMG_8739; The signature is a loose cursive scrawl in paint; ''Frosall'' is my best reading but ''Frosell'', ''Fresall'' or ''Trosall'' are all possible. I did not find a label, stamp or stretcher inscription - the back was not photographed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8731',41.0,48.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "old-masters", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["White", "Blue", "Purple", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(115,'ilan-115','tablo','yayinda','Old Master Style Still Life with Pineapple, J. Mattison, Signed, Framed','J. Mattison. A generous heap of fruit is piled on a pale stone ledge against a deep, almost black-brown ground: a small pineapple at the centre, bunches of pale green and dusky red grapes with their vine leaves, ripe peaches, two yellow-green pears and a scatter of wild strawberries in front. A shallow duck-egg blue bowl holds more peaches at the left. The palette is the classic Dutch-revival one - warm amber, russet and green lifted out of a dark chiaroscuro background - and the paint is smooth and blended with glossy highlights on each fruit. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in red-brown paint, reading "J. Mattison". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: J. Mattison (painted signature, lower right). Condition: The painting is wrapped in clear plastic film, which creases and reflects across the surface in every shot and hides fine condition detail. No tears, punctures or obvious losses visible; no craquelure detectable through the film.','J. Mattison','','late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','J. Mattison (painted signature, lower right)','','katalog A066; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8744, IMG_8745; The signature could equally read ''J. Mattson'' or ''J. Matteson''. The protective plastic wrap prevents any real condition assessment of the paint surface and varnish.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8740',40.5,28.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Orange", "Green", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(116,'ilan-116','tablo','yayinda','Orientalist Bath Scene with Seated Nude, Signed, Framed','A pale-skinned nude sits on a carpet-draped divan with her back to the viewer, long auburn hair falling over one shoulder and a white towel across her lap, her head turned towards a shaft of light from a doorway. Behind her a flight of marble steps climbs to a turquoise pool where a second figure in a saffron robe and headscarf crouches. In the foreground are the props of the bath: a shallow brass basin, a copper bowl and a bulbous red-orange ewer. The palette is a cool grey-green architecture against warm flesh, orange and copper accents; handling is smooth and academic. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right, painted in dark colour and partly under the frame rebate. Condition: No tears or losses visible; surface glossy with strong flash glare in the detail shots. Corners of the gilt frame show minor rubbing.','','','20th century, after a 19th-century orientalist composition','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A067; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8750, IMG_8751; The signature is legible only as a capital that looks like ''M'' before the strokes disappear into dark paint and the frame rebate - I would not guess the rest. The composition closely follows a 19th-century orientalist bath subject, so this is very likely a later copy or version rather than an original of that period, but I cannot confirm that from the photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8746',28.2,32.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["asian", "old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Black", "Gold", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(117,'ilan-117','tablo','yayinda','Red Poppies on a Golden Field, Signed, Framed','Eight or nine scarlet poppy heads on slender green stems fill a nearly square canvas, the largest opening at the upper centre like a small sun. Everything is built from thick granular dabs of paint - the flowers are dense mounds of vermilion and crimson, the ground behind is a stippled blaze of chrome yellow, gold and emerald flecks that reads as sunlight through grass. The impasto stands proud enough to cast its own shadows, giving the surface a crusted, almost mosaic texture. Medium: oil on canvas, heavy impasto. Signed lower right of the canvas, scratched into the impasto in dark paint. Condition: No visible damage; the impasto is intact with no flaking seen. Strong flash reflection off the raised paint in the detail shots.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas, heavy impasto','','','','','','katalog A068; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8756, IMG_8757; A signature-like scrawl sits in the paint at the lower right (visible in IMG_8753) but it is completely swallowed by the surrounding texture and I could not read a single letter. No date, label or stamp was photographed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8752',33.0,33.3,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Yellow", "Green", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(118,'ilan-118','tablo','yayinda','Two Cats Beneath a Red Sun, Framed','Two long-eared cats - one blue-grey and striped, one brown and tabby - sit shoulder to shoulder with their tails curled, staring out with wide almond eyes, red noses and neat white whiskers. Above them a crimson sun bursts into a halo of fine red rays, beside a second disc laid in real gold leaf on a slate-grey block. The ground is a patchwork of ochre, cobalt, crimson and cream squares scattered with dotted rosettes and little painted flags, all worked over a thick, deliberately cracked and scratched plaster-like surface. Warm, decorative and Mediterranean in feeling. Medium: acrylic and gold leaf on textured canvas. Condition: The fine crackle across the surface is a deliberate craquelure finish, not damage. No tears, losses or flaking seen; gold leaf passages are intact.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic and gold leaf on textured canvas','','','','','','katalog A069; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8762, IMG_8763; No signature was found in any of the four views of the picture, so the artist is unattributed. Medium is judged from the matte, chalky surface and the crackle ground - acrylic with a modelling paste is most likely, but an oil-and-mixed-media build-up would look similar in photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8758',26.3,30.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["folk", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gold", "Blue", "Red", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(119,'ilan-119','tablo','yayinda','Classical Nude Collaged in Gilded Relief Panel, Framed','At the centre a smooth photographic reproduction of a classical standing nude - one arm raised above her head, the other tipping a jar from which water pours - is collaged onto a deep charcoal field. Around her the surface erupts: thick pale scrolls and coils are trowelled on like piped icing, sheets of gold and copper leaf are laid over swirling combed patterns, and torn patches of crimson, olive and cream break in at the edges. The contrast between the cool, sharply-printed figure and the crusty metallic relief is the whole point of the piece. Presented in a slim gold frame. Medium: mixed media on canvas - printed image, modelling paste relief and metal leaf. Condition: Some of the raised relief is chipped or abraded at the left edge where the pale scrolls meet the dark ground, exposing the layer beneath; this may be an intentional distressed finish. No tears in the canvas visible.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','mixed media on canvas - printed image, modelling paste relief and metal leaf','','','','','','katalog A070; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8768, IMG_8769; The central figure is a printed reproduction of a well-known 19th-century academic nude rather than a hand-painted passage - the tonal smoothness and the sharp edge against the impasto make that clear - but no title, plate mark or publisher line is visible to identify the source. Unsigned. Whether the chipping at the left edge is damage or a deliberate distressed effect cannot be settled from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8764',28.2,32.4,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gold", "Gray", "Beige", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(120,'ilan-120','tablo','yayinda','Night Garden in Blue, Signed and Numbered 16/50, Numbered Edition, Framed','A near-black bush or clipped topiary rises at the centre of a wall of ultramarine and violet, its silhouette dissolving into loose calligraphic scribbles of black and pale blue that suggest railings, benches and a lamp standard. Along the bottom third the picture explodes into broad flat petals of teal, crimson, cream and acid yellow - a bank of flowers caught by artificial light. The handling is fast and gestural throughout, printed with the flat overlapping colour of a hand-pulled screenprint. The deckle-edged sheet is float-mounted on a white mat in a thin black metal frame. Medium: serigraph (screenprint) on deckle-edged paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, after a handwritten title line. Edition: 16/50. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 16/50 (pencil, lower left margin). Condition: Sheet appears clean with no foxing or waviness visible through the glass; deckle edges intact. Heavy window and room reflections across the glazing.','','','late 20th century','serigraph (screenprint) on deckle-edged paper','16/50','','','16/50 (pencil, lower left margin)','','katalog A071; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8774, IMG_8775; The pencil line in the lower right margin carries a handwritten title, what may be a date, and the artist''s signature, but the graphite is faint against the paper and shot at an angle; I could resolve only fragments (a word ending in ''-ge'', possibly ''1928'', and possibly the word ''gouache'') and will not guess the title or the name. The edition fraction ''16/50'' is clear. Medium is judged from the flat overlapping colour areas; a fine offset lithograph would look similar at this resolution.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8770',40.2,30.8,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "seascape", "landscape", "still-life"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Purple", "Red", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(121,'ilan-121','tablo','yayinda','Art Deco Salon with Manhattan Skyline, McKnight, Signed, Framed','McKnight. Three tall arched windows with radiating fanlights fill the back wall of an elegant salon and open onto a dusk-blue skyline of setback skyscrapers and a terrace balustrade. Inside, everything is flattened into crisp decorative shapes: a powder-blue settee heaped with stylised red roses, a scalloped peach wing chair, a grey neoclassical fireplace, a spiky black palm, a fluted uplighter and a bowl of peaches on a wrought-iron table. The palette is pale and cool - lilac, dusty pink, powder blue, mint - laid down in flat, evenly graded areas typical of a hand-pulled serigraph. Float-mounted on a broad cream mat with a gold fillet in a pale ivory frame. Medium: serigraph (screenprint) on paper. Signed lower right, on the sheet below the image, reading "McKnight". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: McKnight (cursive signature, lower right below the image). Condition: No foxing, tears or discolouration visible through the glass. Considerable reflection and a photographer''s silhouette across the glazing in most views.','McKnight','','1980s to 1990s','serigraph (screenprint) on paper','','','','McKnight (cursive signature, lower right below the image)','','katalog A072; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8780, IMG_8781; The signature is cursive and read at an angle through glass; ''McKnight'' is my best transcription but the middle letters are ambiguous. No edition fraction or publisher line is visible - if one exists it is hidden under the mat, since only the signature clears the mat opening.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8776',36.6,34.4,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Black", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(122,'ilan-122','tablo','yayinda','Yachts of the America''s Cup: The Schooner, Thompson, Signed in the Plate, Framed','Thompson. A black-hulled schooner drives from left to right under a full press of cream canvas, the Stars and Stripes at her masthead, her wake breaking green-white beneath the bow. The sea is a deep bottle green worked in short choppy strokes; the sky behind is a warm haze of cream and grey through which a square-rigger and the chalky bulk of the coast loom half-dissolved. The mood is quiet and atmospheric rather than dramatic. Presented on a printed mount with a titled caption panel, double-matted in slate grey and cream in an oak frame. Medium: offset lithograph on paper, hand-signed. Signed twice - printed within the image at lower left, and hand-signed in pencil on the mount at lower right, reading "Thompson". Edition: Special Edition. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Yachts of the America''s Cup; THE SCHOONER; On August 22, 1851, the yacht America outsailed the whole British fleet in a race around the Isle of Wight. The nearest British yacht to her, Aurora, finished 8 minutes after the America. America is pictured at the Nab Light with the rest of the fleet following her into Sandown Bay. The 100 Guinea Cup she won was renamed in her honor ''The America''s Cup''.; Special Edition (pencil, lower left of the mount). Condition: No foxing or staining visible; mats clean and square. Heavy glare and a photographer''s silhouette across the glazing in the frontal shot.','Thompson','Yachts of the America''s Cup - THE SCHOONER','late 20th century','offset lithograph on paper, hand-signed','Special Edition','','','Yachts of the America''s Cup; THE SCHOONER; On August 22, 1851, the yacht America outsailed the whole British fleet in a race around the Isle of Wight. The nearest British yacht to her, Aurora, finished 8 minutes after the America. America is pictured at the Nab Light with the rest of the fleet following her into Sandown Bay. The 100 Guinea Cup she won was renamed in her honor ''The America''s Cup''.','','katalog A073; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8788, IMG_8789; The pencil signature on the mount ends clearly in ''-hompson'' but the given name or initials in front of it are a flourish I cannot resolve, so I have recorded only the surname. ''Special Edition'' is written where an edition fraction would normally sit, so no numbered edition size is stated. Medium is judged as a photomechanical print from the smooth continuous tone and the printed caption panel, but I could not see a dot screen or plate mark at this resolution.','no certificate photographed; the printed caption panel on the mount carries the title and historical note','IMG_8782',30.5,24.9,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Green", "Gray", "Brown"]}'::jsonb),
(123,'ilan-123','tablo','yayinda','Green Branching Form on Sand Ground, Crespi, Signed, Framed','Crespi. A single sage-green shape spreads diagonally across a small square sheet, its body pierced by pale oval voids so that it reads at once as a lichen, a canopy of leaves and a run of arches. The green is soft and granular, as though brushed onto damp paper, and it sits on a warm sand-and-oatmeal ground flecked with grey. Everything else is empty. Wide pencil margins carry the edition number at the left and the artist''s signature at the right; the sheet is double-matted in cream and deep mocha with a silver bevel, inside a broad brushed champagne frame. Medium: giclee print on textured rag paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Crespi". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Crespi (pencil, lower right margin). Condition: No foxing, cockling or tears visible through the glass; mats clean. Strong reflections across the glazing.','Crespi','','late 20th to early 21st century','giclee print on textured rag paper','','','','Crespi (pencil, lower right margin)','','katalog A074; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8793, IMG_8794; A pencil edition fraction sits in the lower left margin but the numerator is cut off by the photograph''s edge and the graphite is too faint to read; the denominator looks like ''600'', which would match the 600-piece series stated on the certificate photographed with A075, so this is probably a companion print from the same edition - but I could not confirm the number and have left edition_read null. The signature is a compact cursive; ''Crespi'' is my best reading.','no certificate photographed for this listing','IMG_8790',30.2,30.55,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Green", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(124,'ilan-124','tablo','yayinda','R. Crespi, ''Agee''s Mark'', Giclee 22/600, R. CRESP. (certificate); Crespi (pencil signature on the sheet), Signed…','R. CRESP. (certificate); Crespi (pencil signature on the sheet). A soft sage-green mass spreads across the upper half of the sheet and drops into four squat rounded piers, so the image hovers between a wind-shaped tree and a little arcaded ruin. The green is applied in a granular, absorbent wash that fades to blue-grey at the edges; behind it the ground is a mottled sand and putty field with a faint darker halo around the form. Wide untouched margins, pencil-numbered at the left and pencil-signed at the right. Cream inner mat over a deep mocha mat, in a slim brushed silver-gold frame under glass. Medium: giclee on Arches paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Crespi". Edition: Edition No. 22 of a series edition of 600, plus A/P up to 10%. Accompanied by a certificate: Printed certificate of authenticity for a giclee on Arches paper, artist R. Cresp(i), title ''Agee''s Mark'', series edition 600 with A/P up to 10%, this copy Edition No. 22, signed by the artist and by the publisher Art & Frame Source; the word ''Distributor'' is misspelled ''Distrbutor'' on the form. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: CERTIFICATE OF AUTHENTICITY; This numbered edition is from an authentic single limited publication produced using the Giclee method of printing and is approved, signed and numbered by the artist. The edition has been independently tested for light-fast inks and acid-free papers. The artist and publisher hereby affirm the Authenticity of this limited edition certificate.; Artist: R. CRESP.; Title: Agee''s Mark. Condition: Print clean with no foxing or cockling visible. The certificate is creased from folding and has a handwritten stock number in one corner. Reflections and a photographer''s silhouette across the glazing.','R. CRESP. (certificate); Crespi (pencil signature on the sheet)','Agee''s Mark','late 20th to early 21st century','giclee on Arches paper','Edition No. 22 of a series edition of 600, plus A/P up to 10%','','','CERTIFICATE OF AUTHENTICITY; This numbered edition is from an authentic single limited publication produced using the Giclee method of printing and is approved, signed and numbered by the artist. The edition has been independently tested for light-fast inks and acid-free papers. The artist and publisher hereby affirm the Authenticity of this limited edition certificate.; Artist: R. CRESP.','','katalog A075; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8799, IMG_8800; The artist''s name on the certificate is handwritten and abbreviated - it reads ''R. CRESP.'' with the last letters run together, and the pencil signature on the sheet reads ''Crespi''; I have recorded both as written rather than resolving them. The pencil edition fraction on the sheet itself is too faint to read cleanly (it looks like a two-digit numerator over 600), so the edition number 22 is taken from the certificate. The certificate was photographed with this listing; A074 is an almost identically sized companion print by the same hand, so the possibility that the certificate belongs to that one instead cannot be excluded from the photographs alone.','Printed certificate of authenticity for a giclee on Arches paper, artist R. Cresp(i), title ''Agee''s Mark'', series edition 600 with A/P up to 10%, this copy Edition No. 22, signed by the artist and by the publisher Art & Frame Source; the word ''Distributor'' is misspelled ''Distrbutor'' on the form.','IMG_8796',30.0,30.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Green", "Beige", "Silver"]}'::jsonb),
(125,'ilan-125','tablo','yayinda','Cubist Group of Figures with Musician, B. Kemer, Signed, Framed','B. Kemer. Four attenuated figures with mask-like faces - blank oval heads, one enormous almond eye apiece - stand close together against a pale gridded window. The nearest is a slender nude in bone-white and cream; behind her, figures in crimson, chrome yellow and rose crowd forward, and at the right one cradles a lute or mandolin. The lower half of the canvas turns into broad slabs of forest green, teal, crimson and gold, so the bodies seem to rise out of a field of colour. The paint is loaded and worked with a knife as much as a brush, with visible ridges and scraped edges. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark red-brown over the green passage, reading "B. Kemer". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: B. Kemer (painted signature, lower right). Condition: Paint surface intact with no flaking or losses seen. A small white scuff or paint fleck sits in the green passage near the signature. The gesso ornament on the frame shows light rubbing on the high points, consistent with its antiqued finish.','B. Kemer','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','B. Kemer (painted signature, lower right)','','katalog A076; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8806, IMG_8807; The signature is small, cursive and painted wet-in-wet; ''B. Kemer'' is my best reading and ''B. Kemez'', ''B. Kamer'' or ''B. Komer'' are all plausible alternatives. No date, label or stretcher inscription was photographed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8801',30.8,35.6,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "landscape", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Yellow", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(126,'ilan-126','tablo','yayinda','Country Road with Red House and Horse Cart, Framed','A sandy road runs from the lower right into the middle distance, flanked on the left by a stand of tall bare-branched trees and on the right by a two-storey red brick house with a green roof. Two men in dark coats stand on the verge watching a white horse and cart go by; a small group in long dark clothes waits by the house wall. The sky is a pale wash of buttermilk and eggshell blue, the fields a dry olive and ochre, and the whole thing is painted flatly and rather stiffly, in the naive manner, with the trees drawn in thin dark lines against the light. Set in a deep cerused oak frame with a gold inner lip. Medium: oil on canvas board. Condition: The surface has an aged, slightly dirty varnish with a warm yellow cast, and small dark specks scattered across the sky. A patch of scuffing or abrasion shows on the gold inner lip at the lower centre. No tears or losses visible.','','','mid 20th century','oil on canvas board','','','','','','katalog A077; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8811, IMG_8812; I could not find a legible signature in any of the three views; some dark marks at the lower right of the image may be a signature but resolve to nothing at this resolution. The support is judged to be board rather than stretched canvas from the flat, unyielding surface, but no back view was photographed to confirm it, and no age can be fixed without one.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8808',30.25,24.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas", "panel"], "style": ["impressionist", "folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Red", "Gold", "Brown"]}'::jsonb),
(127,'ilan-127','tablo','yayinda','Still Life with Fruit Bowl, Bottle and Bananas, Framed','A dark wooden bowl heaped with oranges, a yellow apple and green fruit sits at the centre of a table covered in a heavy rose-pink cloth whose folds are blocked in with broad strokes. Around it: three red apples and a green apple in front, a bunch of yellow bananas to the right, a slender gold champagne flute, and a squat brown bottle with a pale label whose lettering dissolves into brushwork. Behind everything hangs a curtain of deep midnight blue and black, giving the warm fruit a dramatic lift. The handling is soft and painterly, with visible brush marks and no fussy detail. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: No tears, losses or craquelure visible; the linen liner is clean. Some flash glare across the darker passages.','','','late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A078; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8816, IMG_8817; No signature was found in any of the four views. The bottle carries a painted label but the lettering is only suggested by brushstrokes and cannot be read. The support is judged to be canvas from the visible weave at the edges, but no back view was photographed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8813',33.1,27.65,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life", "document"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Black", "Orange", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(128,'ilan-128','tablo','yayinda','Japanese Ink Landscape Scroll, Unzen Mountains, Signed, Framed','A tall hanging scroll painted in ink and pale washes on paper: a jagged peak rises through banks of cloud at the top, while below it wooded ridges are built up from thousands of short green and black dabs. A tiny ochre gate or torii sits on the slope at the left, the only man-made note in the composition. The palette is restrained - lamp-black, sage and moss green, faint ochre - against warm cream paper, and the whole scroll is mounted on a pale grey-green silk brocade and set inside a tall dark wood frame under glass. Medium: ink and light colour on paper, mounted as a hanging scroll. Signed lower left of the painting, followed by two red seals. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Brush inscription in two columns at lower left, partly legible: ''於雲仙仁田峠 望普賢'' (approximately ''At Unzen, Nita Pass, looking toward Fugen''); a shorter signature column to its left is not legible; Two square red seals below the inscription. Condition: Paper lightly toned with faint horizontal roll creases across the sky; a few small pale marks in the upper area; heavy ceiling-light glare on the glass in all photographs.','','','mid to late 20th century','ink and light colour on paper, mounted as a hanging scroll','','','','Brush inscription in two columns at lower left, partly legible: ''於雲仙仁田峠 望普賢'' (approximately ''At Unzen, Nita Pass, looking toward Fugen''); a shorter signature column to its left is not legible; Two square red seals below the inscription','','katalog A079; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8821, IMG_8822; The place-name reading of the inscription (Unzen / Nita Pass / Fugen) is my best reading of a cursive brush hand and should be verified; the artist''s signature column and both seals are not legible, so no name is recorded.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8818',23.25,79.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["ink", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Green", "Beige", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(129,'ilan-129','tablo','yayinda','Cassiopeias Gardon I, Signed Limited Edition Print, IRON SCHIO, Numbered Edition, Framed','IRON SCHIO. A large horizontal composition on a mottled gold and bronze ground. A deep blue half-disc filled with a faint constellation diagram dominates the upper half, carrying a white full moon at its centre, and slender white crescents and a spiral drift around it. Below, a house with a red gable and a lit doorway sits beside flat triangular mountains in sage green, silver and slate blue, with a small red sun and a stylised red-leafed plant rising through the middle. Colours are matt and chalky - antique gold, cobalt, oxblood red, olive and plum - and the sheet is presented under a deep white mat in a narrow pewter-silver frame. Medium: serigraph (screenprint) with metallic gold ground on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "IRON SCHIO". Edition: 51/450. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: CASSIOPEIAS GARDON I (pencil, lower left margin); 51/450 (pencil, lower centre margin); IRON SCHIO (pencil, lower right margin). Condition: No visible damage; mat and print appear clean, some reflection on the glass.','IRON SCHIO','CASSIOPEIAS GARDON I','late 20th century','serigraph (screenprint) with metallic gold ground on paper','51/450','','','CASSIOPEIAS GARDON I (pencil, lower left margin); 51/450 (pencil, lower centre margin); IRON SCHIO (pencil, lower right margin)','','katalog A080; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8829, IMG_8830; The pencil signature is hand-printed and ambiguous - it reads as ''IRON SCHIO'' but could equally be ''INON SCHIO'' or similar; the title is written ''GARDON'' although ''Garden'' is clearly intended. Serigraph vs. high-quality offset with metallic ink cannot be settled from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8823',51.25,39.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Blue", "Red", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(130,'ilan-130','tablo','yayinda','Windmill and Cottages, Signed Watercolour, Signed, Framed','A watercolour of a working windmill seen from below: the white-washed tower and its lattice sails fill the upper right, wrapped by a red-brown timber gallery, while a half-timbered cottage with a red roof stands at the left. The sky is worked in broad grey-buff washes that suggest driving cloud, and the foreground is scratched and stippled with dry-brush strokes for grass, figures and hens. The palette is muted - ochre, brick red, olive and slate grey - and the sheet is float-mounted on a deep navy mat inside an ornate gilt frame. Medium: watercolour with bodycolour on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in dark ink or watercolour, reading "A. W…son (only the initial and the final letters are legible)". Condition: Sheet lightly toned; strong reflections on the glass in the detail shots make the surface hard to assess; no obvious tears or losses visible.','','','late 19th to early 20th century','watercolour with bodycolour on paper','','','','','','katalog A081; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8837, IMG_8838; The signature is only partly legible - it begins ''A. W'' and appears to end in ''son'' (possibly Wilson), but I will not commit to a name. Medium is judged as watercolour from the washes and paper; a very good facsimile print cannot be excluded because of glass glare.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8834',20.75,18.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Red", "Gray", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(131,'ilan-131','tablo','yayinda','Harbour with Moored Boats, Signed Buffet Lithograph, Maurice Buffet, Numbered Edition, Framed','Maurice Buffet. A colour lithograph of a low, wide coastline: heavy black brush-drawn masts, spars and reeds rise from an ochre foreshore scattered with pebbles, while two dark boats sit on the pale green water. The far shore carries a small pale town under a broad blue-and-cream sky. Drawing is loose and calligraphic, laid over flat washes of turquoise, sand and rust, with the white of the paper left open through the beach. Signed and numbered in pencil in the margin, mounted on a terracotta mat in a dark wood and gilt frame. Medium: colour lithograph on paper, pencil signed and numbered. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Maurice Buffet". Edition: 121/275. Accompanied by a certificate: Bilingual authentication sheet with a blind seal certifying an original hand-signed lithograph in an edition of 275, stones defaced after printing; supplied with a press clipping about Maurice Buffet. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Maurice Buffet (pencil signature, lower right margin); 121/275 (pencil, lower left margin); AUTHENTICATION - Société de Vérification de la Nouvelle Gravure Internationale of New York and Paris certifies and warrants that this is an original lithograph numbered and limited to an edition of 275, created and individually signed by the artist. The Society further verifies that each lithographic stone has been defaced after the limited edition was completed. The Société de Vérification de la Nouvelle Gravure has been created by The Collector''s Guild Ltd. to set and uphold the highest standards for original lithographs and etchings. (the same text follows in French); THE COLLECTOR''S GUILD LTD. • 180 MADISON AVENUE • NEW YORK, N. Y. 10016. Condition: Print and mat appear clean; the certificate and clipping are creased and lightly toned with a fold across the certificate.','Maurice Buffet','','third quarter of the 20th century','colour lithograph on paper, pencil signed and numbered','121/275','','','Maurice Buffet (pencil signature, lower right margin); 121/275 (pencil, lower left margin); AUTHENTICATION - Société de Vérification de la Nouvelle Gravure Internationale of New York and Paris certifies and warrants that this is an original lithograph numbered and limited to an edition of 275, created and individually signed by the artist. The Society further verifies that each lithographic stone has been defaced after the limited edition was completed. The Société de Vérification de la Nouvelle Gravure has been created by The Collector''s Guild Ltd. to set and uphold the highest standards for original lithographs and etchings. (the same text follows in French)','','katalog A082; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8843, IMG_8844; Note this is Maurice Buffet, not Bernard Buffet - the signature, the certificate wording and the press clipping all agree. Nothing else uncertain.','Bilingual authentication sheet with a blind seal certifying an original hand-signed lithograph in an edition of 275, stones defaced after printing; supplied with a press clipping about Maurice Buffet.','IMG_8840',25.0,19.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Blue", "Black", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(132,'ilan-132','tablo','yayinda','Groombridge, Signed Tom Caldwell Cottage Print, Numbered Edition, Framed, 1989','Tom Caldwell. A finely detailed view of a Kentish cottage: a steep thatched roof and a tall brick chimney stack rise above white-plastered walls crossed by dark half-timbering, and a clipped hedge, brick pier and picket gate run along the front. The whole image is built from a dense stipple of tiny strokes that gives the foliage a frosted, granular look. The palette is cool and almost monochrome - slate blue-grey, chalk white, muted brick red and pale sky. Wide cream mat in a deep mahogany-toned moulding under glass. Medium: offset fine-art reproduction after an egg tempera painting, pencil signed and numbered. Signed lower left margin, in pencil, reading "Tom Caldwell". Edition: 761/1100 (edition size 1100 plus 110 artist''s proofs, printed 1989). Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate giving Title: Groombridge / Artist: Tom Caldwell / Year printed: 1989 / Edition Size: 1100 / Artist Proofs: 110, hand-numbered 761/1100 - photographed as IMG_8853, which was filed with listing A084. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Tom Caldwell (pencil, lower left margin); "Groombridge" (pencil, lower right margin, in quotation marks); 761/1100 (pencil, lower right margin). Condition: Mat lightly soiled with a few small dark specks at the lower edge; print itself appears clean; heavy glass glare in the detail shots.','Tom Caldwell','Groombridge','1989','offset fine-art reproduction after an egg tempera painting, pencil signed and numbered','761/1100 (edition size 1100 plus 110 artist''s proofs, printed 1989)','','','Tom Caldwell (pencil, lower left margin); "Groombridge" (pencil, lower right margin, in quotation marks); 761/1100 (pencil, lower right margin)','','katalog A083; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8851, IMG_8852; The certificate for this print (761/1100, ''Groombridge'', Tom Caldwell) was photographed as IMG_8853, which the frame list assigns to the NEXT listing A084 - the two listings were probably split one frame too late. Surname ''Caldwell'' is clear in the signature; the first name reads ''Tom'' and is confirmed by the certificate.','Certificate giving Title: Groombridge / Artist: Tom Caldwell / Year printed: 1989 / Edition Size: 1100 / Artist Proofs: 110, hand-numbered 761/1100 - photographed as IMG_8853, which was filed with listing A084.','IMG_8846',29.5,30.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "White", "Red", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(133,'ilan-133','tablo','yayinda','Seated Man Reading Newspaper, Genre Scene, Framed','An interior genre scene in warm sepia and ochre. An elderly man in a black overcoat, waistcoat and soft felt hat sits at an angle on a plain wooden chair, wire spectacles on his nose, holding an open newspaper across his knee; a heavy work boot juts into the foreground. Behind him a plaster wall carries four pinned notices - a blue printed sheet, a handbill headed ''Colored People''s Union'' and a yellow reward poster - and a table with papers and a blue book runs off to the left. The colouring is muted, almost monochrome brown, with the blue notice and a red flash at the sitter''s pocket as the only accents. Medium: colour reproduction print (offset/photomechanical) on paper or board, glazed. Accompanied by a certificate: IMG_8853 is a certificate, but its text belongs to the Tom Caldwell print catalogued as A083, not to this picture. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Within the picture, on the wall notices: ''RULES'' (blue sheet, remaining lines illegible); ''Colored People''s Union'' (handbill above the sitter''s shoulder); ''50 C… / REWAR[D] / … / BROTHER … / President … / LIME-KIL[N] …'' (yellow poster at the right, partly hidden by the frame). Condition: Surface shows overall warm discolouration and a faint vertical line at the right of the image; a few small dark flecks; no tears visible. Glass reflections obscure much of the surface.','','','late 19th century subject; the sheet itself probably a 20th-century reproduction','colour reproduction print (offset/photomechanical) on paper or board, glazed','','','','Within the picture, on the wall notices: ''RULES'' (blue sheet, remaining lines illegible); ''Colored People''s Union'' (handbill above the sitter''s shoulder); ''50 C… / REWAR[D] / … / BROTHER … / President … / LIME-KIL[N] …'' (yellow poster at the right, partly hidden by the frame)','','katalog A084; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8856, IMG_8857; Medium is the weak point: the surface is flat with no visible canvas weave, impasto or plate mark, and the picture is glazed, which suggests a reproduction on paper/board - but an original oil on board cannot be ruled out from photographs. No signature was found in any frame. The wall poster refers to the ''Lime-Kiln Club'', the 1880s humorous fraternity, which may help identify the original composition. Also note IMG_8853 (the certificate photographed with this listing) belongs to A083.','IMG_8853 is a certificate, but its text belongs to the Tom Caldwell print catalogued as A083, not to this picture.','IMG_8854',17.0,21.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "panel", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Gold", "Black", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(134,'ilan-134','tablo','yayinda','Montmartre Winter Street Scene after Utrillo, Maurice Utrillo, V., Signed, Framed','Maurice Utrillo, V.. A winter view up a Montmartre lane: a big bare tree and a tangle of branches fill the upper half, and through them the pale domes of Sacré-Coeur appear on the skyline. A white apartment block stands to the left, a gabled cottage with a green fence to the right, and a few dark figures walk the snow-covered street between them. The palette is almost monochrome - white, chalky grey, warm putty and black branch-lines - with tiny touches of green and red. Presented on a cream mat with a grey inner border in a dark wood frame with a gilt inner edge. Medium: colour reproduction print on canvas-textured paper, with facsimile signature. Signed lower right of the image, printed with the picture, reading "Maurice Utrillo, V.". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Maurice Utrillo, V. (lower right of the image); An illegible handwritten title inscription at the lower left of the image. Condition: Mat toned and slightly foxed at the lower edge; the image itself appears clean.','Maurice Utrillo, V.','','mid to late 20th century reproduction','colour reproduction print on canvas-textured paper, with facsimile signature','','','','Maurice Utrillo, V. (lower right of the image); An illegible handwritten title inscription at the lower left of the image','','katalog A085; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8860, IMG_8861; The signature is part of the printed image (a facsimile), so this is a reproduction after Utrillo rather than a hand-signed work; the canvas-like weave visible in the detail is a printed texture, not stretched canvas. The handwritten title at lower left could not be read.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8858',19.25,23.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "canvas", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["White", "Gray", "Black", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(135,'ilan-135','tablo','yayinda','Draped Figure in Blue, Modernist Composition, Signed, Framed','A near-abstract figure stands centrally against a dense midnight-blue field that has been worked with scrubbed and stippled strokes. Its head is a pale oval, and from the shoulders fall broad angular planes of colour - saffron and old gold, wine red, black and white - fanning out like sleeves, wings or a dancer''s skirts, each panel scored with fine parallel hatching. The surface is heavily textured throughout, half painted and half scraped. Presented under a wide tan-gold mat in a dark wood frame with a gilt inner edge. Medium: gouache or acrylic on paper or board, heavily textured. Signed lower right of the image, in reddish-brown. Condition: No visible damage; mat clean; strong reflections on the glass.','','','third quarter of the 20th century','gouache or acrylic on paper or board, heavily textured','','','','','','katalog A086; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8865, IMG_8866; The signature is a two-word cursive scrawl that I cannot read - the first word appears to begin with a large X or K. Medium is uncertain: the surface texture looks like real paint, but a heavily textured serigraph on board would look similar through glass.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8862',19.5,26.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "panel", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Gold", "Red", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(136,'ilan-136','tablo','yayinda','Woman in Pink on a Park Bench, barbara A wood, Numbered Edition, Framed','barbara A wood. A soft, atmospheric figure study: a young woman in a long dusty-rose dress lies back across a grey slatted park bench, one arm flung out along the backrest and one leg extended, her face turned down and half hidden by a bob of auburn hair. Bare winter branches and washy green-grey grass fill the background, and half a dozen small dark birds are scattered over the ground around her. The handling is loose and drawing-like, with pencil-grey contours showing through thin pink and olive washes. Wide cream mat with a rose fillet in a white lacquered frame. Medium: colour lithograph / offset print on paper, pencil signed and numbered. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "barbara A wood". Edition: 366/975. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: barbara A wood (pencil, lower right margin); 366/975 (pencil, lower left margin). Condition: Mat and sheet lightly toned; the white frame has small scuffs at the lower edge; no visible tears or foxing.','barbara A wood','','1970s-1980s','colour lithograph / offset print on paper, pencil signed and numbered','366/975','','','barbara A wood (pencil, lower right margin); 366/975 (pencil, lower left margin)','','katalog A087; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8871, IMG_8872; The pencil signature is a lower-case cursive that I read as ''barbara A wood''; the middle initial is a guess at a flourish. No title or publisher was found on the sheet.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8867',25.5,22.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Pink", "Gray", "Green", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(137,'ilan-137','tablo','yayinda','Scribbled Ink Drawing of a Blossom, Signed, Framed, 1968','A single dense skein of pen line, drawn without lifting, coils into a form that reads as a great open flower or wind-blown tree: heavy dark knots at the centre spread into looser, airier tangles at the edges, with a few long loops escaping to the lower right. Pure black ink on a warm cream sheet, with no colour at all - the drama is entirely in the density of the line. Mounted on a slate-blue mat with a black core line inside a gilt frame under glass. Medium: pen and ink on paper. Signed lower centre of the sheet, in ink, reading "fargo 68". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: fargo 68 (ink, lower centre of the sheet). Condition: Sheet lightly toned; a faint horizontal line runs across the lower left; mat and glass clean apart from reflections.','','','dated 68 (1968)','pen and ink on paper','','','','fargo 68 (ink, lower centre of the sheet)','','katalog A088; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8876, IMG_8877; The signature reads ''fargo 68'' but the first letter is an elongated f/P/L, so ''Pargo'' or ''Largo'' are possible; I have not treated it as a confirmed artist name.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8873',21.0,18.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["ink", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Beige", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(138,'ilan-138','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Landscape in Rose and Grey, Salkind, Signed, Framed','Salkind. A large square-ish abstract laid in with a palette knife and dry brush: broad horizontal bands of putty, warm grey and blush pink cross the canvas, interrupted at the centre by a cluster of blocky shapes in oxblood, aubergine and dull red that read like buildings or boats. Thin drawn lines in cerulean and scarlet cut across the field, and a short row of cobalt dashes sits at the lower left. The paint is thin and rubbed, letting the canvas weave show through, with denser impasto only in the central passage. Presented in a plain thin silver metal frame, unglazed. Medium: oil or acrylic on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in white paint, reading "Salkind". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Salkind (painted signature, lower right of the canvas). Condition: A few small blue paint specks on the upper left field (probably as painted); light surface dust; no craquelure or losses visible.','Salkind','','1960s-1980s','oil or acrylic on canvas','','','','Salkind (painted signature, lower right of the canvas)','','katalog A089; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8881, IMG_8882; The painted signature is cursive and reads ''Salkind'' to me, but ''Silkind'' or ''Selkind'' are possible. Oil versus acrylic cannot be settled from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8878',20.25,24.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "seascape", "landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Gray", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(139,'ilan-139','tablo','yayinda','Autumn River Landscape with Birch Trees, ERNEST, Signed, Framed','ERNEST. A tranquil autumn landscape: a still river cuts diagonally through the composition, mirroring a wide pastel sky streaked with pink, apricot and pale blue. Two slender white birches rise at the centre right, their sparse foliage dabbed in olive and gold, while a bank of rust and copper scrub runs along the left shore toward distant blue hills. The paint is applied thickly with a loaded brush and palette knife, with strong impasto in the reeds and clouds. Framed in an ornate dark bronze and gilt moulding with a linen liner. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in ochre paint, reading "ERNEST". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: ERNEST (painted signature, lower right of the canvas). Condition: Canvas weave shows through thin passages; small rubs and losses to the gilding on the frame corners; no visible tears or craquelure.','ERNEST','','third quarter of the 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','ERNEST (painted signature, lower right of the canvas)','','katalog A090; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8887, IMG_8888; Only the single name ''ERNEST'' is signed - it may be a first name or a trade signature used on decorative gallery paintings; no date or inscription elsewhere.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8883',30.5,27.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Blue", "Green", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(140,'ilan-140','tablo','yayinda','Yellow Poppies in a Green Vase, Egas, Signed, Framed','Egas. A bright still life set against a chartreuse and sage ground: a bulbous pale green vase holds a loose bunch of yellow poppies with dark seed-heart centres, their crumpled petals painted in buttery strokes over feathery blue-green foliage. Two or three blooms and a scatter of petals lie on the pale table in front. The palette is deliberately narrow - cadmium and lemon yellow against every shade of green - and the paint is applied wet-into-wet with visible brush marks. Set in a heavy ornate gold rococo frame with pierced corner scrolls. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark paint, reading "Egas". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Egas (painted signature, lower right of the canvas). Condition: Frame has rubbing and small chips to the gesso ornament, especially at the corners; canvas appears sound with no visible craquelure.','Egas','','third quarter of the 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','Egas (painted signature, lower right of the canvas)','','katalog A091; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8893, IMG_8894; The painted signature is a stylised monogram-like scrawl read as ''Egas''; ''Fgas'' or a longer name partly hidden in the paint are possible.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8889',28.0,32.6,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Green", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(141,'ilan-141','tablo','yayinda','Monet''s Years at Giverny Metropolitan Museum Poster, Claude Monet, Signed, Framed, 1978','Claude Monet. A museum exhibition poster reproducing Monet''s four poplars: four slender trunks rise the full height of the sheet from a lavender-blue band of foliage and its reflection, against a sky broken into flecks of pale blue, rose and cream. The brushwork of the original is fully visible in the reproduction, all short vertical dabs of violet, blue and pink. Below the image the poster carries the exhibition title and dates in fine capitals on a cream ground. Framed in a slim gold anodised aluminium section frame under glass. Medium: offset lithographic exhibition poster on paper. Signed lower left of the reproduced image, printed, reading "Claude Monet 91 (partly legible, part of the reproduced painting)". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: MONET''S YEARS AT GIVERNY; THE METROPOLITAN MUSEUM OF ART · APRIL 22 - JULY 9 1978; Fine print line at the foot of the sheet, only partly legible: ''The exhibition, organized by The Metropolitan Museum of Art in cooperation with The St. Louis Art Museum, has been made possible in part by a grant from the Robert Wood Johnson … Charitable Trust''. Condition: Poster lightly toned; a faint diagonal crease runs through the upper right of the image; frame clean.','Claude Monet','MONET''S YEARS AT GIVERNY','1978','offset lithographic exhibition poster on paper','','','The Metropolitan Museum of Art','MONET''S YEARS AT GIVERNY; THE METROPOLITAN MUSEUM OF ART · APRIL 22 - JULY 9 1978; Fine print line at the foot of the sheet, only partly legible: ''The exhibition, organized by The Metropolitan Museum of Art in cooperation with The St. Louis Art Museum, has been made possible in part by a grant from the Robert Wood Johnson … Charitable Trust''','','katalog A092; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8897, IMG_8898; This listing is almost certainly the same framed poster as A093 - A092 has only the full view and no measurement, A093 has only a detail and the two tape shots, and both show the same Monet poplars image in a slim gold metal frame. They should probably be merged. Merged with former listing A093 (same work).','no certificate photographed','IMG_8895',24.25,30.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": [], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Pink", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(142,'ilan-142','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Composition in Sand and Crimson, Signed, Unframed','A wide unframed canvas worked in creamy sand, buff and pale apricot, across the middle of which runs a horizontal band of stacked shapes in crimson, olive-brown, mauve and grey. Small accents of turquoise and a hot pink stripe punctuate the cluster, and a long pale diagonal sweeps out to the lower right, giving the whole a landscape-like horizon without describing anything. The paint is brushed thinly and blended wet-into-wet, with the canvas weave showing through the lighter passages, and the upper half is left almost empty as breathing space. The painted image continues over the stretcher edges, so it hangs as-is without a frame. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in white paint, reading "Audrey Salkind". Condition: No tears, dents or flaking visible; light reflected glare across the surface in every shot. Edges of the stretched canvas look clean.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A094; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8903, IMG_8904; The white cursive signature is only partly legible; it reads as a first name like ''Audrey'' and a surname beginning ''Salk'', so no artist name is asserted. Oil versus acrylic cannot be settled from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8899',30.25,24.5,'canvas',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Green", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(143,'ilan-143','tablo','yayinda','Colonial Fifer Stipple Print, Numbered 25/100, MAltz, Numbered Edition, Framed, 1985','MAltz. A small black-and-white figure study built entirely from stipple dots, showing a boy or young soldier in a tricorn hat, full-sleeved shirt, breeches, stockings and buckled shoes, marching to the right while playing a fife. A haversack swings at his hip and a light dotted shadow trails behind his feet, the only ground indicated. The image sits on white paper with a ruled black border, hand numbered ''25/100'' at lower left and signed in pencil at lower right. It is presented in a wide cream mat with a fine black line and a moulded dark cherry-red timber frame under glass. Medium: limited-edition print after a pen-and-ink stipple drawing (offset or photo-lithograph). Signed in pencil below the image at lower right, plus a copyright line inside the image, reading "MAltz". Edition: 25/100 (hand numbered in pencil). Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 25/100; ©MAltz ''85. Condition: Print and mat look clean; heavy reflections on the glass in every shot, and a small tag or sticker is caught under the glass at the upper left in IMG_8905/8909.','MAltz','','1985 (dated in the image)','limited-edition print after a pen-and-ink stipple drawing (offset or photo-lithograph)','25/100 (hand numbered in pencil)','','','25/100; ©MAltz ''85','','katalog A095; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8908, IMG_8909; The pencil signature and the in-image copyright both read as ''MAltz'' / ''Maltz'' but the letterforms are stylised, so the spelling is not certain. The printing process (offset vs lithograph) cannot be confirmed at this resolution.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8905',11.0,13.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "ink", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "White", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(144,'ilan-144','tablo','yayinda','Chinese Butterflies and Pink Blossoms on Silk, Signed, Framed','A delicate export-style painting on a warm tan silk ground: a slender stem of green rounded leaves enters from the upper left and carries two pink blossoms, while three butterflies hover below and to the right. Each butterfly is picked out with fine hair-thin antennae and jewel-like wings in cobalt, turquoise, scarlet, gold and black. The handling is meticulous and miniature in scale, the silk left bare across most of the surface so the insects float in empty space. It is double-matted in cream with a fine gold-brown inner line and set in a narrow gilt frame under glass. Medium: gouache and ink on silk. Signed small red seal at the lower left of the silk. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: $40 (handwritten price sticker on the mat, upper right). Condition: Silk is toned but even; some faint pencil marks and light soiling on the mat at lower left; strong glare on the glass. Small adhesive price sticker still attached to the mat.','','','20th century','gouache and ink on silk','','','','$40 (handwritten price sticker on the mat, upper right)','','katalog A096; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8911, IMG_8912; The red seal at lower left is too small and faint to read, so no artist can be named. Whether the support is silk or a fine silk-textured paper cannot be settled from photographs. The price sticker digits could read $20 rather than $40.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8910',11.0,9.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal"], "medium": ["watercolour", "ink", "textile"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Black", "Blue", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(145,'ilan-145','tablo','yayinda','Chinese Butterflies with Orange Lily on Silk, Framed','Companion piece in the same manner as A096: on a warm tan silk ground, a stem of long green blade-like leaves rises at the left carrying two orange-red lily flowers with yellow throats, and four butterflies and moths are scattered across the open ground to the right. Their wings are painted in russet, gold, turquoise, cobalt and scarlet with fine dark veining and threadlike antennae. The composition is spare and asymmetric, with most of the silk left empty. Presented in the same cream mat with fine ruled line and narrow speckled gilt frame under glass. Medium: gouache and ink on silk. Condition: Silk evenly toned; a small light spot on the mat at the right and general glare on the glass. No tears or losses visible.','','','20th century','gouache and ink on silk','','','','','','katalog A097; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8915, IMG_8916; No seal or signature is visible in any frame, so the piece is unattributed. Silk versus silk-textured paper cannot be confirmed. Almost certainly a pair with A096, but nothing photographed states that.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8914',11.0,8.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life", "animal"], "medium": ["watercolour", "ink", "textile"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Orange", "Blue", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(146,'ilan-146','tablo','yayinda','Reflections Cape Cod Harbour Watercolour by John Hare, Signed, Framed','JOHN HARE. A moody harbour watercolour: a dark-hulled fishing boat with two raised tan sails lies alongside a pier, a second smaller sail behind it, and a grey shingled dock shed fills the right of the composition. A lone figure in dark clothing stands on the wet planking carrying a red bucket, the one warm note in an otherwise cool scheme of slate grey, olive, ochre and blue-black. Broad wet washes are laid in for the stormy sky and the water, with the reflections of the pilings dragged downward in loose vertical strokes and small gulls flicked into the sky. The sheet is mounted on a cream mount with a ruled ink border, titled in pencil below the image, and set in a narrow moulded dark wood frame under glass. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right within the image, in dark ink or paint, reading "JOHN HARE". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: REFLECTIONS - CAPE COD (pencil, on the mount below the image); $1200 (handwritten price sticker on the mount at lower right). Condition: Paper and washes look clean and unfaded; the mount is lightly toned. Heavy reflections on the glass. A price sticker is stuck to the mount.','JOHN HARE','REFLECTIONS - CAPE COD','mid to late 20th century','watercolour on paper','','','','REFLECTIONS - CAPE COD (pencil, on the mount below the image); $1200 (handwritten price sticker on the mount at lower right)','','katalog A098; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8921, IMG_8922; The title and signature are clearly legible; nothing photographed dates the work, so the period is inferred from style and framing alone.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8917',14.0,16.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Green", "Gold", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(147,'ilan-147','tablo','yayinda','Chinese Ink Painting of Willows and Zigzag Bridge, Signed, Framed','A quiet monochrome ink landscape: two large willows lean in from the left and right, their trailing branches drawn in fine grey strokes, and a low zigzag plank bridge with a railing crosses the water behind them. In the foreground a small dark boat sits on the shore beside a rock, with reeds and scrub dotted along the bank. The painting is almost entirely grey-black ink on cream paper, wet-brushed for the foliage masses and drawn with dry fine lines for the hanging branches. A brushed two-character signature and a small red seal sit at the upper right; the sheet is set behind a slate-grey mat and a natural linen-toned surround in a plain gilt frame under glass, with a small engraved brass plaque fixed to the mount at the bottom. Medium: ink and light wash on paper. Signed upper right of the sheet, brushed in ink above a red seal. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: HAND-PAINTED ... (first line of the brass plaque, only partly legible); ... FRAMED IN NEWPORT NEWS. (second line of the brass plaque). Condition: Paper is lightly toned overall with no visible foxing or tears; strong glare and shadow across the glass in most shots.','','','mid to late 20th century','ink and light wash on paper','','','','HAND-PAINTED ... (first line of the brass plaque, only partly legible); ... FRAMED IN NEWPORT NEWS. (second line of the brass plaque)','','katalog A099; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8926, IMG_8927; The brass plaque is engraved in small capitals and only partly readable at this resolution - the first line begins ''HAND-PAINTED'' and the second ends ''FRAMED IN NEWPORT NEWS.'' The two-character brushed signature and the four-character seal cannot be transcribed; the first character of the signature appears to be a small three-stroke form. Paper versus silk is not certain.','no certificate; only an engraved brass plaque on the mount','IMG_8923',15.25,18.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["ink", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Gray", "Beige", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(148,'ilan-148','tablo','yayinda','Coastal Lighthouse Watercolour by Rebecca Albaugh, REBECCA P. ALBAUGH, Signed, Framed','REBECCA P. ALBAUGH. A breezy coastal watercolour dominated by an expanse of streaked blue-grey sea and a soft cloud-banded sky that fills the upper half of the sheet. A cluster of low white cottages with terracotta roofs sits on a headland at the right, a slim white lighthouse tower rising among them beside a dark cypress. The foreground bank is brushed in dry ochre and olive grasses over sandy paper, and a thin pale strip of far shoreline runs across the horizon at the left. The washes are transparent and quickly laid, with white paper left for the buildings and the wave crests. It is double-matted in cream over a dark blue-grey inner mat in a slim polished silver-gilt metal frame under glass. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right within the image, in dark pencil or ink, reading "Rebecca Albaugh 1971". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: REBECCA P. ALBAUGH / ARTIST / 1226 ST PAUL (handwritten over the printed street line) / BALTIMORE, MD 21202 / WATERCOLORS PASTELS (business card taped to the backing board); About The Artist. Rebecca Albaugh is an artist of a new day. Primarily a watercolorist, her subject matter reflects an intense interest in skyscapes. Ms. Albaugh employs space and transparency with the interplay of sky and clouds. Although some of the cloud depictions are almost accurately rendered, there is a feeling of romantic sensitivity to movement, composition and light. Born in Philadelphia in 1949, Rebecca was greatly influenced by her father, James Pearl, a watercolorist known throughout the eastern United States. She attended the Maryland Institute College of Art, and the Schuler School of Fine Art where she studied with Frederick Briggs. Her work has been featured in the Baltimore Sun and The News American. She has shown her work in one person exhibitions as well as the City Hall Courtyard Gallery, The Turner Auditorium, The Johns Hopkins University, the Grannery Gallery in Frederick, Md. and The Five Stalls Gallery, Monkton. Thomas Cole said "It is of the greatest importance for the painter always to have his mind on nature as the star by which he is to steer to excellence in his art." Sky and clouds, elements which are almost always in motion, have a certain fascination for Rebecca Albaugh who finds there an infinite source of challenge and inspiration for her painting. (printed clipping taped to the backing board). Condition: Washes fresh and unfaded, mats clean; the backing board is toned brown with age and the paper clipping and card are yellowed. Hanging wire and metal frame intact.','REBECCA P. ALBAUGH','','1970s (signature dated)','watercolour on paper','','','','REBECCA P. ALBAUGH / ARTIST / 1226 ST PAUL (handwritten over the printed street line) / BALTIMORE, MD 21202 / WATERCOLORS PASTELS (business card taped to the backing board); About The Artist. Rebecca Albaugh is an artist of a new day. Primarily a watercolorist, her subject matter reflects an intense interest in skyscapes. Ms. Albaugh employs space and transparency with the interplay of sky and clouds. Although some of the cloud depictions are almost accurately rendered, there is a feeling of romantic sensitivity to movement, composition and light. Born in Philadelphia in 1949, Rebecca was greatly influenced by her father, James Pearl, a watercolorist known throughout the eastern United States. She attended the Maryland Institute College of Art, and the Schuler School of Fine Art where she studied with Frederick Briggs. Her work has been featured in the Baltimore Sun and The News American. She has shown her work in one person exhibitions as well as the City Hall Courtyard Gallery, The Turner Auditorium, The Johns Hopkins University, the Grannery Gallery in Frederick, Md. and The Five Stalls Gallery, Monkton. Thomas Cole said "It is of the greatest importance for the painter always to have his mind on nature as the star by which he is to steer to excellence in his art." Sky and clouds, elements which are almost always in motion, have a certain fascination for Rebecca Albaugh who finds there an infinite source of challenge and inspiration for her painting. (printed clipping taped to the backing board)','','katalog A100; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8932, IMG_8933; The last two digits of the date beside the signature are blurred - it reads 1971 but could be 1977. The artist''s name is taken from her business card and biography on the backing board, which agree with the signature.','no certificate, but a printed ''About The Artist'' biography and the artist''s own business card are taped to the backing board','IMG_8928',24.0,18.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "architecture"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Gray", "Beige", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(149,'ilan-149','tablo','yayinda','Three Women Carrying Baskets Through Birch Woods, Signed, Framed, 1992','Three slender women in dark indigo, teal and maroon saris walk away from the viewer along a pale ochre path, each balancing a shallow dark basket on her head. Behind them a stand of leafless white-trunked trees rises against a dusky violet-brown hillside, the trunks drawn as fine pale lines over mottled, sponged colour. Large grey and lavender boulders block the left foreground, painted with dry stippled highlights that give the whole picture a granular, tapestry-like surface. The palette is muted and dusky - stone grey, olive, plum and sand - with the figures reading as dark silhouettes against the lit path. It is floated on a lavender-grey mat in a plain dark timber frame under glass. Medium: gouache or tempera on paper. Signed lower left within the image, in dark ink. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: ''92 (date following the signature). Condition: Image and mat look clean and unfaded; a small scuff or paper flaw on the mat above the image at upper left; heavy reflections on the glass.','','','1992 (dated in the signature)','gouache or tempera on paper','','','','''92 (date following the signature)','','katalog A101; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8938, IMG_8939; The signature is written in Devanagari script and cannot be transcribed reliably from the photograph, so no artist name is given; only the year ''92 is legible. Gouache versus tempera or acrylic on paper cannot be settled visually.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8935',14.0,16.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["asian", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Gold", "Purple", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(150,'ilan-150','tablo','yayinda','Asian Ink Painting of Bird on Rock, Signed, Framed','A softly worked ink painting on a toned silk-like ground: a small brown-breasted bird with a long tail perches on a jutting grey rock at the centre, its head turned to the left. Bamboo leaves and slender stems sweep in from the right and below, and a single pale yellow-white blossom opens above the bird. The ink is applied in dilute washes with darker accents on the leaves and the bird''s markings, and the whole scene is faded and atmospheric rather than crisp. Two columns of cursive calligraphy and two vermilion seals are placed at the upper left. It is set behind a black inner line mat and a natural raw-silk surround in a broad gold-leaf frame under glass. Medium: ink and light colour on silk or paper. Signed upper left of the picture, two columns of cursive characters with two red seals beside them. Condition: The ground is browned and mottled with age and the image is faded; no tears or losses visible through the glass. Strong glare in every frame.','','','20th century or earlier','ink and light colour on silk or paper','','','','','','katalog A102; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8943, IMG_8944; The inscription is in cursive grass-script and cannot be transcribed, and the seals are illegible, so neither artist nor date is established. Whether the support is silk or paper, and whether the work is Chinese or Korean, cannot be determined from the photographs. Age is uncertain - the toning could be genuine or deliberate.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8940',17.75,16.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal"], "medium": ["ink", "textile", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Beige", "Green", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(151,'ilan-151','tablo','yayinda','Modernist Lithograph of a Green-Faced Prophet and Angel, Framed','A dramatic colour lithograph in the School-of-Paris biblical manner: the head and shoulders of an old bearded man fill the left of the sheet, his face and hands washed in acid green with a black flowing beard drawn in loose crayon curls. A small white angel with outstretched wings and a round pale face floats in the upper right against a smoky black-brown ground, and a second green form appears at the lower right. The colour is laid in flat, grainy crayon patches over a mottled black and ochre field, with the lithographic tooth of the crayon visible throughout and no plate mark or margins showing. It is presented in a gold fillet-lined mount, a wide cream linen mat and a black-and-gilt frame under glass. Medium: colour lithograph. Condition: Colours strong, no foxing or tears visible; the sheet is trimmed close and hidden under the fillet so the margins cannot be inspected. Reflections on the glass.','','','mid 20th century','colour lithograph','','','','','','katalog A103; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8947, IMG_8948; No signature, edition number, publisher line or label is visible anywhere, so the work is unattributed. The grainy crayon texture indicates a lithograph rather than a painting, but with the margins hidden the printing method and whether this is an original stone lithograph or a later reproduction cannot be confirmed. Almost certainly a pair with A104.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8945',18.0,21.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Black", "Gold", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(152,'ilan-152','tablo','yayinda','Modernist Lithograph of Mother and Child with Angel, Framed','A colour lithograph drawn in sweeping black and vermilion crayon lines over a warm grey-taupe ground. A woman with a red-haloed head bends over a sleeping child held across her lap, the pair described almost entirely by looping contour lines with red hatching filling the folds of her robe, her bare feet and hands left as pale outlined shapes. In the upper left a small winged angel in red and black dives towards them, and loose scribbled strokes suggest a landscape behind. The mark-making is fast and calligraphic and the paper tone is left to do most of the work. Framed to match A103: gold fillet, cream linen mat, black-and-gilt moulding under glass. Medium: colour lithograph. Condition: Clean and bright with no foxing or cockling visible; margins hidden under the fillet. Some glare on the glass.','','','mid 20th century','colour lithograph','','','','','','katalog A104; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8951, IMG_8952; Unsigned, unnumbered and without any label or publisher line, so the work is unattributed. The margins are covered, so the printing method cannot be fully verified. Framed as a pair with A103 and clearly from the same series.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8949',18.0,21.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(153,'ilan-153','tablo','yayinda','Medieval Knight Brass Rubbing in Gold on Black, Framed','A tall narrow rubbing taken from a medieval monumental brass: a knight stands facing forward in a mail coif and hauberk, the rings rendered as thousands of tiny stippled marks, his surcoat falling in long vertical folds. He holds a heater shield charged with a bend and fleur-de-lys against his left side, a sword hilt at his waist, and a lion or hound crouches beneath his feet, with large heraldic rosettes flanking his shoulders. The whole figure is worked in metallic gold, copper and silver wax over a dense black ground, so it glows against the dark paper. It is glazed and set in a narrow gilt frame that emphasises the tall vertical format. Medium: wax rubbing (brass rubbing) on black paper. Condition: No tears or creases visible; the glass carries heavy reflections and a ceiling light burns out part of the head in one shot. Frame corners look sound.','','','20th century, after a medieval original','wax rubbing (brass rubbing) on black paper','','','','','','katalog A105; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8957, IMG_8958; No inscription, title or maker''s mark is visible, so neither the church of origin nor the rubbing''s maker can be named. That this is a wax rubbing rather than a printed reproduction is a judgement from the granular metallic surface seen through glass.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8953',15.75,38.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Gold", "Orange", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(154,'ilan-154','tablo','yayinda','Oil Painting of a Gaunt Mother and Child, Jesus Vill, Signed, Framed','Jesus Vill. A sombre figure painting in the social-realist manner: a hollow-cheeked woman in a pale blue headscarf sits close to the picture plane, a thin child pressed cheek to cheek against her, both painted with elongated limbs, heavy eyelids and blunt sculptural hands. She wears a mustard-yellow blouse over a rose-red skirt, the child a sea-green tunic, and their enormous pale hands and the child''s bare feet are laid across the foreground in a knot at the centre. A terracotta jug and a white bowl stand on a ledge behind them against a bare grey-green wall. The paint is dry and scumbled with visible brush drag, the palette drab olive, grey and ochre lit by the two strong notes of yellow and red. It is set in a broad mahogany-toned frame with a carved grapevine inner band. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower left within the image, in dark paint, reading "Jesus Vill". Condition: Surface looks stable with no flaking or tears seen; a soft grey bloom or dust haze sits over the darks and there is glare from the room lights. Frame carving intact.','Jesus Vill','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A106; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8963, IMG_8964; The signature clearly begins ''Jesus Vill'' but the rest of the surname runs into an illegible flourish, so the full name cannot be given. Oil versus acrylic and canvas versus board are judgements from the photographs; the back was not photographed.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8959',28.0,37.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Gold", "Red", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(155,'ilan-155','tablo','yayinda','Large Cubist Panel of Birds and Masked Faces, Signed, Framed','A big, jubilant composition in which dozens of stylised birds, fish and mask-like human profiles interlock like puzzle pieces across the whole panel. Every shape is bounded by a raised black outline and filled with high-gloss enamel-bright colour - scarlet, cadmium yellow, cobalt, sea green, pink and cream - many of them patterned with stripes, scallops, wavy lines or rows of white dots. Two large frontal faces with wide staring eyes and bared teeth anchor the centre, surrounded by fan-shaped tails and beaked heads that read equally as feathers or fins. The surface is glassy and lacquer-like, with the pooled colour and ridged outlines giving a cloisonne or stained-glass effect. It is set in a plain broad off-white frame with a thin gold inner fillet, unglazed. Medium: lacquer or enamel-like paint on board with raised outlines. Signed lower right of the image, painted in dark red-brown block letters, reading "S. MiTk". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: S. MiTk (with three dots after the final letter). Condition: Glossy surface bright and unchipped in the shots available; strong specular highlights everywhere because of the high-gloss finish. Frame face is clean cream with light handling marks.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','lacquer or enamel-like paint on board with raised outlines','','','','S. MiTk (with three dots after the final letter)','','katalog A107; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8972, IMG_8973; The signature reads as ''S. MiTk'' followed by three dots but the last letters are ambiguous - it could be MITR, MITH or MITK - so no artist is named. The technique is judged from the raised outlines and glassy pooled colour; it could be lacquer, enamel, or acrylic under heavy gloss varnish, and the support could be board or panel.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8966',30.0,42.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["panel"], "style": ["folk", "contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Yellow", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(156,'ilan-156','tablo','yayinda','Large Abstract Landscape in Magenta and Chartreuse, Signed, Framed','A large, almost square abstract that reads loosely as a landscape: a broad indigo-navy band runs across the upper middle like deep water, with runnels of hot pink dripping down through it, while a tall magenta shape rises at the right like a figure or a tree trunk. Below, chartreuse and cadmium yellow fields are scratched and scraped into a bank of grass, and a wedge of bare white breaks through at the bottom centre. The paint is heavily impasted and worked with a knife, with spattered black speckles, sgraffito lines scored back through the crust and dry pigment dragged over the ridges. Colour is loud and saturated - magenta, crimson, chartreuse, gold and violet against the dark blue. It is set in a deep, wide, high-gloss dark mahogany frame with a stepped scoop profile. Medium: acrylic or oil with heavy impasto on canvas. Signed lower centre-left within the image, scratched in red paint. Condition: Thick impasto intact with no visible cracking or loss; some drips and spatter are part of the making. The glossy frame shows minor handling marks and reflections.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic or oil with heavy impasto on canvas','','','','','','katalog A108; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8978, IMG_8979; The red cursive signature is scratched over textured paint and is illegible, so the artist cannot be named. Oil versus acrylic cannot be determined from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8974',40.0,40.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Pink", "Blue", "Yellow", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(157,'ilan-157','tablo','yayinda','Mediterranean Hillside Village at Sunset, Signed, Framed','A stylised Mediterranean village climbs a hill above a deep cobalt sea, with terracotta roofs, a slender campanile and two palms silhouetted against a saffron sky. The paint is built up in dense, granular impasto: the whole surface is stippled with raised flecks that catch the light, and the sunset sky is dotted with hundreds of tiny highlights. Forms are simplified into flat geometric planes - wedge-shaped walls, a pale road, and olive-green banks - so the picture reads as much as pattern as landscape. Palette is dominated by golden ochre, burnt orange, cream and a single band of cobalt for the water. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower centre-left, on the pale road. Condition: No visible damage, tears or losses; heavy impasto is intact. Some raking-light glare on the textured surface in the detail shots.','','','late 20th / early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A109; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8984, IMG_8985; The dark cursive signature in IMG_8981 is not legible at 900px, so no artist name is recorded. Both tape readings are approximate because the zero end of the tape is off-frame in both photographs.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8980',38.5,39.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gold", "Orange", "Beige", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(158,'ilan-158','tablo','yayinda','Hibel Mother and Two Children, Hand-Painted Lithograph, Signed, Framed','Hibel. Three figures - a young woman, a curly-haired toddler on her shoulder and an older child at her hip - are drawn in fine sepia and charcoal line over a chalky pale-turquoise ground. Colour is applied thinly and dryly so the coarse canvas weave shows through everywhere, giving the whole image a frescoed, faded-tapestry look. Coral, rose and ochre accents pick out the drapery folds and the children''s hair, while faint architectural verticals float behind the group. The handling is deliberately unfinished, with pentimenti and open drawing left visible around the edges. Medium: lithograph with hand-applied oil colour on canvas-textured support. Signed lower right of the image, in reddish-brown, reading "Hibel". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: unique lithograph and oil. Condition: Surface is dry and matte with pronounced canvas texture; no tears or losses seen. The gilt frame shows scattered rubbing and small losses to the high points of the ornament.','Hibel','','third quarter of the 20th century','lithograph with hand-applied oil colour on canvas-textured support','','','','unique lithograph and oil','','katalog A110; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8991, IMG_8992; The pencil/crayon inscription in IMG_8993 reads ''unique lithograph and oil'' but the first word is partly abraded; it could also read ''original''. No edition number, publisher or gallery label was photographed, so it is unclear whether this is a numbered edition piece.','no certificate photographed; the medium is declared in the artist''s own hand on the face of the work','IMG_8986',37.5,47.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "print", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Pink", "Brown", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(159,'ilan-159','tablo','yayinda','Row of Autumn Trees on a Golden Horizon, Signed, Framed','A minimal, almost abstract landscape: a thin band of squat trees with rust-red canopies and pale trunks runs across the centre of the panel, dividing a deep crimson upper field from a glowing amber lower one. The colour is laid as a smooth vertical gradient from carmine through orange to pale gold, then broken all over by a dense scatter of raised gold and cream flecks that read as texture rather than as depicted objects. The effect is contemplative and poster-like, with no horizon detail beyond the trees themselves. Medium: oil on canvas with textured/gilded surface treatment. Signed lower right of the canvas. Condition: No visible damage; surface texture and gilding intact. Frame has an intentionally distressed speckled finish that should not be mistaken for wear.','','','late 20th / early 21st century','oil on canvas with textured/gilded surface treatment','','','','','','katalog A111; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8999, IMG_9001; The black cursive signature in IMG_8996 is fluent but illegible at this resolution; no name recorded. The gold flecking may be applied metallic leaf or heavy gilded impasto - it cannot be distinguished from photographs, hence medium confidence only.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8995',31.0,43.2,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Orange", "Gold", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(160,'ilan-160','tablo','yayinda','White Roses Still Life, Framed Floral Print, Signed, Framed','Full-blown white roses crowd the picture plane, painted with loaded, buttery strokes so each bloom reads as a mass of impasto-like white touches over soft grey shadow. Behind them the ground dissolves into scumbled olive, ochre and oxblood, with a suggestion of a table edge and a picture frame in the upper left. The handling is loose and painterly, the palette warm and low-key apart from the brilliant whites, and the image is signed in white script at the lower right. Presented under glass with a wide white mat and a thin black inner mat. Medium: offset/giclee reproduction print on paper. Signed lower right, within the image, in white script. Condition: No visible damage to the sheet. Heavy reflections and a ceiling-light hotspot on the glass in several frames obscure the surface; the mat is clean.','','','late 20th / early 21st century','offset/giclee reproduction print on paper','','','','','','katalog A112; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9006, IMG_9007; Called a print because the white signature sits within the image and the surface shows no true impasto relief under the glass, but the glare makes this a judgement rather than a certainty. The white cursive signature (two words, second appears to begin with a capital T) is not legible enough to record a name.','no certificate or gallery label photographed','IMG_9002',47.75,36.3,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["White", "Beige", "Green", "Brown"]}'::jsonb),
(161,'ilan-161','tablo','yayinda','Metaphysical Still Life with Classical Head, Chirico, Signed, Framed, 1988','Chirico. A dense metaphysical assemblage: a white plaster head with closed eyes and a curling beard sits at the right, propped among stacked canvases, a scrolled Ionic volute, a fluted column, a red-brick wall and a small painted pediment. Everything is described with firm dark contours and broad, flat brushwork in a muted range of terracotta, cream, umber and slate, punctuated by one saturated blue rectangle. Perspective is deliberately unstable, with objects tipping toward the viewer on a warm plank floor. Surface texture is visibly brushy with soft ridges where the paint is loaded. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower centre, on the plank floor, reading "Chirico 1988". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Chirico 1988. Condition: No tears or losses visible; the paint film is sound with normal brush relief. Some surface sheen and glare in the raking-light shots.','Chirico','','later 20th century (dated 1988 in the signature)','oil on canvas','','','','Chirico 1988','','katalog A113; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9012, IMG_9013; The signature is transcribed exactly as painted - ''Chirico 1988''. Giorgio de Chirico died in 1978, so a 1988 date means this cannot be an autograph work by him; it is a later homage, copy or a different hand using the same name. The final two digits are slightly ambiguous and could read 1980.','no certificate or gallery label photographed','IMG_9008',37.25,49.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Beige", "Brown", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(162,'ilan-162','tablo','yayinda','Wooded River Landscape with Cattle, Signed, Framed','A traditional pastoral scene: a stand of tall trees in russet and olive fills the left half, opening onto a silvery river that recedes to a soft distant horizon. A small group of cattle, one picked out in rust-red, is driven along the near bank beside a figure, painted with small flickering touches. The sky is broadly brushed in cream, dove grey and pale blue with lit cloud edges, and the whole is kept in a mellow, low-contrast key of browns, greens and greys. A red cursive signature sits at the lower right. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right, in red. Condition: No obvious tears or flaking. Some surface gloss and glare; a fine craquelure cannot be ruled out from these images. Frame finish is evenly worn.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A114; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9018, IMG_9019; The small red signature at the lower right (IMG_9015) resolves as roughly six or seven letters but is not legible with certainty; it has the shape of a name ending in -son but no name is recorded rather than guess.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_9014',42.25,30.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Gray", "Beige", "Brown"]}'::jsonb),
(163,'ilan-163','tablo','yayinda','The Road to Paradise, Signed Panoramic Print, Numbered Edition, Framed','An extremely wide panoramic composition in which a line of hunched figures in grey overcoats and caps pedal from left to right; their bodies are painted as soft, almost photographic grey masses while the bicycles are reduced to bold, hand-drawn red circles and lines that float over them. The ground shifts from a warm blush pink at the right to a deep navy band at the left, with drifting shadows beneath the riders. The contrast of muted figures against graphic red linework gives the image a witty, poster-like rhythm. Pencil signed, titled and numbered in the wide bottom margin. Medium: limited-edition lithograph or serigraph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil. Edition: 40/125. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: The Road to Paradise.; 40/125. Condition: Sheet and mat look clean and bright with no foxing visible. Strong reflections on the glass throughout.','','The Road to Paradise.','late 20th / early 21st century','limited-edition lithograph or serigraph on paper','40/125','','','The Road to Paradise.; 40/125','','katalog A115; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9024, IMG_9025; The pencil signature at the lower right is a rapid monogram-like scrawl beginning with what looks like an M; it is not legible, so no artist name is recorded. Print process (lithograph vs serigraph) cannot be confirmed through glass - no plate mark or dot screen is resolvable.','no certificate photographed; hand-signed, titled and numbered in the margin','IMG_9020',44.5,17.2,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gray", "Red", "Black", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(164,'ilan-164','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Fan and Disc with Gold Leaf, Framed','A large circle filled with fine vertical pen-hatching in slate blue sits at the centre, crossed from the left by a rectangular band of coral, rose and gold Japanese textile patterning and overlapped at the right by a huge fan-shaped segment printed in metallic gold over dark ink. Splatters and flicks of gold, coral and navy are scattered across the cream ground, and rows of ruled construction lines run through the design. The result is graphic and richly metallic, mixing kimono and obi motifs with hard-edged geometry. Presented under glass in a deep burgundy mat. Medium: serigraph with metallic gold and silver inks on paper. Condition: Sheet appears clean and unfaded; metallic inks are bright. Heavy reflections of the room on the glass in every frame. No signature or edition margin is exposed - the mat may be covering it.','','','1980s','serigraph with metallic gold and silver inks on paper','','','','','','katalog A116; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9030, IMG_9031; No signature, title or edition number is visible in any frame - if the work is pencil-signed the margin is hidden under the mat, so it cannot be attributed. Serigraph is inferred from the flat metallic ink layers and hard-edged registration; this was not verified against a plate mark or dot screen.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_9026',42.0,34.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "ink", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Gray", "Red", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(165,'ilan-165','tablo','yayinda','Stylised Reclining Figure in Terracotta, Framed','A tall, narrow composition built from a few sweeping calligraphic curves: a stylised female form arches from the top of the panel, her head and shoulder rendered as a swelling coral and cream mass, then tapers into a long dark tail that coils into a spiral at the base. The palette is restricted to terracotta, rust, coral, cream and a soft teal accent on a sand-coloured ground, with the drawing carried by confident charcoal contours. The support has a visible woven texture, giving the flat colours a canvas-like grain. Presented under glass with a cream mat and a thin black inner border. Medium: reproduction print on textured board or canvas-textured paper. Condition: No visible damage; mat and glass are clean apart from a ceiling-light reflection in the detail shots.','','','late 20th / early 21st century','reproduction print on textured board or canvas-textured paper','','','','','','katalog A117; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9035, IMG_9036; No signature, title or edition mark is visible in any of the five frames. Called a print because of the even, flat colour and absence of paint relief, but the visible woven texture leaves open the possibility of an original acrylic on canvas board.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_9032',21.3,37.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "canvas", "panel", "paper"], "style": ["art-nouveau", "contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Orange", "Beige", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(166,'ilan-166','tablo','yayinda','Northern Sky, Signed Limited Edition Print, MON SCHIO, Numbered Edition, Framed','MON SCHIO. A mottled gold and bronze ground, textured like weathered gilt plaster, is cut by a deep indigo wedge sprinkled with tiny stars in the upper left and by a great sweeping golden arc that curves across the lower half. A pale pink disc floats top right, a crimson circle and a dark green leaf sit at centre, and a small chequered tower with a red roof anchors the composition below. The palette is warm and metallic - antique gold, bronze, plum, indigo - with a single blue horizontal rule for contrast. Pencil signed, titled and numbered in the bottom margin. Medium: serigraph or lithograph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "MON SCHIO". Edition: 285/450. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 285/450; MON SCHIO; NORTHERN SKY. Condition: Sheet is clean with bright metallic passages and no foxing visible. Some reflection on the glass; the silver frame shows minor handling marks.','MON SCHIO','NORTHERN SKY','1980s-1990s','serigraph or lithograph on paper','285/450','','','285/450; MON SCHIO; NORTHERN SKY','','katalog A118; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9042, IMG_9044; The pencil signature is written in block capitals and reads ''MON SCHIO''; it is clearest on the companion lots A120 and A121, but the letter group SCH could also be read SER or SCR. This artist name has not been verified against any reference.','no certificate photographed; pencil-signed, titled and numbered in the margin','IMG_9037',32.0,38.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Blue", "Purple", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(167,'ilan-167','tablo','yayinda','Sky Lore II, Signed Limited Edition Print, MON SCHIO, Numbered Edition, Framed','MON SCHIO. Two large discs dominate - a mottled gold one above and a saturated ultramarine one below, ringed in crimson - set against a ground that shifts from bronze and oxblood to deep plum. A fine silver crescent arcs over the gold disc, a tapering red spire rises from the lower left, and small blue leaf shapes and a pale pink moon are scattered around the edges. Fine ruled lines and drawn arcs tie the elements together over a heavily speckled, weathered-metal surface. Second in a numbered series; pencil signed, titled and numbered in the bottom margin. Medium: serigraph or lithograph on paper. Signed lower left margin, in pencil, reading "MON SCHIO". Edition: 17/450. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: MON SCHIO; SKY LORE II; 17/450. Condition: Sheet clean and bright, no foxing seen. Reflections on the glass in the angled shots; frame in good order.','MON SCHIO','SKY LORE II','1980s-1990s','serigraph or lithograph on paper','17/450','','','MON SCHIO; SKY LORE II; 17/450','','katalog A119; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9051, IMG_9052; The title is transcribed from a rough pencil hand as ''SKY LORE II''; the final word could conceivably read LORD or LOND. The signature reads ''MON SCHIO'' but the second word is ambiguous (SCH / SER / SCR). Same artist and series as A118, A120 and A121.','no certificate photographed; pencil-signed, titled and numbered in the margin','IMG_9045',31.75,42.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "seascape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Blue", "Purple", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(168,'ilan-168','tablo','yayinda','Sky Lore I, Signed Limited Edition Print, MON SCHIO, Numbered Edition, Framed','MON SCHIO. A large lavender-blue disc sits top right beside a pale crescent and a small cobalt dot, while below a great oxblood circle and a soft blue arc balance the design. At the centre a slim chequered column in pink, cream and gold rises to a red gabled cap, crossed by fine horizontal rules and a delicate stem with leaves. The ground is a rich mottled bronze flecked with gold and mauve, and the whole is drawn with light silver linework. First in the numbered series; pencil signed, titled and numbered in the bottom margin. Medium: serigraph or lithograph on paper. Signed lower centre margin, in pencil, reading "MON SCHIO". Edition: 13/450. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: MON SCHIO; SKY LORE I; 13/450. Condition: Clean bright sheet with no visible foxing or waviness. Some glare on the glass; frame sound.','MON SCHIO','SKY LORE I','1980s-1990s','serigraph or lithograph on paper','13/450','','','MON SCHIO; SKY LORE I; 13/450','','katalog A120; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9059, IMG_9060; Title transcribed as ''SKY LORE I'' from a rough pencil hand; the third word could read LORD or LOND. Artist signature reads ''MON SCHIO'' with the second word ambiguous. Companion to A118, A119 and A121, which share the frame, format and 450-piece edition size.','no certificate photographed; pencil-signed, titled and numbered in the margin','IMG_9053',31.4,42.2,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Purple", "Gold", "Blue", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(169,'ilan-169','tablo','yayinda','Sky Lore III, Signed Limited Edition Print, MON SCHIO, Numbered Edition, Framed','MON SCHIO. A pale ladder climbs the centre of the sheet past a large mottled gold disc and a cobalt-blue sphere marked with a fine constellation, while a red-capped chequered post stands at the base. Crescents in silver and gold sweep across the upper third and a rose-red circle is outlined at the right. The ground is a soft plum and rose wash over bronze speckle, the whole held together by thin ruled lines and drawn arcs. Third in the numbered series; pencil signed, titled and numbered in the bottom margin. Medium: serigraph or lithograph on paper. Signed lower centre margin, in pencil, reading "MON SCHIO". Edition: 9/450. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: MON SCHIO; SKY LORE III; 9/450. Condition: Sheet clean and bright with no visible foxing. Reflections on the glass in the angled views; frame in good condition.','MON SCHIO','SKY LORE III','1980s-1990s','serigraph or lithograph on paper','9/450','','','MON SCHIO; SKY LORE III; 9/450','','katalog A121; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9068, IMG_9069; This is the clearest of the four title inscriptions and reads ''SKY LORE III'', which is why the whole series has been transcribed as SKY LORE. The artist signature reads ''MON SCHIO''; the second word is ambiguous and could be SER or SCR.','no certificate photographed; pencil-signed, titled and numbered in the margin','IMG_9062',31.5,41.9,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Pink", "Gold", "Blue", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(170,'ilan-170','tablo','yayinda','Fanch, Garden Terrace Through Open Windows, Numbered Edition, Framed','Fanch. Tall white multi-pane French windows are thrown open onto a sunlit terrace laid with irregular honey-coloured flagstones. Beyond them a formal garden of clipped lawn, palm trees and a turquoise pool leads to a range of snow-topped mountains under a pink and pale-blue sky. Inside, a wrought-iron table and chairs, a classical bust on a mahogany console and a rose-red dado ground the foreground. Everything is drawn with crisp, even outlines and filled with flat, clean colour in the artist''s characteristic naive-precise manner. Pencil signed and numbered in the margin, under glass with a cream mat. Medium: serigraph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Fanch". Edition: 143/250. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Fanch; 143/250; label photographed as IMG_9077, moved here from A123. Condition: Sheet appears clean and unfaded, colours strong. Reflections on the glass in several frames; gilt frame shows light rubbing on the high points.','Fanch','','1980s-1990s','serigraph on paper','143/250','','','Fanch; 143/250; label photographed as IMG_9077, moved here from A123','','katalog A122; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9075, IMG_9076; The pencil signature clearly reads ''Fanch''. A printed biography label found taped to the paper backing photographed under A123 (IMG_9077) identifies ''Francois (Fanch) Ledan born 1949, France'' and describes his lithography from 1973 - that label almost certainly belongs to this lot rather than to A123, but it was photographed on the adjacent frame, so the connection is inferred, not proven. No title is inscribed on the sheet.','no certificate photographed with this lot, but see note on the biography label in A123','IMG_9070',40.0,38.7,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["folk", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["White", "Red", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(171,'ilan-171','tablo','yayinda','Simbari, Boy on Bicycle, Signed Lithograph, Numbered Edition, Framed','Simbari. Broad slabs of unmixed colour build the scene: sheets and striped towels in red, white and cobalt hang across the right half, while a small figure in violet and pink pushes a bicycle along a shadowed path at the left. The garden behind is laid in with vigorous vertical strokes of olive, sap green and cadmium yellow, and the whole surface is worked with the flat palette-knife touch typical of the artist. There is no modelling and almost no line - the picture is held together entirely by colour blocks and their edges. Pencil signed and numbered in the margin, with a gallery certificate on the backing paper. Medium: lithograph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Simbari". Edition: 297/300. Accompanied by a certificate: Typed certificate of authenticity taped to the paper backing certifying ''Boy on Bicycle'' as a lithograph by Simbari, edition number 297/300. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 297/300; MAGNA GALLERY; CERTIFICATE OF AUTHENTICITY; This is to Certify that. Condition: Sheet and mat are clean; the mat has slightly warm/toned edges. The brown paper backing is intact with original tape and hanging cord. Reflections on the glass in most frames.','Simbari','Boy on Bicycle','third quarter of the 20th century','lithograph on paper','297/300','','MAGNA GALLERY','297/300; MAGNA GALLERY; CERTIFICATE OF AUTHENTICITY','','katalog A123; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9083, IMG_9084; The certificate types the artist as ''Simbari'' (Nicola Simbari is the obvious candidate but is not named on the label). IMG_9077, also filed under this lot, shows a printed biography of ''Francois (Fanch) Ledan born 1949, France'' taped to a brown paper backing - that label describes a different artist and almost certainly belongs to lot A122; it is recorded here because the photograph sits in this lot''s sequence. The pencil signature is fluent but only partly legible; it is consistent with ''Simbari'' as typed on the certificate.','Typed certificate of authenticity taped to the paper backing certifying ''Boy on Bicycle'' as a lithograph by Simbari, edition number 297/300.','IMG_9078',43.5,40.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Yellow", "Blue", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(172,'ilan-172','tablo','yayinda','Brittany Village Lane, Signed Serigraph Artist''s Proof, Christian Title, Signed in the Plate, Framed','Christian Title. An impressionist village view built from short, loaded strokes: a rutted lane sweeps in from the lower right past a low whitewashed wall, leading the eye to a cluster of stone cottages with terracotta roofs and a slender clock tower. A stand of tall poplars rises at the right against a bank of blue-grey and cream cloud, while at the left a field of rust and crimson foliage burns beside a picket fence. The palette is cool blue and green-grey against warm russet and terracotta, and a single small figure walks the lane. Presented with a wide blush-linen double mat inside a broad gold moulding under glass. Medium: serigraph on paper. Edition: limited edition of 60; the numbers 60 and 8 are struck through and the ''artist''s proof'' box is ticked, so this is designated an artist''s proof. Accompanied by a certificate: Certifies an original serigraph by Christian Title titled ''Brittany'', designated an artist''s proof, issued 8/13/90. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Certificate of Authenticity; This certifies, to the best of our knowledge, based on the information furnished to us, that this work of art is authentic as described below:; Media: Original Serigraph; Artist: Christian Title. Condition: No damage visible through the glass. Heavy overhead glare on the glazing in the angled shots. The backing paper is scuffed and the certificate is taped to it with a lifting corner.','Christian Title','Brittany','late 20th century; certificate dated 8/13/90','serigraph on paper','limited edition of 60; the numbers 60 and 8 are struck through and the ''artist''s proof'' box is ticked, so this is designated an artist''s proof','','Fine Arts Gallery, Inc.','Certificate of Authenticity; This certifies, to the best of our knowledge, based on the information furnished to us, that this work of art is authentic as described below:; Media: Original Serigraph','','katalog A124; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9089, IMG_9090; No artist signature is visible on the sheet itself: the lower edge of the image sits under the mat in every shot. The artist name is read from the handwritten certificate, where the surname is legible as ''Title'' but is cursive. The edition line is contradictory - both the edition size and the copy number are struck through in favour of the artist''s proof tick.','Certifies an original serigraph by Christian Title titled ''Brittany'', designated an artist''s proof, issued 8/13/90.','IMG_9086',43.1,37.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Orange", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(173,'ilan-173','tablo','yayinda','Large Crimson and Magenta Abstract on Canvas, Audrey Salkind, Signed, Unframed','Audrey Salkind. A tall unframed canvas dominated by a broad upper mass of crimson, raspberry and oxblood laid in wide flat strokes, some scraped back to reveal the weave. Across the centre a horizontal band of cobalt blue, chalk white and dark plum breaks the red like a distant shoreline, with two short blue dashes set as a deliberate counter-accent. The lower third opens into pale cream and blush, streaked by drips and a rust-red vertical that bleeds downward. Handling is loose and palette-knife flat rather than impasto, and the sides of the stretcher are painted, so it hangs unframed. Medium: acrylic on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas face, in thin grey-blue line, reading "Audrey Salkind". Condition: No tears, punctures or flaking visible. Surface shows a satin sheen and camera flare in the raking shots; the canvas edges are clean.','Audrey Salkind','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic on canvas','','','','','','katalog A125; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9096, IMG_9097; The signature is scratched in very lightly over the pale ground; the surname reads clearly as ''Salkind'' but the first name is faint and ''Audrey'' is the best but not certain reading. Whether the paint is acrylic or thinned oil cannot be settled from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9092',30.0,40.0,'canvas',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Pink", "Blue", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(174,'ilan-174','tablo','yayinda','Small Still Life, Lidded Bowl and Kumquats, Signed, Framed','An intimate tonal still life: a squat lidded bowl in warm cream and grey sits centre-left, its knob catching the light, with two or three small orange fruits and one green leaf arranged around its base. The background is worked in dry, dragged strokes of dove grey, pale blue and cream that read as a studio wall rather than a described space. Everything is held in a narrow tonal band so that the orange fruits carry all the colour weight. The canvas weave shows through the thinner passages and the paint is applied softly, with no heavy impasto. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, in dark cursive. Condition: No visible damage, craquelure or losses; the frame is intact with light handling marks.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A126; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9100, IMG_9101; The signature was photographed twice at close range and is still not legible; it is a fast cursive that appears to end in ''-liff'' or ''-iff'', but no reliable transcription is possible, so no name is recorded. Oil versus acrylic cannot be confirmed from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9098',13.0,10.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gray", "Blue", "Beige", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(175,'ilan-175','tablo','yayinda','Presentazione, Antique Equestrian Engraving, Signed, Framed, 1893','A large monochrome plate in the Victorian sporting-genre manner. At the left a mounted rider in top hat and dark coat holds three horses on a gravel walk before a castellated house half-hidden in trees; at the right a young man in pale breeches gestures towards a lady in a long white dress and wide hat, seated on a stone bench beside a low wall. A whippet stands on the steps between the two groups. The tone runs from deep velvety blacks in the horses and foliage to soft open greys in the sky and the lady''s dress, and the paper has warmed to a uniform ivory-tan. Lettered beneath the plate in small letterpress, mounted without a mat in a black-and-gilt frame under glass. Medium: photogravure or steel engraving on paper. Signed in the plate, lower left inside the image, reading "S. E. Waller. 1893.". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: PAINTED BY E.B. DAVIS; PRESENTAZIONE. Condition: The sheet is age-toned overall with light scattered foxing in the margins and a darker tide-line along the upper edge. Frame corners show rubbing and small losses to the gilt. Strong glass glare in every shot.','','PRESENTAZIONE','late 19th century; the plate is dated 1893','photogravure or steel engraving on paper','','','','PAINTED BY E.B. DAVIS; PRESENTAZIONE','','katalog A127; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9106, IMG_9107; Two conflicting attributions appear on the sheet. The in-plate signature reads ''S. E. Waller. 1893.'' though the surname could be ''Walter''; the letterpress credit beneath the plate reads ''PAINTED BY ?.B. DAVIS'' with the first initial indistinct (E or R). Because they disagree, no single artist name is recorded. The engraver/publisher line at the lower right of the sheet is present but too small and glare-obscured to read. The Italian title suggests an Italian-market printing of an English painting.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9102',28.7,24.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "animal", "figurative", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Brown", "Gray", "Beige", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(176,'ilan-176','tablo','yayinda','Red Tulips, Original Signed Watercolour, CAROL VOROSMARTI, Signed, Framed','CAROL VOROSMARTI. A wet-in-wet floral watercolour in which seven or eight tulip heads in crimson, rose and coral float across a diffused pink and lilac wash. The stems and blade leaves are painted in olive, sage and blue-green with confident single strokes, several of them left to bleed into the background so the bouquet has no hard edge. White paper is reserved for highlights on the petals and a scatter of pigment splatter animates the lower ground. The handling is fluid and unlaboured throughout. Set in a wide cream mat behind glass in a slim polished silver metal frame. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower left of the sheet, in pencil, reading "CAROL VOROSMARTI". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: CAROL VOROSMARTI. Condition: No foxing or fading visible through the glass. Old tape residue and a lifting adhesive patch on the inside of the glass at the upper right corner of the frame; the metal frame corner there is slightly open.','CAROL VOROSMARTI','','late 20th century','watercolour on paper','','','','CAROL VOROSMARTI','','katalog A128; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9112, IMG_9113; The signature is pencil on the painted sheet and reads clearly, but no date, title or edition information is present. Nothing was photographed of the reverse.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9110',28.25,22.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Red", "Green", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(177,'ilan-177','tablo','yayinda','Picot, Two Femmes au Jardin a Theoule, Picot, Jean-claude, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 2000','Picot, Jean-claude. A high-keyed Riviera view looking down over a terraced garden to a wide turquoise bay with a headland, small islands and a freighter on the horizon. Umbrella pines, a tall palm and a flowering pink tree frame the descent, while ruled rows of vines and a red-roofed villa fill the middle ground. In the upper corner two seated figures in red take the shade under an orange awning. The colour is fauve-bright and unmodulated: cerulean and turquoise water, emerald and olive foliage, coral pink blossom and ochre paths, all drawn with quick calligraphic outlines. Presented in a white mat with a lavender inner border inside an ornate gilt moulding under glass. Medium: seriolithograph in colour on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, below the image, reading "J Picot". Edition: From the edition of 9500; signed in the plate. Accompanied by a certificate: Park West Gallery COA no. 109084 guaranteeing a 2000 seriolithograph by Jean-Claude Picot, 15 3/4 x 20 in, plate-signed, from an edition of 9500, signed by director Albert Scaglione. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: PARK WEST GALLERY; Certificate of Authenticity; According to the terms of the guarantee on the verso of this certificate, we guarantee the authorship of the following work of art:; Registration No. 109084. Condition: Image and mat appear clean and unfaded. A small adhesive/tape residue mark sits on the mat near the top edge, visible in IMG_9118. Glass glare in the angled shots.','Picot, Jean-claude','Two Femmes au Jardin a Theoule','2000, per the certificate','seriolithograph in colour on paper','From the edition of 9500; signed in the plate','','Park West Gallery','PARK WEST GALLERY; Certificate of Authenticity; According to the terms of the guarantee on the verso of this certificate, we guarantee the authorship of the following work of art:','','katalog A129; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9118, IMG_9119; The signature in the lower margin reads as a short ''J Picot'' flourish; the certificate states the work is signed in the plate rather than hand-signed, so the mark on the sheet should be treated as a plate signature, not an autograph. Only the frame was measured; the sheet size comes from the certificate, not from the tape.','Park West Gallery COA no. 109084 guaranteeing a 2000 seriolithograph by Jean-Claude Picot, 15 3/4 x 20 in, plate-signed, from an edition of 9500, signed by director Albert Scaglione.','IMG_9114',30.0,26.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Blue", "Green", "Black", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(178,'ilan-178','obje','yayinda','The Last Supper, Silvered Metal Relief Plaque, Framed','A deep repousse relief in silvered metal reworking Leonardo''s composition: the long draped table runs the full width with the apostles grouped in agitated threes, Christ calm at the centre beneath a coffered ceiling and a round-headed doorway. Fluted columns rise at each end, each with a small standing putto on a moulded base and a grotesque mask below. A ribbon panel across the foot carries the Latin text in raised capitals. The metal is bright on the high points and darkened in the recesses, giving a strong pewter-to-charcoal contrast. Set in a deep ebonised composition frame with a moulded foliate scroll pattern and a copper-toned inner slip. Medium: silvered or electroplated metal repousse relief on a board backing. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: AMEN DICO VOBIS QUIA UNUS VESTRUM ME TRADITURUS EST; M. REGISTRADA. Condition: Tarnish and darkening throughout the recesses, which reads as age rather than damage. Light rubbing to the black frame at the corners and a small chip at the lower right. No dents or splits in the relief.','','','mid 20th century','silvered or electroplated metal repousse relief on a board backing','','','','AMEN DICO VOBIS QUIA UNUS VESTRUM ME TRADITURUS EST; M. REGISTRADA','','katalog A130; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9125, IMG_9126; The mark ''M. REGISTRADA'' (Spanish for registered trademark) is stamped into the floor of the relief at the lower right, but no maker name is legible beside it, so the country of manufacture is a suggestion only. Whether the plaque is solid metal, a plated electroform or a metallised composition cannot be judged from photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9121',30.25,19.7,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": [], "medium": ["panel"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Silver", "Gray", "Black", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(179,'ilan-179','tablo','yayinda','Egyptian Papyrus, Cartouches and Fruiting Tree, Signed, Framed','A hand-painted papyrus with deliberately ragged deckle edges, laid on a deep brick-red backing. Two tall vertical cartouches with feathered wing motifs and blue-and-red banded columns stand at either side, each enclosing a stack of hieroglyphs including a falcon, a white ibis, a red vessel and a fish. Between them a spreading tree in olive and sage bears small red fruits, with a black-and-white crested hoopoe perched above and a blue bird below. The papyrus fibre grain runs visibly across the whole sheet, and the colour is opaque and flatly laid within crisp black outlines. Broad copper-gilt flat frame. Medium: gouache and ink on papyrus. Signed lower centre, on the papyrus beside the tree trunk. Condition: The papyrus is intact with its natural irregular edges and fibre voids; no tears, creases or losses seen. The red mount board is clean and the frame finish is even.','','','late 20th century','gouache and ink on papyrus','','','','','','katalog A131; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9131, IMG_9132; A short scrawled signature in a cursive script sits at the base of the tree but is not legible. It is unclear from the photographs whether the frame is glazed; the tape appears to rest directly on the surface in IMG_9131, which suggests no glass. The ragged edges are decorative and typical of modern papyrus production, so the sheet should not be taken as antique.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9127',25.7,22.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life", "animal"], "medium": ["watercolour", "ink", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(180,'ilan-180','tablo','yayinda','Southwest Figure in Green Hat, Framed Print, Signed, Framed','A boldly graphic Santa Fe style composition. A seated figure wrapped in a striped serape of gold, purple and rust leans forward beneath a wide green hat trimmed with a feather; a smaller wrapped figure rests against them. Behind, purple and magenta mesas rise into a lilac and gold sky, with an adobe wall and a dark window at the right. The whole image is enclosed by a painted geometric border of turquoise, terracotta and blue Southwestern banding, and a stylised flower motif sits at the foot. Flat unmodelled colour and heavy black contour lines throughout, with faint dot structure visible in the graded passages. Cream mount inside a chunky off-white painted frame under glass. Medium: offset lithograph or colour reproduction on paper. Signed lower left within the image, in dark cursive over the purple robe. Condition: The painted frame is chipped and scuffed along the outer edges and at the corners, with a small dark mark on the top rail. Dust and glare on the glass. The image itself shows no fading or foxing.','','','late 20th century','offset lithograph or colour reproduction on paper','','','','','','katalog A132; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9136, IMG_9137; The signature is a long flowing two-word cursive over a dark ground and could not be resolved even at high magnification; it appears to end in ''-rman'' and ''-rns'' but no reliable transcription is possible, so no name is recorded. No edition number, plate mark or deckle is visible, and faint even dot structure in the graded areas points to a photomechanical reproduction rather than an original serigraph, but the glazing prevents certainty. Note that frame IMG_9134 is absent from this listing.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9133',16.65,14.85,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Pink", "Gold", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(181,'ilan-181','tablo','yayinda','Chrysanthemums in a Blue Vase, Oil Painting, Framed','A generous bouquet fills almost the whole canvas: dense white and cream pompom chrysanthemums cluster at the left and right, with butter yellow, russet-red and dusty lilac blooms massed through the centre and a few slender stems breaking free at the top. The flowers are built from short loaded touches of impasto so the petals catch real light, while the leaves are dropped in as loose olive and blue-green strokes. Below, a rounded jug in soft powder blue sits on a grey cloth against a pale, scrubbed background of warm white and grey. Traditional and painterly, with a quiet, chalky palette. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: No craquelure, flaking or tears visible. A small pale mark on the shoulder of the blue jug may be a paint highlight or a tiny loss. Frame is clean with light rubbing on the outer edge.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog A133; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9139, IMG_9140; No signature was found in any photograph, and neither the reverse nor the stretcher was shot, so the work is unattributed. Only three frames exist for this listing and there is no close-up of the paint surface, so oil versus acrylic rests on the impasto and canvas weave visible in the tape shots.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9138',15.15,17.6,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["White", "Yellow", "Blue", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(182,'ilan-182','tablo','yayinda','German Night Street with Lamp, Signed Etching, Bruno Bielefeld, Signed, Framed','Bruno Bielefeld. A moody nocturne of a German old town. A steep-gabled house with dormers and a half-timbered upper storey dominates the left, its windows glowing amber against a night of granular charcoal and umber. A wrought-iron lamp on a scrolled bracket burns at the right, throwing light down a narrow cobbled lane where a lone figure walks past shuttered shopfronts and a tangle of climbing foliage. Tone is built in soft aquatint-like granulation rather than line, with warm sepia and amber lifting the darkest passages. The sheet has toned to a deep tan and is presented without a mat, directly behind glass in a dark carved wooden frame. Medium: etching with aquatint on paper, warm-toned. Signed in pencil in the lower right margin, beneath the plate, reading "Bruno Bielefeld". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Bruno Bielefeld. Condition: The sheet is browned overall with age, with a distinct darker stain and abrasion at the upper right of the margin and scattered foxing. The frame has losses and flaking to the moulding at the upper left corner. Heavy reflections on the glass throughout.','Bruno Bielefeld','','early to mid 20th century','etching with aquatint on paper, warm-toned','','','','Bruno Bielefeld','','katalog A134; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_9145, IMG_9146; The pencil signature reads as ''Bruno Bielefeld'' but is very faint and photographed through glass, so the reading is good rather than certain. A second faint pencil annotation sits in the lower left margin (usually the technique or edition on prints of this type) and is completely illegible. Whether this is an original etching with aquatint or a photogravure reproduction cannot be settled without seeing a plate mark, which is hidden by the frame rebate.','no certificate photographed','IMG_9142',13.6,16.6,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Orange", "Gray", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(183,'ilan-183','tablo','yayinda','Large Crimson and Orange Abstract Canvas, Signed, Unframed','A large square gallery-wrapped canvas built from broad blocks of deep crimson and burgundy set against creamy off-white and pale grey grounds. A central passage of magenta, violet and orange is pulled through with thin dragged lines and scraped edges, and a vertical ribbon of orange runs down the left. The paint is applied thinly and dry-brushed so the weave shows through, with soft feathered boundaries rather than hard edges; the painted image continues around the sides of the stretcher. Medium: acrylic or oil on canvas. Signed top edge of the canvas (turnover edge), centre, reading "Audrey Salkind". Condition: No visible damage; surface reads as clean with light handling marks on the canvas edges. Photographed leaning on a tiled floor, so the lower edge is not fully visible.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic or oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog B001; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7796, IMG_7797; The pencil signature on the top canvas edge is faint; it reads plausibly as ''Audrey Salkind'' but the surname is not certain, so no artist name is entered as a confirmed reading. Acrylic versus thinned oil cannot be told apart from the photographs.','no certificate seen','IMG_7793',42.0,42.0,'canvas',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Beige", "Orange", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(184,'ilan-184','tablo','yayinda','Still Life with Oranges and Lemon, Framed','A boldly painted still life in which oranges and a single bright yellow lemon sit in a blue-rimmed bowl above a table crowded with an orange-filled jar, a striped tumbler and a glass bowl with a spoon laid across it. The palette is dominated by saturated orange, cobalt and teal against olive and grey-green shadows. Handling is broad and opaque, with visible directional brushwork and unmodulated colour blocks that flatten the forms in a modernist manner. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: No visible damage, tears or losses; some surface sheen in the photographs. The reverse and the canvas edges were not shown.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog B002; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7800, IMG_7801; No signature was found on the visible surface and the reverse was not photographed, so the artist is unknown. Canvas versus board could not be confirmed because the edges are hidden by the liner.','no certificate seen','IMG_7799',27.5,34.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Blue", "Yellow", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(185,'ilan-185','tablo','yayinda','''Sing Praises'' Signed Print of Rearing Horses, Richardson, Numbered Edition, Framed, 1997','Richardson. A limited-edition print in which two ghostly white horses rear out of a smoky black and charcoal ground. The animals are drawn with rapid scratched white lines, while the surrounding field is worked in grainy aquatint-like tone. Bursts of rust red at the left and cobalt and turquoise at the right frame the composition, and the image sits on a wide untouched paper margin carrying the pencil title, number and signature. Medium: colour etching / aquatint on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "Richardson ''97". Edition: 33/35. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 33/35; "Sing Praises"; Richardson ''97. Condition: Heavy reflections and glare on the glazing in every shot; no tears, foxing or staining visible through the glass.','Richardson','Sing Praises','1997','colour etching / aquatint on paper','33/35','','','33/35; "Sing Praises"; Richardson ''97','','katalog B003; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7805, IMG_7806; Only the surname ''Richardson'' is legible in the pencil signature; no first name is present. The printing process is judged from a grainy tonal surface seen through glass and could be an etching, a lithograph or a monotype.','no certificate seen','IMG_7802',16.75,16.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape", "animal"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "White", "Orange", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(186,'ilan-186','tablo','yayinda','Artist''s Proof Floral Fantasy with Hidden Faces, Signed in the Plate, Framed','A flowing horizontal composition of blooms that dissolve into human profiles and half-hidden faces, drawn with fine black contour lines over freely bled washes. Colour moves diagonally from hot orange and crimson at the left through magenta and gold to green, turquoise and deep blue at the right, all floating on a cream ground. A pale bird-like form sits at the lower centre, and the handling is deliberately liquid, with feathered and blotted edges. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower centre of the sheet, in ink, reading "E.A.". Edition: E.A. (epreuve d''artiste / artist''s proof). Inscribed on the reverse or mount: E.A.. Condition: Strong point-source reflections on the glazing; no tears, foxing or discolouration visible through the glass.','','','late 20th century','colour lithograph on paper','E.A. (epreuve d''artiste / artist''s proof)','','','E.A.','','katalog B004; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7809, IMG_7810; The name following ''E.A.'' is a rapid flourished signature and cannot be read with confidence, so no artist name is recorded. The same signature appears on B005. The medium is inferred: the ''E.A.'' annotation indicates a print edition, but the washes are so liquid that an original watercolour cannot be entirely excluded.','no certificate seen','IMG_7807',30.0,22.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Red", "Pink", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(187,'ilan-187','tablo','yayinda','Artist''s Proof Charcoal Study of Violinist and Companion, Signed in the Plate, Framed','A tall monochrome study of two slender figures pressed close together, the rear one drawing a bow across a violin while the other leans back with her hair falling in long strokes. The drawing is built from feathery charcoal hatching that leaves the faces smooth and pale and dissolves the gown into loose vertical sweeps at the hem. The paper is left bare around the figures so the group floats without background. Medium: lithograph after a charcoal drawing, on paper. Signed lower left of the sheet, in ink, reading "E.A.". Edition: E.A. (epreuve d''artiste / artist''s proof). Inscribed on the reverse or mount: E.A.. Condition: Reflections and a soft haze on the glazing; no visible foxing, tears or losses.','','','late 20th century','lithograph after a charcoal drawing, on paper','E.A. (epreuve d''artiste / artist''s proof)','','','E.A.','','katalog B005; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7814, IMG_7815; The signature after ''E.A.'' is a flourish that reads roughly as ''J. de Vas'' but cannot be resolved at this resolution, so no artist name is recorded. It appears to be the same hand as B004. Whether this is a printed edition or an original charcoal drawing cannot be settled through the glass, though the ''E.A.'' annotation points to a print.','no certificate seen','IMG_7812',24.0,31.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Black", "Beige", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(188,'ilan-188','tablo','yayinda','Wet Country Lane with Bare Trees, Signed, Framed','A muddy country lane recedes into the middle distance, its puddles catching pale sky light in slabs of ochre, white and grey. Tall bare and half-leafed trees rise on both sides against a soft blue sky broken by cumulus. The foreground is worked wet and loose with thick impasto ridges and palette-knife drags in umber, olive and yellow-green, while the distant field and hedgerow are handled thinly. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the image, in red paint. Condition: Bright reflections across the glazing in several shots; the frame shows light rubbing on the corners. No tears or losses visible.','','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog B006; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7819, IMG_7820; The red signature at the lower right is a rapid cursive flourish and is not legible at any available resolution. The work is glazed, which is unusual for an oil; the support could be canvas board rather than stretched canvas.','no certificate seen','IMG_7817',23.5,27.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Green", "Gold", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(189,'ilan-189','tablo','yayinda','Winter Watercolour of Stone Tower and Flag, Signed, Framed','A crenellated stone tower rises beside a low gabled lodge with a red roof, framed by dark evergreen spruces and a flagpole carrying the Stars and Stripes. The sky is laid in with loose blue and grey washes and the snow-covered foreground is left largely as bare paper with pale grey-green shadow strokes. Handling is fluid and transparent, with dry-brush texture picking out the masonry and branches. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right of the image, in black ink, reading "Nickou". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Nickou. Condition: Reflections and light haze on the glazing; the image itself shows no foxing, staining or cockling that is visible through the glass.','','','late 20th century','watercolour on paper','','','','Nickou','','katalog B007; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7824, IMG_7825; The signature is a looped initial followed by block letters that read as ''NICKOU''; the initial and the exact spelling are not certain. Whether the sheet is an original watercolour or a high-quality reproduction cannot be settled through the glass, although the pigment pooling suggests an original.','no certificate seen','IMG_7821',24.5,21.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "White", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(190,'ilan-190','tablo','yayinda','Blue Barn and Willow Tree Oil Painting, Framed','A tall blue-grey clapboard barn with an open loft stands at the left, its timbers picked out in strokes of slate and white, while a broad-crowned willow spreads over the centre in short green and grey dabs. A low rail fence and a rust-red outbuilding run across the middle ground above a meadow of yellow and green flecks. The paint is thick and choppy throughout, with pronounced impasto and a visible craquelure over the sky. Medium: oil on canvas. Condition: Fine craquelure is visible across the sky and upper paint layers; the frame shows rubbing, small losses to the gilding and general age wear. No tears or flaking noted.','','','mid 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog B008; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7828, IMG_7829; No signature was found in the corners that were photographed, and the reverse was not shown. The support is judged canvas from the weave visible under the impasto but could be canvas board.','no certificate seen','IMG_7827',22.25,18.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Green", "Yellow", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(191,'ilan-191','obje','yayinda','Gothic Brass Rubbing of Madonna and Child, Framed','A brass rubbing taken in silver-white wax on near-black paper, showing the crowned Virgin seated on a canopied Gothic throne with the Child on her knee. Her mantle falls in long looping folds that are rendered as thousands of parallel rubbed lines, and the halo, crocketed pinnacles and traceried canopy are picked out in fine crisp detail. The strong tonal reversal gives the whole sheet the look of a negative engraving. Medium: wax rubbing (brass rubbing) on dark paper. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 125 (handwritten in black on a round red price sticker on the glass, upper right). Condition: The glazing is dusty and scuffed with a round red price sticker adhered at the upper right; the black frame shows minor rubbing. The rubbing itself appears intact with no tears visible.','','','20th century rubbing after a medieval brass','wax rubbing (brass rubbing) on dark paper','','','','125 (handwritten in black on a round red price sticker on the glass, upper right)','','katalog B009; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7833, IMG_7834; The brass being reproduced is not identified anywhere on the piece, and there is no artist, church or date inscription. The reverse was not photographed.','no certificate seen','IMG_7831',11.25,17.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Silver", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(192,'ilan-192','tablo','yayinda','1985 Presidential Inauguration Gala Poster, Signed, Framed, 1985','A large celebratory poster reproducing a loosely painted head-and-shoulders portrait of a laughing grey-haired man in a dark suit and white collar. The face is built entirely from short unblended strokes of peach, coral, pale blue, ochre and green over a cobalt sky-blue ground, with the same broken colour running through the shoulders. A white band across the foot carries the title in classical capitals, and a pencil dedication and signature run above it. Medium: offset lithograph poster on paper. Signed lower centre right, in pencil across the white band, reading "James paul". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: PRESIDENTIAL INAUGURATION - A TASTE OF AMERICA; for Clyde ~ 1985 ~ James paul (pencil, across the white lower band). Condition: Several bright point reflections on the glazing; the sheet appears clean and unfaded with no visible tears or foxing.','','PRESIDENTIAL INAUGURATION - A TASTE OF AMERICA','1985','offset lithograph poster on paper','','','','PRESIDENTIAL INAUGURATION - A TASTE OF AMERICA; for Clyde ~ 1985 ~ James paul (pencil, across the white lower band)','','katalog B010; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7837, IMG_7838; The pencil line reads as a dedication, ''for Clyde ~ 1985 ~ James paul'', but the first word and the signature are hard to resolve, so the name is recorded with low confidence and not as a confirmed artist. The sitter is not named on the poster; the 1985 date and the inauguration title suggest Ronald Reagan''s second inauguration, but nothing on the sheet states this.','no certificate seen','IMG_7835',32.25,25.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Gold", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(193,'ilan-193','tablo','yayinda','Marsha Newfield ''Catching Butterflies'' Lithograph, Numbered Edition, Framed','MARSHA NEWFIELD. A charming folk-style lithograph of a boy in a yellow polka-dot shirt and a girl in denim reaching skyward toward a cluster of butterflies. Around and below them the ground is filled with flat outlined daisies, blue and pink blooms and leafy sprigs, plus more butterflies at the lower edge. Everything is drawn with an even black contour line and filled with clear flat colour on a cream ground bounded by a printed yellow border. Medium: lithograph on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil, reading "marsha Newfield". Edition: 102/180, pencil signed. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: marsha Newfield (pencil, lower right of the sheet); MARSHA NEWFIELD   Titled: Catching Butterflies; Lithograph, Pencil Signed & # 102/180; Born in New York. Studied art in New York. She is an advocate of the Women''s Liberation Movement. She believes her art should provoke the inner feelings of all people. She loves children, and much of her work includes them.. Condition: The sheet has warmed to a cream tone with light overall toning; a small dark spot and a slight cockle appear at the lower right of the sheet near the yellow border. Glazing shows scattered reflections. The typed backing label is torn at its edges.','MARSHA NEWFIELD','Catching Butterflies','1970s to 1980s','lithograph on paper','102/180, pencil signed','','','marsha Newfield (pencil, lower right of the sheet); MARSHA NEWFIELD   Titled: Catching Butterflies; Lithograph, Pencil Signed & # 102/180','','katalog B011; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7841, IMG_7842; The edition number on the label reads 102/180 but the handwriting is cramped; the first digits could be misread. No edition number was found written on the sheet itself in the frames provided.','No certificate, but a typed biographical dealer label is glued to the backing board naming the artist, title, medium and edition number','IMG_7839',24.25,30.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Yellow", "Blue", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(194,'ilan-194','tablo','yayinda','Father Christmas with Toys and Tree, Signed, Framed','A vertical winter vignette of Father Christmas trudging through deep snow, a sack of toys on his back spilling a jack-in-the-box, a teddy bear, a doll and a trumpet, and a small decorated fir carried on a staff. His crimson coat and hat are trimmed with heavy white fur painted in thick raised strokes, and his beard is a mass of impasto white. The background is a soft blue-grey hillside flecked with falling snow, and the whole surface is heavily textured. Medium: oil on board. Signed lower left of the image, in pale yellow paint. Condition: Strong reflections and dust on the glazing; no damage visible to the painted surface.','','','late 20th century','oil on board','','','','','','katalog B012; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7846, IMG_7847; The pale signature at the lower left is illegible against the light ground; it appears to begin with a capital that could be an M, but no reading is recorded. Board versus canvas cannot be confirmed through the glass.','no certificate seen','IMG_7844',14.0,18.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "panel"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Red", "White", "Blue", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(195,'ilan-195','belge','yayinda','''We Saw the Sea'' Follow the Fleet Sheet Music, Signed, Framed, 1936','An Art Deco sheet-music cover printed in two colours, steel blue on cream. Fred Astaire in sailor whites and bell-bottoms and Ginger Rogers in a nautical blouse are shown mid-step with arms flung wide, balanced on the bow of a battleship above a band of stylised blue waves. The title is set in wide spaced sans-serif capitals across the top, with the credits and song list ranged below in small blue type. Medium: lithographed sheet music cover on paper. Signed upper right of the sheet, in faint pencil below the composer credit. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: WE SAW THE SEA; Lyrics and Music by IRVING BERLIN; From the RKO Musical Production "FOLLOW THE FLEET" starring FRED ASTAIRE and GINGER ROGERS; A Pandro S. Berman Production. Condition: The paper has toned to a warm tan with darker mottling across the upper area and along the edges, consistent with age; a faint pencil inscription sits at the upper right. No tears are visible through the glass.','','WE SAW THE SEA','1936 (Follow the Fleet was released that year)','lithographed sheet music cover on paper','','','','WE SAW THE SEA; Lyrics and Music by IRVING BERLIN; From the RKO Musical Production "FOLLOW THE FLEET" starring FRED ASTAIRE and GINGER ROGERS','','katalog B013; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7850, IMG_7851; A faint pencil signature under the Irving Berlin credit is illegible and could be a previous owner''s name rather than an autograph. The date 1936 comes from the film credited on the cover, not from a printed date on the sheet.','no certificate seen','IMG_7848',15.25,18.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "architecture", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(196,'ilan-196','tablo','yayinda','Abstract Charcoal Drawing with Coiled Eye Form, Signed, Framed','A dense charcoal drawing on cream paper in which smoky masses of black and grey are pulled into a rounded rectangular field. At its centre a tight spiral coil suggests an eye or shell, ringed by radiating scratched strokes, while heavier bands sweep across the lower half like a reclining form. The tone is built by smudging and stumping with sharper drawn lines cut through it, and the paper is left bare at the outer margins. Medium: charcoal on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil. Condition: The sheet shows light overall toning and a soft waviness; some glare on the glazing. No tears or losses visible.','','','mid to late 20th century','charcoal on paper','','','','','','katalog B014; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7855, IMG_7856; The pencil signature is a compact monogram-like flourish and cannot be resolved into letters. Charcoal versus lithographic crayon or a printed reproduction of a drawing cannot be settled through the glass.','no certificate seen','IMG_7852',22.5,20.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(197,'ilan-197','tablo','yayinda','East Asian Pine and Waterfall on Gold Ground, Signed, Framed','A horizontal landscape on a warm gold-ochre ground in which a twisted pine leans in from the right, its needle clusters dabbed in dark green and blue-green. Pale bands of white and cream sweep across the lower left to read as falling water and mist, with dark ink rocks anchoring the upper left corner. The ink work is calligraphic and economical, and a column of brushed characters with a red seal sits in the upper right. Medium: lithograph after an East Asian ink and colour painting. Signed upper right of the image: a vertical column of brushed characters with a red seal at its foot. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: a lithograph by John Glidden (pen, on the brown paper backing of the frame). Condition: The ground shows age toning, scattered dark specks and foxing-like spotting, with lighter rubbed patches in the pale water area. The brown paper backing is creased, dented and torn along one edge.','','','20th century','lithograph after an East Asian ink and colour painting','','','','a lithograph by John Glidden (pen, on the brown paper backing of the frame)','','katalog B015; olcu kareleri galeride degil: yok; The handwritten backing note says ''a lithograph by John Glidden'', which sits oddly with the East Asian brushwork and red seal on the front; the note may describe the print''s publisher or a previous attribution rather than the original artist. The vertical characters and the seal could not be transcribed at this resolution. No tape shots were provided, and it is not certain from the photographs whether the piece is glazed.','no certificate; the only documentation is the handwritten note on the paper backing','IMG_7858',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["print", "ink", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Green", "Beige", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(198,'ilan-198','tablo','yayinda','Antique East Asian Pine and Birds Painting, Signed, Framed','A wide ink-and-colour composition on a deeply toned ochre ground: a twisting pine with clusters of dark green needles rises from a rocky spur at lower right, while a pale drifted bank sweeps across the lower left. A small russet and dark bird perches on rock at upper left and a pale winged form hovers at upper right, with fine trailing willow strokes across the empty upper field. The palette is limited to earth ochre, sepia, deep green and a single note of vermilion, and the surface is heavily aged and mottled. Set in a gilt faux-bamboo frame with a dark red inner slip. Medium: ink and colour on paper, laid down. Signed upper right. Condition: Heavy overall discolouration and foxing of the ground, scattered dark stains and small losses, surface abrasion; frame gilding rubbed at the corners.','','','probably early to mid 20th century or earlier','ink and colour on paper, laid down','','','','','','katalog B016; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7861, IMG_7862; The red inscription and seal at upper right are calligraphic characters I cannot transcribe, so no artist can be read. Whether the work is Chinese or Japanese, and whether it is painted on paper or thin silk laid to board, is not certain from the photographs. It appears unglazed but no glass edge is visible to confirm.','no certificate present','IMG_7860',25.5,15.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "animal"], "medium": ["ink", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Brown", "Green", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(199,'ilan-199','tablo','yayinda','Watercolour of Bare Trees Beside Still Water, Signed, Framed','A soft, wet-in-wet watercolour of a bare-branched tree rising from a mossy bank of grey boulders, with slender saplings behind and a pale apricot glow of sky through the winter woods. The bank is mirrored in still water below in long vertical grey and umber reflections. The handling is restrained and atmospheric, with dry-brush twig work over broad washes on textured paper. Colours stay within grey, warm brown, soft green and a blush of pink. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, reading "Iva B. Hull M.H.". Condition: No visible damage to the image; light glare on the glass and slight toning of the mat.','','','mid to late 20th century','watercolour on paper','','','','','','katalog B017; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7866, IMG_7867; The pencil/ink signature is small and faint; I read it as ''Iva B. Hull'' followed by two more letters that may be initials, but the reading is tentative and I have not entered it as a confirmed artist name.','no certificate present','IMG_7863',13.0,17.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Brown", "Green", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(200,'ilan-200','tablo','yayinda','Signed Drypoint Christmas at Estill Fork Alabama, Constance Huddleston Anderson, Numbered Edition, Framed','Constance Huddleston Anderson. A small, finely worked intaglio print in warm sepia-brown ink: three or four figures sit bundled on a bench in the shadowed breezeway of a plank cabin, looking out through the open passage to sunlit trees and rough grass beyond. The image is built entirely from nervous, scratchy drypoint line, with dense cross-hatched shadow inside the passage and open white paper for the light outside. Printed on cream handmade paper with a visible plate impression and deckled edges, double matted in white. Medium: drypoint etching on handmade Italian paper. Signed in pencil below the plate, lower right, reading "Constance Anderson". Edition: 24/50. Accompanied by a certificate: Typed sheet taped to the backing board giving title, artist, medium and plate size (3 1/4" x 5 1/4") and explaining the drypoint process; it carries no issuer name or signature. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 24/50; Christmas at Estill Fork Alabama    Constance Anderson; Christmas at Estill Fork, Alabama / by Constance Huddleston Anderson / Drypoint, 3 1/4" x 5 1/4"; A drypoint is a form of etching. It is designated a drypoint because the artist etches directly into the plate, whereas an etching is done with acid.. Condition: Print clean and unfaded; the typed documentation sheet on the back is torn at the edges and toned, held with old tape.','Constance Huddleston Anderson','Christmas at Estill Fork, Alabama','mid to late 20th century','drypoint etching on handmade Italian paper','24/50','','','24/50; Christmas at Estill Fork Alabama    Constance Anderson; Christmas at Estill Fork, Alabama / by Constance Huddleston Anderson / Drypoint, 3 1/4" x 5 1/4"','','katalog B018; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7870, IMG_7871; The typed sheet gives the plate size as 3 1/4" x 5 1/4", but the printed image is taller than it is wide, so those figures may be listed height first or refer to the sheet.','Typed sheet taped to the backing board giving title, artist, medium and plate size (3 1/4" x 5 1/4") and explaining the drypoint process; it carries no issuer name or signature.','IMG_7868',10.0,13.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(201,'ilan-201','tablo','yayinda','East Asian Painting of Guardian Demon Figures, Framed','Painted on a mottled cream ground, a tall standing figure in a patterned leopard-spot robe holds a golden bowl at left, while two squat, muscular horned demons crouch to the right, one russet-skinned and one blue-black, each raising an instrument to its mouth. Drawing is in fine dark ink line with flat washes of iron red, slate, ochre and black, in the manner of Buddhist guardian imagery. The paper is heavily aged and cloudy, which gives the figures a smoky, antique presence. Presented in a plain bright gilt frame. Medium: ink and colour on paper. Condition: Ground heavily discoloured and blotched with age staining; scattered small losses and abrasion along the edges of the sheet.','','','probably 19th to early 20th century','ink and colour on paper','','','','','','katalog B019; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7875, IMG_7876; No signature, seal or inscription of any kind is visible, so origin (Japanese, Chinese or Korean) and date rest on style alone. Whether the support is paper or a fine silk laid down cannot be settled from the photographs.','no certificate present','IMG_7873',11.5,9.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["ink", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Red", "Gray", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(202,'ilan-202','tablo','yayinda','Hand-Coloured Etching 3200 O Street Georgetown, Joan Graybeal-Menard, Numbered Edition, Framed','Joan Graybeal-Menard. A crisp line etching of a Washington row-house street, hand-tinted in transparent watercolour: brick and clapboard fronts with stoops, shutters and window boxes recede down a sunlit pavement, a tall street lamp standing in the centre foreground. The line work is loose and calligraphic, the colour applied lightly in ochre for the pavement, soft blue-grey for the sidewalk, warm brick red and fresh green for the trees, with small accents of scarlet and yellow flowers. Printed on cream paper with a clear plate mark, double matted in grey with a gold inner line. Medium: line etching with hand-applied watercolour. Signed in pencil below the plate, lower right, reading "Joan Graybeal-Menard". Edition: 31/100. Accompanied by a certificate: Typed artist''s biography sheet headed ''Etching by Joan Graybeal-Menard'', tied to the back of the frame, describing the artist and the etching process. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 3200 O Street, Georgetown    31/100; Etching by Joan Graybeal-Menard; THE ARTIST: Joan Graybeal-Menard was born March 1954, in Washington, D.C. She has lived in Maryland, California, Ohio, and Georgia. She now lives in Virginia.; At an early age Joan showed interest in the arts and crafts, and with family encouragement was enrolled in public and private lessons, including studies during her family''s brief stays in Europe. Joan received her B.A. in Art from Marietta College in Ohio. She has worked for an arts and crafts shop, managed an art gallery, and taught child, adult and elderly arts and crafts classes. She presently works full time on her etchings.. Condition: Image and colour fresh; the typed sheet on the back is toned and creased. No visible foxing.','Joan Graybeal-Menard','3200 O Street, Georgetown','late 20th century','line etching with hand-applied watercolour','31/100','','','3200 O Street, Georgetown    31/100; Etching by Joan Graybeal-Menard; THE ARTIST: Joan Graybeal-Menard was born March 1954, in Washington, D.C. She has lived in Maryland, California, Ohio, and Georgia. She now lives in Virginia.','','katalog B020; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7880, IMG_7881; The pencil edition number reads as 31/100 but the final digits are small and could be another hundred-count. There is also a tiny signature within the plate at lower right that I cannot read separately.','Typed artist''s biography sheet headed ''Etching by Joan Graybeal-Menard'', tied to the back of the frame, describing the artist and the etching process.','IMG_7877',9.5,12.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life"], "medium": ["watercolour", "print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Red", "Green", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(203,'ilan-203','tablo','yayinda','Pastel Portrait of a Smiling Auburn-Haired Woman, Framed','A vigorous pastel head study of a woman with short auburn hair, blue eyes and a broad open smile, worked on toned paper. Flesh is built from strokes of terracotta, cream and rose left frankly visible, with cool blue-grey in the shadows of the neck and collar. The background is divided between a slate-blue panel at left and a scumbled ochre passage at right, both left deliberately unfinished. The touch is quick and confident, the whole thing more sketch than formal portrait. Medium: pastel on toned paper. Condition: Slight toning of the mat; heavy glare on the glass in every shot. No visible tears or losses.','','','mid to late 20th century','pastel on toned paper','','','','','','katalog B021; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7885, IMG_7886; No signature is visible within the exposed sheet; one may be hidden under the mat. Pastel versus soft chalk or oil pastel cannot be settled through the glass, and the medium reading is judged from the granular strokes.','no certificate present','IMG_7883',12.0,15.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["charcoal", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Beige", "Gray", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(204,'ilan-204','tablo','yayinda','Chinese Print Proud Lady with Child and Pine, Ling Fu-Yang, Signed, Framed','Ling Fu-Yang. A delicate Chinese-style composition: a slender lady in a pale robe with blue ribbon sashes carries a lacquer tray of tea things past a massive gnarled pine, while a small child in an orange jacket and grey trousers runs after her. Behind them a low railing and a thatched pavilion dissolve into misty grey wash, and the ground is suggested with soft dry-brush strokes and a few dark rocks. The palette is muted - dove grey, pale celadon, ivory and a single warm orange accent. A brush-written inscription and seal sit at the upper left of the image. Medium: colour reproduction print (collotype/photolithograph) after a watercolour. Signed below the image, lower right, reading "Ling Fu-Yang". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Proud; Ling Fu-Yang. Condition: Mat and sheet toned overall; a round red sale sticker is stuck to the glass at lower right; heavy reflections on the glass.','Ling Fu-Yang','Proud','mid 20th century','colour reproduction print (collotype/photolithograph) after a watercolour','','','','Proud; Ling Fu-Yang','','katalog B022; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7891, IMG_7892; The title ''Proud'' and the signature are both in a pencil-like script that appears printed rather than hand-written, which is why I read this as a reproduction rather than an original watercolour; the surname could also read ''Ping Fu-Yang''. The brushed characters and seal inside the image are not transcribable.','no certificate present','IMG_7887',11.75,15.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "print", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Beige", "Orange", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(205,'ilan-205','tablo','yayinda','Indian Painted Panel Krishna with Gopis and Cows, Unframed','A painted wooden panel in the Rajasthani manner: a haloed blue-skinned Krishna plays his flute on a lotus pedestal, flanked by four gopis in orange, green and yellow skirts beneath tall stylised palms, all set against a deep midnight ground stippled with white dots. Below, two white cows with red flower markings face a small cowherd, above a border of lotus blossoms on pale water. The whole image is enclosed by a broad orange border of black scrolling foliage. The surface is thickly and naively painted with hard bright colour and fine white dot outlining. Medium: gouache/tempera and gesso on wood panel. Condition: Paint losses and flaking along the top edge and corners, wear and rubbing to the orange border, edge chips to the wood, general grime consistent with age and use.','','','20th century','gouache/tempera and gesso on wood panel','','','','','','katalog B023; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7895, IMG_7896; No inscription or signature is present, so date and region rest on style only. Whether this is a repurposed cupboard or shutter panel or was made as a picture is not clear from the photographs, and the back was not shown.','no certificate present','IMG_7894',10.75,18.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": [], "medium": ["watercolour", "panel"], "style": ["asian", "folk"], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Orange", "Green", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(206,'ilan-206','tablo','yayinda','Hand-Coloured Etching of Rothenburg Roderbogen, Signed, Framed','A finely bitten etching of a medieval German street: a stone archway spans the cobbled way at centre, framed by tall gabled and half-timbered houses with shuttered windows, a stone fountain at right and a lone walking figure in the foreground. The plate is worked in dense fine line, then hand tinted with muted watercolour - terracotta roofs, dull teal shutters, warm stone and a soft grey pavement. The paper is cream and shows a clear plate mark within a deep charcoal mat. Medium: etching with hand colouring on paper. Signed in pencil below the plate, lower right. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Rothenburg, Roderbogen; Orig. Rad.. Condition: Paper lightly toned; heavy reflections and some haze on the glass; no visible foxing or tears.','','Rothenburg, Roderbogen','first half of the 20th century','etching with hand colouring on paper','','','','Rothenburg, Roderbogen; Orig. Rad.','','katalog B024; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7900, IMG_7901; The pencil signature at lower right is a compressed cursive I cannot read with confidence (it may end in -egen or -eger), so no artist name is entered. The second pencil line reads as ''Orig. Rad.'' - German shorthand for original etching - but the abbreviation is faint.','no certificate present','IMG_7897',14.0,18.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Beige", "Blue", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(207,'ilan-207','tablo','yayinda','Modern Watercolour Portrait Face in Blue, Signed, Framed','A large contemporary watercolour in which a mask-like face is drawn out of loose, flooded washes: the features are reduced to two arched brows, almond eyes, a straight nose line and full lips, while the hair sweeps back in broad sweeps of indigo, plum and olive. Salt and granulation effects speckle the darker passages with white, and the light falls as a cream diagonal across the cheek. The mood is cool and decorative, closer to graphic design than to portraiture, presented in a plum mat with a pink inner line and a black frame. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet. Condition: No visible damage; strong glare and reflections on the glass in all views.','','','1980s-1990s','watercolour on paper','','','','','','katalog B025; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7905, IMG_7906; The signature is a fluid cursive of about six letters that I cannot resolve even at full resolution, so no name is recorded. Whether this is an original watercolour or a very good giclee reproduction cannot be proven through the glass, though the granulation and salt texture read as original.','no certificate present','IMG_7902',16.75,21.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Purple", "Beige", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(208,'ilan-208','tablo','yayinda','Artist Proof Etching of a Crowded Market Street, Signed in the Plate, Framed','A lively etching, hand tinted with washes of ochre, rust and slate, showing a crowded street market beneath a stone gateway and tall blocky buildings. Dozens of small figures in long coats and caps stoop over trestle stalls or move away up the sunlit roadway, drawn in nervous scribbled line with the colour laid on loosely and allowed to run beyond the contours. The foreground stalls are worked in dense black hatching against the pale sanded roadway. A small monogram appears within the image at lower left. Medium: etching/drypoint with hand colouring on paper. Signed in pencil below the plate, lower right, with a date. Edition: Artist Proof. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Artist Proof. Condition: Mat toned and lightly foxed at the lower edge; strong glare on the glass; image itself appears clean.','','','third quarter of the 20th century','etching/drypoint with hand colouring on paper','Artist Proof','','','Artist Proof','','katalog B026; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7910, IMG_7911; The pencil signature is a rapid cursive followed by a four-digit year; it reads to me as something like ''Ira Moskowitz 1969'' and there is an ''IM''-style monogram inside the plate, but I could not confirm the letters, so no artist name is entered.','no certificate present','IMG_7907',19.0,15.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Orange", "Gray", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(209,'ilan-209','tablo','yayinda','Watercolour of Prague Castle and Charles Bridge, Framed','A bright, freely painted panorama of Prague: the arcaded Charles Bridge crosses the Vltava from the right, its piers reflected in choppy blue and grey water, while the Mala Strana roofs in terracotta lead up to the pale bulk of Prague Castle and the spires of St Vitus Cathedral. The sky is a wash of clean blue with dragged cloud, and the foliage is put in with quick dabs of sap green. Handling is loose and confident, with fine pen-like detail reserved for spires and arches. Medium: watercolour on paper. Condition: No visible issues; the picture is small within a very wide mat and the glass shows reflections.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','watercolour on paper','','','','','','katalog B027; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7916, IMG_7917; I could not find a legible signature; there are one or two faint marks in the lower left corner of the image that may be an initial. The work is small relative to its very large mat and frame.','no certificate present','IMG_7912',18.0,14.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Blue", "Orange", "Green", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(210,'ilan-210','belge','yayinda','GoodFellas Limited Edition Autographed Script Display, Numbered Edition, Unframed','A two-part memorabilia set: a black ring binder holding a reproduction of the GoodFellas screenplay whose white title page carries the film''s credits and a dense scatter of blue and black cast signatures, shown beside a black lacquered display plaque. The plaque mounts the familiar red-and-sepia GoodFellas one-sheet image of the three leads above a small painted clapperboard and a gilt nameplate. A numbered certificate of authenticity on clapperboard letterhead accompanies the set. Medium: printed paper script in a binder with reproduction signatures, plus a laminated poster print on a lacquered wood plaque. Signed across the script title page, reading "Mike Starr; Julie Garfield; Samuel L. Jackson; Tony Darrow; Michael Imperioli". Edition: 270/500, limited edition of 500 per display, reproduction signatures. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity for the Limited Edition Autographed Script Series, hand-numbered 270/500, stating plainly that the script is a faithful reproduction carrying reproduction signatures. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: GoodFellas; Written by Nicholas Pileggi & Martin Scorsese; Directed by Martin Scorsese; Produced by Irwin Winkler. Condition: Clean and complete; a retail tag hangs from the display, tape residue on the plaque below the poster, minor scuffing to the black lacquer.','','GoodFellas','late 1990s to 2000s','printed paper script in a binder with reproduction signatures, plus a laminated poster print on a lacquered wood plaque','270/500, limited edition of 500 per display, reproduction signatures','','','GoodFellas; Written by Nicholas Pileggi & Martin Scorsese; Directed by Martin Scorsese','','katalog B028; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7924, IMG_7925; The certificate states outright that the signatures are reproductions, not hand-signed. Of roughly fifteen signatures I could only read a handful with any confidence; the rest, including what may be Scorsese, De Niro, Liotta and Sorvino, are not legible enough to transcribe. The measurements are the least reliable in this batch.','Certificate of Authenticity for the Limited Edition Autographed Script Series, hand-numbered 270/500, stating plainly that the script is a faithful reproduction carrying reproduction signatures.','IMG_7920',15.0,12.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["unframed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Black", "White", "Red", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(211,'ilan-211','tablo','yayinda','Old Master Style Oil Genre Scene with Parrot, Framed','A small, darkly lit interior in the seventeenth-century Dutch manner: a young man in a russet-brown jacket leans over a table holding a small glass, while an elderly woman in a white linen coif and dark blue-green shawl sits at right, one hand raised. A scarlet and green parrot perches on the table edge between them, the brightest note in an otherwise deep brown and olive scheme, with a wine-red curtain behind. The paint is smooth and thinly worked with careful modelling of the faces and hands. It sits in a heavily ornamented gilt and gesso frame with a white-washed acanthus outer moulding. Medium: oil on panel or board. Condition: Numerous small white specks and spots across the paint surface, most likely flyspecking or spots of loss/mould in the varnish; frame with chips and losses to the gesso ornament, particularly the lower rail; darkened varnish overall.','','','19th to early 20th century, in a 17th century manner','oil on panel or board','','','','','','katalog B029; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7928, IMG_7929; No signature, label or inscription was found and the back of the panel was not photographed, so the date rests entirely on style and frame. Whether the support is wood panel, copper or prepared board cannot be determined from the images, and the white speckling could be damage or could be surface dirt.','no certificate present','IMG_7926',11.75,14.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "panel"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Green", "Red", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(212,'ilan-212','tablo','yayinda','Japanese Gold Ground Painting of Mount Fuji, Signed, Framed','A tall gold-ground painting in the Japanese decorative manner: a heavy pine leans out from a rocky knoll at left, its dark trunk and layered green needle clusters silhouetted against a burnished ochre sky, with the white cone of Mount Fuji rising beyond a pale lake. A small figure in a red-collared robe stands on the knoll, a boat and a tiny promontory sit far out on the water, and a spray of pink blossom crosses the upper right. Colour is limited to gold, ink black, moss green and touches of coral, and the ground carries a granular gilt sparkle. Medium: ink, colour and gold ground on paper or board. Signed lower right, a vertical column of characters with a red seal below. Condition: Extensive brown foxing and water staining across the lower half of the gold ground, with scattered spots throughout; light surface abrasion; frame sound with minor rubbing.','','','early to mid 20th century','ink, colour and gold ground on paper or board','','','','','','katalog B030; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7933, IMG_7934; The brushed signature column and red seal at lower right are not transcribable from these photographs, so no artist is recorded. Whether the gold is applied leaf or gold paint, and whether the support is paper laid to board, cannot be judged from the images. This piece is framed identically to B016 and the two were probably acquired together.','no certificate present','IMG_7931',15.75,25.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["ink", "panel", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Green", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(213,'ilan-213','tablo','yayinda','Grau Sala Colour Lithograph, En Visite, Numbered Edition, Framed','GRAU SALA. A crowded interior scene drawn in soft lithographic crayon: at left an older woman in an enormous black plumed hat and dark lace shawl leans over a checkered tablecloth, while at right a dark-haired girl in a frilled russet dress leans in from the other side. Between them stand a blue-and-white teapot, cups, a footed dish of fruit and a glass vase of pink roses, against a mottled patterned backdrop of ochre, rust and olive. The colour is dry and chalky with visible crayon grain and a wide bare paper margin, and the whole sheet is floated in a cream mount. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right, in pencil below the image, reading "Grau Sala". Edition: #186/220, pencil signed. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: pencil fraction at lower left of the sheet, indistinct in the photographs, with a small embossed blind stamp beneath it; "En Visite"  GRAU SALA (1911)  ORIGINAL LITHOGRAPH  #186/220  PENCIL SIGNED  (typed label taped to a brown-paper backing board; the label was photographed as IMG_7941, filed with the following listing); label photographed as IMG_7941, moved here from B032. Condition: Light overall toning of the sheet and mount; some spotting on the mount at lower left; scattered lamp reflections on the glass. No tears or losses visible.','GRAU SALA','En Visite','mid 20th century','colour lithograph on paper','#186/220, pencil signed','','','pencil fraction at lower left of the sheet, indistinct in the photographs, with a small embossed blind stamp beneath it; "En Visite"  GRAU SALA (1911)  ORIGINAL LITHOGRAPH  #186/220  PENCIL SIGNED  (typed label taped to a brown-paper backing board; the label was photographed as IMG_7941, filed with the following listing); label photographed as IMG_7941, moved here from B032','','katalog B031; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7938, IMG_7939; The typed label naming the work and edition was photographed as IMG_7941, which the frame grouping placed with the following listing (B032); it describes a pencil-signed lithograph of this type and almost certainly belongs to the backing board of this picture, but that link is inferred from content, not seen in one photograph. The pencil edition fraction on the sheet itself is too faint to read directly.','no certificate; identification comes from a typed label on the backing board','IMG_7935',27.5,21.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Black", "Pink", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(214,'ilan-214','tablo','yayinda','Half-Timbered Riverside Town With Cathedral, Framed','A busy 19th-century townscape: at left a masted barge lies at a quay while workmen roll logs ashore, and a pair of grey horses drags a timber sledge across the foreground. Behind them rise a slate-roofed stone tower and a tight row of half-timbered gabled houses with external stairs and balconies, with the twin openwork spires of a gothic cathedral in the pale distance. The palette is soft and aged: cream sky, ochre and umber timberwork, slate blues and a few red and blue accents on the small figures. Medium: colour print (chromolithograph/oleograph) on paper. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: "En Visite"  GRAU SALA (1911)  ORIGINAL LITHOGRAPH  #186/220  PENCIL SIGNED  (typed label on a brown-paper backing board, IMG_7941; it describes a pencil-signed lithograph and appears to belong to the preceding listing B031, not to this picture). Condition: Overall yellowing/darkening of the image, small dark flecks and surface soiling; gilding rubbed and chipped along the frame ornament, with losses at the corners.','','','late 19th to early 20th century','colour print (chromolithograph/oleograph) on paper','','','','"En Visite"  GRAU SALA (1911)  ORIGINAL LITHOGRAPH  #186/220  PENCIL SIGNED  (typed label on a brown-paper backing board, IMG_7941; it describes a pencil-signed lithograph and appears to belong to the preceding listing B031, not to this picture)','','katalog B032; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7945, IMG_7946; Whether this is a chromolithograph on paper or a small oil on board could not be settled from the photographs: no dot screen, plate mark or canvas weave is visible, and the glass reflects strongly. No signature was found. The typed label filed with this listing (IMG_7941) belongs to a different work.','no certificate present','IMG_7942',28.25,25.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "architecture", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Gold", "Brown", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(215,'ilan-215','tablo','yayinda','Cumulus Clouds East River, Henri Robert Giclee, Numbered Edition, Framed, 2002','Henri Robert. A golden, atmospheric harbour view: a broad sunlit sky of cumulus burns behind the masts of moored schooners, and the water catches a long band of light. Dark warehouse blocks frame the composition at left and right, a covered ferry shed sits at centre right with a lit lamp, and small dark figures, a hansom and barrels animate the wet quayside. The handling is loose and tonal, all amber, sepia and smoky violet-grey with a few red accents on the awnings. Medium: colour lithograph giclee on paper. Edition: 408/750; "The Golden Age of American Art by Fine Art Museum 408/750". Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity from Artwork Registry, registered 01-20-2003, serial 1.000.447, describing a color lithograph giclee, paper 19 x 13 in, edition 408/750. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 408/750 (pencil, lower right margin); embossed blind stamp at the far lower right of the sheet; Certificate of Authenticity / Artwork Registry , Title: Cumulus Clouds, East River / Author: Henri Robert / Country: USA / Registration date: 01-20-2003 / Serial number: 1.000.447 / Artwork: Painting / Medium: Color Lithograph Giclee / Paper Size: 19 x 13 inch / Year created: 2002 / Edition: The Golden Age of American Art by Fine Art Museum 408/750; Artwork Registry acknowledges that the above information including the image of the artwork were correct; therefore this certificate of registration including registration number 1.000.447 has been issued sealed & stamped , www.artworkregistry.com. Condition: No visible damage; the sheet is clean with full margins. Lamp reflections and a faint pink flare on the glass in the photographs.','Henri Robert','Cumulus Clouds, East River','created 2002, after an earlier American impressionist manner','colour lithograph giclee on paper','408/750; "The Golden Age of American Art by Fine Art Museum 408/750"','','','408/750 (pencil, lower right margin); embossed blind stamp at the far lower right of the sheet; Certificate of Authenticity / Artwork Registry , Title: Cumulus Clouds, East River / Author: Henri Robert / Country: USA / Registration date: 01-20-2003 / Serial number: 1.000.447 / Artwork: Painting / Medium: Color Lithograph Giclee / Paper Size: 19 x 13 inch / Year created: 2002 / Edition: The Golden Age of American Art by Fine Art Museum 408/750','','katalog B033; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7950, IMG_7951; The certificate calls the medium a ''Color Lithograph Giclee'', which is a marketing hybrid; from the photographs the sheet reads as an inkjet/offset reproduction rather than a hand-pulled stone lithograph. No hand signature was found on the sheet. ''Henri Robert'' is transcribed from the certificate only.','Certificate of Authenticity from Artwork Registry, registered 01-20-2003, serial 1.000.447, describing a color lithograph giclee, paper 19 x 13 in, edition 408/750.','IMG_7947',23.0,19.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Orange", "Gold", "Brown", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(216,'ilan-216','tablo','yayinda','Japanese Woodblock Print, Genji Series Courtier, 豊国画 (Toyokuni ga), Signed, Framed','豊国画 (Toyokuni ga). A full-length standing figure fills the sheet: a young nobleman in layered robes of indigo, russet and cream, patterned with roundels, chrysanthemum sprays and key-fret bands, his hair dressed in a black court style. He stands on a pale ground scattered with dark speckles, with a spray of plum blossom at lower left and a red rectangular title cartouche plus a small pictorial inset at upper right. Colours are limited to indigo, rust orange, olive and cream on toned, lightly foxed paper. Medium: colour woodblock print (nishiki-e) on Japanese paper. Signed cartouche at lower left of the print, reading "豊国画 (Toyokuni ga)". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 源氏後集餘情 (Genji goshu yojo) , red title cartouche, upper right; small white cartouche below the title with cursive kana, not legible in the photographs; 豊国画 (Toyokuni ga) , red toshidama-style signature cartouche, lower left; 横川彫竹 (Yokokawa Horitake) , black square block-carver''s seal beside the signature. Condition: Paper toned overall with scattered light foxing and a few brown stains at the right of the image; colours still strong. Viewed under glass with lamp reflections.','豊国画 (Toyokuni ga)','源氏後集餘情 (Genji goshu yojo)','mid 19th century, late Edo period','colour woodblock print (nishiki-e) on Japanese paper','','','','源氏後集餘情 (Genji goshu yojo) , red title cartouche, upper right; small white cartouche below the title with cursive kana, not legible in the photographs; 豊国画 (Toyokuni ga) , red toshidama-style signature cartouche, lower left','','katalog B034; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7959, IMG_7960; The signature cartouche reads ''Toyokuni ga'', the studio signature used by Utagawa Kunisada (Toyokuni III), but attribution beyond that transcription is not made here. The cursive chapter cartouche, the publisher''s mark and the date/censor seal could not be read. Whether this is a period impression or a later reprint cannot be judged from photographs.','no certificate present','IMG_7954',14.25,19.4,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Blue", "Orange", "Beige", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(217,'ilan-217','tablo','yayinda','Japanese Woodblock Print, Seated Beauty, Genji Series, 豊国画 (Toyokuni ga), Signed, Framed','豊国画 (Toyokuni ga). A kneeling woman turns her head to the left, an ornamental hairpin in her piled black coiffure. Her outer kimono is deep black scattered with orange and blue chrysanthemum roundels over an under-robe of banded geometric orange and blue, the fabric spreading in a broad triangle across the lower sheet. Small lacquer vessels sit on the ground at lower right, the field is flecked with dark speckles, and a red title cartouche with a blue chapter cartouche sits at upper right. Colours are black, rust orange, indigo and cream on toned paper. Medium: colour woodblock print (nishiki-e) on Japanese paper. Signed cartouche at centre left of the print, reading "豊国画 (Toyokuni ga)". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 源氏後集餘情 (Genji goshu yojo) , red title cartouche, upper right; blue chapter cartouche below the title, cursive characters, not legible in the photographs; 豊国画 (Toyokuni ga) , red toshidama-style signature cartouche, centre left; 横川彫竹 (Yokokawa Horitake) , block-carver''s seal beside the signature. Condition: Paper toned with light foxing and a few small stains; colours strong, black robe still dense. Glass reflects a lit sign in the room in one photograph.','豊国画 (Toyokuni ga)','源氏後集餘情 (Genji goshu yojo)','mid 19th century, late Edo period','colour woodblock print (nishiki-e) on Japanese paper','','','','源氏後集餘情 (Genji goshu yojo) , red title cartouche, upper right; blue chapter cartouche below the title, cursive characters, not legible in the photographs; 豊国画 (Toyokuni ga) , red toshidama-style signature cartouche, centre left','','katalog B035; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7965, IMG_7966; Same series and signature as B034, so the two are almost certainly a matched pair, but that is an inference. The chapter cartouche and the small seals at lower left could not be read; period versus later impression cannot be judged from photographs.','no certificate present','IMG_7961',14.25,19.4,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["asian"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Black", "Orange", "Blue", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(218,'ilan-218','tablo','yayinda','Winslow Homer Homeward-Bound Wood Engraving, Signed, Framed','WINSLOW HOMER. A black-and-white wood engraving of a crowded, canting deck: a bearded gentleman in a bowler walks arm in arm with a woman whose crinoline sweeps the planks, while behind them passengers cluster in bonnets and top hats, one man raising a spyglass. A great spar and a web of rigging cut diagonally across the upper half against a light cloudy sky, and at lower right two figures recline on a bench with a book. The image is built entirely of fine engraved line and cross-hatching, printed in dense black on cream wove paper. Medium: wood engraving on paper. Signed monogram cut into the block on the spar at upper right; the artist is also named in the printed caption, reading "W. F. (partially obscured by glare)". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: HOMEWARD-BOUND., [DRAWN BY WINSLOW HOMER.] , printed caption below the image; monogram in the block on the spar at upper right, reading approximately ''W. F.'', partly hidden by a lamp reflection. Condition: Paper lightly toned with faint scattered spotting; no tears or losses visible. Strong lamp reflections on the glass in every shot.','WINSLOW HOMER','HOMEWARD-BOUND.','third quarter of the 19th century','wood engraving on paper','','','','HOMEWARD-BOUND., [DRAWN BY WINSLOW HOMER.] , printed caption below the image; monogram in the block on the spar at upper right, reading approximately ''W. F.'', partly hidden by a lamp reflection','','katalog B036; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7971, IMG_7972; The caption format is that of a Harper''s Weekly full-page wood engraving after Homer, but no publication line or date is visible within the mat, so the periodical and year are not confirmed. The block monogram is partly hidden by glare, so its letters are uncertain, and whether this is an original 1860s impression or a later restrike cannot be judged.','no certificate present','IMG_7967',28.75,21.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Black", "Beige", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(219,'ilan-219','tablo','yayinda','Peter Max Better World Collage, Painted Mixed Media, MAX, PETER, Signed, Framed, 2002','MAX, PETER. A small rectangular collage of a stylised sunrise landscape - a red-orange sun over layered hills, a lone tree and a striped foreground - is mounted just left of centre on a broad ground brushed in loose bands of grass green, turquoise and cobalt. Over the ground the artist has run quick orange, red and white gestural squiggles and drips, with a scrubbed pale halo around the collaged panel. A cursive painted signature sits at lower centre, and the sheet is floated on a black mat inside a heavy gold frame. Medium: acrylic and paper collage (label: PAINTING WITH COLLAGE). Signed lower centre, painted in blue, reading "MAX". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: VOYAGER   03/10/2002   C999-0600; Burch, J. Gary; C/O AccuBanc Mortgage; 2670 Crain Highway, Suite #101. Condition: No visible damage to the surface; heavy lamp reflections on the glass. Frame shows minor rubbing.','MAX, PETER','Better World Collage, (Large)','late 20th century, sold 2002','acrylic and paper collage (label: PAINTING WITH COLLAGE)','','','VOYAGER (auction/sale label, 03/10/2002)','VOYAGER   03/10/2002   C999-0600; Burch, J. Gary; C/O AccuBanc Mortgage','','katalog B037; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7975, IMG_7976; The support under the mat is not visible; paper is assumed. The painted ''MAX'' signature is legible but stylised, and the auction label - not a certificate - is the only documentation. The label carries a private individual''s name, address and telephone numbers, which should not be republished in a listing.','no certificate; a printed sale/consignment label on the backing board records artist, title and medium','IMG_7973',26.5,28.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Green", "Blue", "Orange", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(220,'ilan-220','tablo','yayinda','G. Harvey The Warmth of Friendship Print, Numbered Edition, Framed, 1996','G. HARVEY. A warm-toned winter twilight: a sorrel and a chestnut horse stand saddled at a hitching rail while two men in long coats and hats talk beside a slender red gas pump with a lit globe. Behind them a clapboard store glows amber through its windows, smoke rises from a stone chimney, and a bare-branched tree and telegraph pole break the pale gold sky. Wheel ruts and hoof tracks cut through the blue-shadowed snow in the foreground; the palette is amber, ochre and warm brown against cool violet-blue snow shadow. Medium: offset lithograph reproduction on paper. Signed lower right of the image; a printed signature with a hand-applied signature and copyright symbol below it, reading "G. Harvey". Edition: Year issued 1996; edition size 1500, artist proofs 250; foil seal on the certificate reads 17/250 A/P. Accompanied by a certificate: Publisher''s Certificate of Authenticity for a limited-edition reproduction, 1996, edition 1500 plus 250 artist proofs, with a gold seal numbered 17/250 A/P. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: THE WARMTH OF FRIENDSHIP / G. HARVEY , engraved brass plaque on the frame; G. Harvey (twice at lower right of the image, one within the printed image and one applied below it, with a small copyright symbol); Certificate of Authenticity , Statement of Authenticity: This Certificate of Authenticity by Somerset House Publishing, Inc., the publisher, documents the year of issue and the total edition size of a reproduction on paper and/or MasterGraphics On Canvas of original art. The artist''s signature verifies that each reproduction has been personally inspected and approved by the artist. This Certificate of Authenticity further ensures that, upon the publisher''s final sale of the proclaimed quantity of reproductions, the edition will be closed. Somerset House Publishing, Inc., reserves the right to use this image or portions thereof on other dissimilar products.; Specifications , TITLE: THE WARMTH OF FRIENDSHIP / ARTIST: G. HARVEY / YEAR ISSUED: 1996 / EDITION SIZE: 1500 / ARTIST PROOFS: 250. Condition: No visible damage; surface clean under glass with lamp reflections. Frame ornament intact with light rubbing.','G. HARVEY','THE WARMTH OF FRIENDSHIP','issued 1996','offset lithograph reproduction on paper','Year issued 1996; edition size 1500, artist proofs 250; foil seal on the certificate reads 17/250 A/P','','','THE WARMTH OF FRIENDSHIP / G. HARVEY , engraved brass plaque on the frame; G. Harvey (twice at lower right of the image, one within the printed image and one applied below it, with a small copyright symbol); Certificate of Authenticity , Statement of Authenticity: This Certificate of Authenticity by Somerset House Publishing, Inc., the publisher, documents the year of issue and the total edition size of a reproduction on paper and/or MasterGraphics On Canvas of original art. The artist''s signature verifies that each reproduction has been personally inspected and approved by the artist. This Certificate of Authenticity further ensures that, upon the publisher''s final sale of the proclaimed quantity of reproductions, the edition will be closed. Somerset House Publishing, Inc., reserves the right to use this image or portions thereof on other dissimilar products.','','katalog B038; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7982, IMG_7983; The certificate describes ''a reproduction on paper and/or MasterGraphics On Canvas'', so paper versus canvas is not settled by the document; from the photographs the surface reads as paper under a mat. The lower of the two ''G. Harvey'' signatures appears hand-applied, but printed and hand signatures cannot be separated with certainty through glass. The A/P number on the seal (17/250) is small and slightly blurred.','Publisher''s Certificate of Authenticity for a limited-edition reproduction, 1996, edition 1500 plus 250 artist proofs, with a gold seal numbered 17/250 A/P.','IMG_7978',38.25,33.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Gold", "Brown", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(221,'ilan-221','tablo','yayinda','Girl With White Horse, Gold Leaf Artwork, Signed, Framed','A deckle-edged sheet with the look of a weathered fresco: a small white horse stands in profile at left, and at right a dark-eyed young figure in a curly headdress and a heavily encrusted, gold-flecked robe leans on a ledge. The ground is terracotta and rust, cracked and rubbed like old plaster, with faint architectural shapes behind. Squares of applied gold leaf catch the light at the lower right of the image and along the mount, and the whole is set on a black mat with gold fillets in a deep ornate gilt frame. Medium: mixed media with gold leaf on deckle-edged paper (possibly a hand-embellished print). Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil/ink beside a gold leaf square. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: handwritten inscription at lower left of the sheet and a signature at lower right, both cursive and not legible in the photographs; the signature ends in a form close to that on listing B040; WHITE HOUSE ART GALLERY / ORIGINAL LITHOGRAPH • OIL PAINTING / FINE POSTERS & CUSTOM FRAMING / ONE HOUR CUSTOM FRAMING / 741 15TH STREET, N.W. • WASHINGTON, DC 20005 / TEL: 202-393-6752 FAX: 202-393-6753 , gallery label. Condition: No visible damage to the sheet; the glass has pronounced lamp reflections and a scuff-like bloom at upper left in one shot. Frame intact.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','mixed media with gold leaf on deckle-edged paper (possibly a hand-embellished print)','','','WHITE HOUSE ART GALLERY, 741 15TH STREET, N.W., WASHINGTON, DC 20005','handwritten inscription at lower left of the sheet and a signature at lower right, both cursive and not legible in the photographs; the signature ends in a form close to that on listing B040; WHITE HOUSE ART GALLERY / ORIGINAL LITHOGRAPH • OIL PAINTING / FINE POSTERS & CUSTOM FRAMING / ONE HOUR CUSTOM FRAMING / 741 15TH STREET, N.W. • WASHINGTON, DC 20005 / TEL: 202-393-6752 FAX: 202-393-6753 , gallery label','','katalog B039; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7990, IMG_7991; The medium is the main open question: the sheet has a deckle edge and a canvas-like texture in close-up with real gold leaf applied, so it could be a hand-embellished serigraph/lithograph or an original mixed-media work. The gallery label lists both lithographs and oil paintings and does not identify this piece. Neither the inscription at lower left nor the signature could be read; the same hand appears to have signed B040.','no certificate; only a framer''s/gallery label','IMG_7986',40.25,34.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Orange", "Gold", "Beige", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(222,'ilan-222','tablo','yayinda','Large Fresco-Style Panel With Gold Leaf, Signed, Framed','A long horizontal composition worked to look like a wall painting recovered from a ruin: chalky white columns, capitals and drapery-like forms emerge from a scumbled ground of grey-green, ochre and dusty rose, with passages scraped back and rubbed to bare texture. Broad white sweeps run across the middle like a plaster course, and touches of applied gold leaf glint along the right edge. The paint is dry and thickly worked, with visible brush ridges, and the panel is set behind a broad gold-leafed border inside a plain gilt frame. Medium: oil/mixed media with gold leaf on canvas or canvas-textured panel. Signed lower right of the panel, handwritten in dark ink/pencil. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: handwritten line across the lower edge of the panel, partly legible: it begins with a word reading approximately ''Dubrost?ego'', followed by ''P.A.'' and ending in a signature that reads approximately ''Bede? Mihal''; the individual letters are not certain; faint painted pseudo-lettering within the composition at upper right, decorative and not readable. Condition: Surface intentionally distressed, so wear is hard to separate from the technique; no obvious damage, tears or flaking seen. Some dust along the lower frame edge.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','oil/mixed media with gold leaf on canvas or canvas-textured panel','','','','handwritten line across the lower edge of the panel, partly legible: it begins with a word reading approximately ''Dubrost?ego'', followed by ''P.A.'' and ending in a signature that reads approximately ''Bede? Mihal''; the individual letters are not certain; faint painted pseudo-lettering within the composition at upper right, decorative and not readable','','katalog B040; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_7998, IMG_7999; Signature and inscription are handwritten in a cursive that resists reading; the ending closely matches the signature on B039, so the two are probably by the same hand, but no name is asserted. Whether the surface is glazed is not certain - the highlights in the close-ups could be glass or varnish - and whether it is a painting or a heavily embellished print could not be settled, though the visible brush ridges favour a painting.','no certificate present','IMG_7994',48.0,28.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas", "panel"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["White", "Gray", "Gold", "Pink"]}'::jsonb),
(223,'ilan-223','tablo','yayinda','Corbelle Cap d''Antipe Colour Lithograph, Signed, Numbered Edition, Framed','CORBELLE. A light, quickly drawn coastal scene: spiky palm fronds and a bare-branched tree are sketched in fine black ink over washes of pale blue, lemon yellow and sea green. Behind them a promenade runs past a colonnaded building and a row of masts and flags, with tiny figures in red, yellow and blue under parasols, and a low headland closing the bay. The paper is left largely open, the wash thin and drippy, giving a sunny, calligraphic feel in the manner of Dufy. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right within the image, in pencil, reading "Corbelle". Edition: 275/350, hand signed (certificate states edition 350). Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity naming the work ''Cap d''Antipe'' by/after Corbelle, colour lithograph, edition 350, hand signed, registration no. 1552. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Corbelle (pencil signature, lower right); 275/350 (pencil, beneath the signature); Patrician Galleries, Inc. Certificate of Authenticity , TITLE: CAP D''ANTIPE / BY / AFTER: CORBELLE / MEDIA: COLOR LITHOGRAPH / EDITION: 350 / OTHER: HAND SIGNED / We hereby certify that to our best knowledge and belief this work of art is as represented above. / REGISTRATION NO. 1552. Condition: No visible damage; sheet clean, mat clean. Strong lamp reflections on the glass.','CORBELLE','CAP D''ANTIPE','second half of the 20th century','colour lithograph on paper','275/350, hand signed (certificate states edition 350)','','Patrician Galleries, Inc.','Corbelle (pencil signature, lower right); 275/350 (pencil, beneath the signature); Patrician Galleries, Inc. Certificate of Authenticity , TITLE: CAP D''ANTIPE / BY / AFTER: CORBELLE / MEDIA: COLOR LITHOGRAPH / EDITION: 350 / OTHER: HAND SIGNED / We hereby certify that to our best knowledge and belief this work of art is as represented above. / REGISTRATION NO. 1552','','katalog B041; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8004, IMG_8005; The certificate spells the title ''CAP D''ANTIPE'' (as transcribed); the place is normally spelled Cap d''Antibes. The certificate says ''BY / AFTER: CORBELLE'', which leaves open whether the artist drew the stone himself, and the pencil signature is legible but the artist''s full name is not given anywhere.','Certificate of Authenticity naming the work ''Cap d''Antipe'' by/after Corbelle, colour lithograph, edition 350, hand signed, registration no. 1552.','IMG_8001',36.25,29.75,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Yellow", "Green", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(224,'ilan-224','tablo','yayinda','Barbara A. Wood Signed Print, Woman With Roses, Numbered Edition, Framed','BARBARA A. WOOD. A softly brushed figure study: a woman with an upswept blue and green coiffure bows her head, her cheek flushed coral, towards a cluster of deep magenta and teal roses at lower right. The forms are built from loose, sweeping strokes of violet, plum, cornflower blue and sea green, with the pale oval of her face and a sliver of white blouse as the lightest notes. The whole is set in wide double cream mats with a thin gold fillet inside a pale lacquered frame. Medium: offset lithograph on paper, pencil signed and numbered. Signed lower right margin, in pencil, reading "barbara A. wood". Edition: 871/975 (first digit indistinct; denominator 975). Inscribed on the reverse or mount: barbara A. wood (pencil signature, lower right margin); pencil edition number at lower left margin reading approximately ''871/975'' (the first digit is indistinct and could be a 4); WINDSOR ART , MANUFACTURERS • CREATORS DECORATIVE WALL ACCESSORIES / ITEM NUMBER: C 1158 695 DESCRIPTION: WILD FLOWER / WINDSOR ART PRODUCTS INCORPORATED / PICO RIVERA, CA 90660 , label on the backing board; TO PROPERLY HANG YOUR BEAUTIFUL NEW ''WINDSOR MIRRORS/PICTURE'' ... THE CORRECT WAY / THE UNSAFE WAY , printed hanging instruction sheet on the backing board, with ''5269'' written on it in ink. Condition: No visible damage; sheet and mats clean. Backing paper is intact with its original labels. Lamp reflections on the glass.','BARBARA A. WOOD','WILD FLOWER','late 20th century','offset lithograph on paper, pencil signed and numbered','871/975 (first digit indistinct; denominator 975)','','Mal Camino, Multiple Images, Esplanade, 150 Worth Ave., Palm Beach, Florida 33480','barbara A. wood (pencil signature, lower right margin); pencil edition number at lower left margin reading approximately ''871/975'' (the first digit is indistinct and could be a 4); WINDSOR ART , MANUFACTURERS • CREATORS DECORATIVE WALL ACCESSORIES / ITEM NUMBER: C 1158 695 DESCRIPTION: WILD FLOWER / WINDSOR ART PRODUCTS INCORPORATED / PICO RIVERA, CA 90660 , label on the backing board','','katalog B042; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8011, IMG_8012; The title ''Wild Flower'' comes from the framer''s item label rather than from the artist, so it may be Windsor Art''s product name rather than the artist''s title. The first digit of the edition number is not legible. The print process (offset lithograph versus serigraph) cannot be confirmed through glass.','no certificate; a printed artist biography sheet and a Windsor Art Products label are attached to the backing board','IMG_8007',20.0,26.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Purple", "Blue", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(225,'ilan-225','tablo','yayinda','Stakes Race, Watercolour-Style Horse Racing Print, Signed, Framed','Five racehorses come straight at the viewer out of a smoky blue-grey haze, their jockeys in scarlet, emerald, gold and blue silks with goggles down. The horses'' heads and chests are painted with wet, bleeding washes of chestnut, black and umber, while the track below dissolves into loose ochre and rust streaks with spattered clods of dirt. A pale crowd is only suggested behind. The printed title sits in the white margin under the image, and the sheet is double matted in cream and burgundy. Medium: offset lithograph reproduction of a watercolour, on paper. Signed lower left of centre, within the image. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: STAKES RACE , printed in capitals in the lower margin of the sheet; cursive signature across the lower part of the image, not legible in the photographs. Condition: No visible damage; sheet clean with full printed margin. Heavy lamp reflections on the glass in every shot.','','STAKES RACE','late 20th century','offset lithograph reproduction of a watercolour, on paper','','','','STAKES RACE , printed in capitals in the lower margin of the sheet; cursive signature across the lower part of the image, not legible in the photographs','','katalog B043; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8018, IMG_8019; The typeset title in the margin indicates a published reproduction rather than an original watercolour, but no publisher line, edition number or plate mark is visible inside the mat. The signature within the image could not be read and it is unclear whether it is printed or hand-applied.','no certificate present','IMG_8015',32.5,27.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "animal"], "medium": ["watercolour", "print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Brown", "Gray", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(226,'ilan-226','tablo','yayinda','Naive Paris Street Scene, Signed Colour Lithograph, Numbered Edition, Framed','A pale, delicately drawn city street: a green-fronted café and a yellow awninged shop run across the middle distance, their windows outlined in fine pen, with blue shutters and hanging lanterns. Bare, wiry trees rise the full height of the sheet, and tiny doll-like figures in ochre, pink, blue and green walk the pavement, one on a bicycle, one with a small dog, another seated on a green bench. Everything is washed in soft grey-green and straw yellow with a chalky, almost misty surface. The sheet has wide white margins, pencil numbering at lower left and a signature at lower right. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right margin, in pencil. Edition: 245/250 (digits indistinct). Inscribed on the reverse or mount: pencil signature at lower right, a single cursive word beginning ''Cha'' and ending in a small hook; not confidently legible; pencil edition number at lower left reading approximately ''245/250'' (the middle digit is indistinct); a shop sign lettered within the image begins ''CHEZ ...'', the rest not legible. Condition: No visible damage; sheet and mount clean. Lamp reflections and a slight bloom on the glass.','','','second half of the 20th century','colour lithograph on paper','245/250 (digits indistinct)','','','pencil signature at lower right, a single cursive word beginning ''Cha'' and ending in a small hook; not confidently legible; pencil edition number at lower left reading approximately ''245/250'' (the middle digit is indistinct); a shop sign lettered within the image begins ''CHEZ ...'', the rest not legible','','katalog B044; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8024, IMG_8025; The pencil signature is a compact cursive word that I could not resolve into a name, so no artist is given; the edition fraction is also partly indistinct. Whether the sheet is a colour lithograph or a fine serigraph cannot be confirmed through glass.','no certificate present','IMG_8020',23.25,23.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Gray", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(227,'ilan-227','tablo','yayinda','Still Life With Stoneware Jug and Fruit, Segal, Signed, Framed','Segal. A warm-keyed still life: a bulbous red-brown glazed jug with a looped handle stands on a pale stone slab, flanked by a shallow wooden bowl of dark purple plums, a cluster of white eggs and two ripe oranges. Behind it the ground blazes in strokes of chrome yellow, gold and ochre suggesting sunlit grass, and the foreground drops into cool green and olive. The paint is applied thickly with a loaded brush, ridges catching the light on the jug''s shoulder and along the ledge, and the canvas weave shows through the thinner passages. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, painted in dark brown, reading "Segal". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Segal (painted signature, lower right). Condition: Paint layer looks sound with no visible craquelure or losses; the linen slip is lightly soiled and the carved frame is rubbed and chipped along the outer edges with old dark finish worn back to bare wood at the corners.','Segal','','mid to late 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','Segal (painted signature, lower right)','','katalog B045; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8029, IMG_8030; The signature reads ''Segal'' but could be ''Sagal''; no first name or date is present and no label or stamp was photographed on the back, so the artist cannot be identified further.','no certificate present','IMG_8027',26.25,32.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Gold", "Brown", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(228,'ilan-228','tablo','yayinda','Portrait of a Seated Young Man after Modigliani, Signed, Framed','An elongated, almond-eyed figure in the manner of Modigliani, seated with hands folded, wearing a dark jacket over a vertically striped shirt. The background is a flat ochre wall broken by faint incised lines. The palette is warm and restrained: mustard, brick red, black and cream. Presented in a wide off-white painted moulding with a thin gilt inner lip. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed upper right of the canvas, reading "modigliani". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: faint printed canvas-maker stamp on the reverse, illegible; retail price tag on the frame reading $439. Condition: surface appears sound; some glare in the photographs.','','','20th century','oil on canvas','','','','faint printed canvas-maker stamp on the reverse, illegible; retail price tag on the frame reading $439','','katalog B046; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8035, IMG_8036; The signature reads modigliani but this is almost certainly an after / homage rather than an autograph Modigliani. Treat the name as a signature transcription only.','none seen','IMG_8032',24.0,30.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "Red", "Black", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(229,'ilan-229','tablo','yayinda','In the Clearing, Figures by a River, A. Moreau, Signed, Framed','A. Moreau. A small, jewel-like river scene painted with a loaded brush. A group of figures in cream, wine and grey stand on the near bank, parasol raised, while a boatman in tall boots poles a dark punt through the shallows. Hills recede into a warm amber sky. The impasto is heavy in the foliage and water, giving the panel a glittering surface. Set in a deep gilt composition frame with a beaded inner edge. Medium: oil on panel. Signed lower right, in red, reading "A. MOREAU". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Alton''s Picture Store, 110 W. Lexington St, Balto, Md.; A. Moreau #449; 1843-1906; In the Clearing. Condition: no visible damage; heavy varnish gloss.','A. Moreau','In the Clearing','late 19th century','oil on panel','','','Alton''s Picture Store, 110 W. Lexington St, Baltimore, Md.','Alton''s Picture Store, 110 W. Lexington St, Balto, Md.; A. Moreau #449; 1843-1906','','katalog B047; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8041, IMG_8042; The dealer label gives the dates 1843-1906, which match Adrien Moreau. The signature reads A. MOREAU. Attribution beyond the transcription is not established here.','handwritten dealer label only, in a plastic sleeve with a wax seal','IMG_8037',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "panel"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Orange", "Green", "Beige", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(230,'ilan-230','tablo','yayinda','Amish Farmstead and Buggy with Reflection, Signed, Framed','A long horizontal pen and watercolour study in a restrained palette of slate blue, warm brown and rust. A shingle-roofed farmhouse, a white picket fence and a flowering tree sit behind a chestnut horse pulling a black buggy. Two pale blue discs behind the buildings read as sky or sun, and the whole scene is doubled in a soft reflection along the lower edge. Titled and signed in pencil on the sheet below the image. Medium: pen, ink and watercolour on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: pencil title along the lower edge of the sheet, not legible at this resolution. Condition: clean sheet, no visible foxing.','','','late 20th century','pen, ink and watercolour on paper','','','','pencil title along the lower edge of the sheet, not legible at this resolution','','katalog B048; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8046, IMG_8047; Both the signature and the pencil title need a closer photograph to transcribe. Height not measured.','none seen','IMG_8044',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture", "animal"], "medium": ["watercolour", "ink", "paper"], "style": ["folk"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Orange", "Brown", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(231,'ilan-231','tablo','yayinda','Woman with Headdress and White Horse, Gold Leaf, Signed, Framed','A richly worked mixed-media print in bronze, umber and gold. A woman in a jewelled headdress looks out to the left, her face lit warm against a dark interior in which a pale horse stands. Broad vertical bands of applied gold leaf frame the image at both sides, embossed with a small cartouche. The effect is deliberately Byzantine, part icon and part fashion plate. Double-matted in tan under a dark wood frame. Medium: serigraph or giclee with applied gold leaf. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: pencil signature and what appears to be an edition note along the lower margin, not legible at this resolution. Condition: no visible damage; heavy glare from the glazing.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','serigraph or giclee with applied gold leaf','','','','pencil signature and what appears to be an edition note along the lower margin, not legible at this resolution','','katalog B049; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8052, IMG_8053; Artist signature not legible. This is very likely a signed limited edition; the edition number needs a closer photograph.','none seen','IMG_8048',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gold", "Brown", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(232,'ilan-232','tablo','yayinda','Flamenco Dancers, Espana, Signed, Framed','A loose, energetic figure study on a sepia-washed ground. The dancer''s skirt is a single sweep of cadmium red flecked with black spots; her partner is a hard black silhouette with a flash of orange at the collar. Calligraphic scribbles crowd the background like applause. Titled and signed along the lower edge. Presented in a plain black float frame. Medium: acrylic and ink on canvas. Signed lower right, in black, reading "Flamenco - ESPANA". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Flamenco - ESPANA inscribed beside the signature. Condition: no visible damage.','','Flamenco - Espana','late 20th century','acrylic and ink on canvas','','','','Flamenco - ESPANA inscribed beside the signature','','katalog B050; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8056, IMG_8057; The artist''s name beside the title is not legible at this resolution.','none seen','IMG_8054',24.0,30.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["ink", "canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Red", "Black", "Brown", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(233,'ilan-233','tablo','yayinda','Bamboo and Blossom, Abstract Botanical, Signed, Framed','A brisk botanical abstraction in olive, acid green and warm ochre. Dark verticals of bamboo cut the sheet while paler stems and small white blossoms scatter across a sand-coloured wash. The handling is fast and confident, with drybrush scratches over flat washes. Signed along the lower right. Set in a slim gilt frame with a deep olive mat. Medium: watercolour and gouache on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: cursive signature at the lower right, not legible at this resolution. Condition: no visible damage.','','','mid to late 20th century','watercolour and gouache on paper','','','','cursive signature at the lower right, not legible at this resolution','','katalog B051; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8061, IMG_8062; Signature not legible; height not measured.','none seen','IMG_8058',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Gold", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(234,'ilan-234','tablo','yayinda','Desert Barn Beneath Blue Mountains, William Perry Schimmel, Signed, Framed','William Perry Schimmel. A confident plein-air watercolour. A long grey barn with a bright tin roof sits low against violet-blue mountains, its shadowed timbers rendered in single loaded strokes. The foreground is a band of ochre grass with scattered brushwood, and the sky is left almost bare. Signed in the image at the lower right. Presented in a plain white painted frame with a cream mat. Medium: watercolour on paper. Signed lower right, within the image, reading "WILLIAM PERRY SCHIMMEL". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: pencil dedication on the backing board reading in part To Deb and Bob ... Christmas. Condition: clean sheet; slight cockling under the mat.','William Perry Schimmel','','mid to late 20th century','watercolour on paper','','','','pencil dedication on the backing board reading in part To Deb and Bob ... Christmas','','katalog B052; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8068, IMG_8069; Height not measured. The pencil dedication is only partly legible.','none seen','IMG_8064',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "architecture"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Gold", "Gray", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(235,'ilan-235','tablo','yayinda','Montmartre Cafe Terrace, Paris, Charles Blondin, Signed, Framed','Charles Blondin. A bright Parisian street scene worked in short broken strokes. Plane trees screen the domes of Sacre-Coeur and a slim bell tower; below, a scarlet awning shelters a row of cafe tables crowded with figures in dark coats. The palette is fresh green and cream with the awning as the single hot accent. Signed at the lower right. Framed in black with a gilt inner lip. Medium: gouache or mixed media on paper. Signed lower right, within the image, reading "Charles Blondin". Condition: paper toned overall; no visible tears.','Charles Blondin','','mid 20th century','gouache or mixed media on paper','','','','','','katalog B053; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8073, IMG_8074; Signature read as Charles Blondin; a closer photograph would confirm the surname.','none seen','IMG_8070',25.0,32.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Beige", "Red", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(236,'ilan-236','tablo','yayinda','Venice, Soft Focus Canal Study, Signed, Framed','A dreamlike canal view in which the palazzi, boats and bridge blur into vertical smears of violet, pewter and pale blue, as though seen through rain on glass. Only the moored hulls hold their edges. Titled Venice in pencil at the lower left of the mat and signed at the lower right. Wide white mat in a gold moulding. Medium: photographic print, soft focus. Signed lower right of the mount, in pencil. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Venice, in pencil at the lower left of the mount. Condition: no visible damage.','','Venice','late 20th to early 21st century','photographic print, soft focus','','','','Venice, in pencil at the lower left of the mount','','katalog B054; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8079, IMG_8080; The signature is a short cursive mark and cannot be transcribed at this resolution.','none seen','IMG_8075',24.0,26.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "architecture"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Purple", "Gray", "Blue", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(237,'ilan-237','tablo','yayinda','Winter Street with Tram, Limited Edition, Numbered Edition, Framed','A wintry townscape in umber and pewter, the snow laid in thick creamy strokes across the roadway. A church spire rises at the left and a dark tram advances under a smoking sky. Figures in black hurry along the pavements. Numbered 202/750 and signed in pencil in the lower margin. Ornate gilt frame with a tan mat. Medium: limited edition reproduction print on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil. Edition: 202/750. Accompanied by a certificate: a Certificate of Authenticity headed Artwork Registry accompanies the piece; the body text is not legible in this photograph. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 202/750 in pencil at the lower right of the sheet. Condition: no visible damage.','','','reproduction of an earlier composition','limited edition reproduction print on paper','202/750','','','202/750 in pencil at the lower right of the sheet','','katalog B055; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8084, IMG_8085; The certificate text needs a straight-on photograph; artist and title are unread.','a Certificate of Authenticity headed Artwork Registry accompanies the piece; the body text is not legible in this photograph','IMG_8081',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "18th-and-earlier", "color": ["Brown", "Gray", "Beige", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(238,'ilan-238','tablo','yayinda','Blue Nude, Abstracted Figure, Signed, Framed','A bold figure abstraction in ultramarine, cobalt and cadmium yellow against a cream ground. The body reads as a sequence of curved black outlines and flat colour fields; a yellow diagonal cuts across the torso and a red note sits at the hip. Confident, poster-like handling with visible brush drag. Signed at the upper left. Plain black frame. Medium: acrylic on canvas. Signed upper left. Condition: no visible damage.','','','late 20th century','acrylic on canvas','','','','','','katalog B056; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8089, IMG_8090, IMG_8091; Signature is a short monogram and not legible.','none seen','IMG_8087',24.0,36.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "nude", "seascape", "landscape"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Yellow", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(239,'ilan-239','tablo','yayinda','Tall Ship at a Busy Quayside, Signed, Framed','A detailed maritime scene in clear watercolour tones. A three-masted ship flying the American flag lies alongside a wharf stacked with barrels, sacks and crates, while dockworkers, carts and a steam tug fill the middle ground. A second vessel and a smoking stack close the horizon. Signed in pencil in the lower margin. Dark moulding with a gilt lip and a white mat. Medium: offset or giclee reproduction on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, in pencil. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: pencil signature and a date at the lower right of the sheet, not legible at this resolution. Condition: no visible damage.','','','late 20th century','offset or giclee reproduction on paper','','','','pencil signature and a date at the lower right of the sheet, not legible at this resolution','','katalog B057; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8095, IMG_8096; Signature and any edition note need a closer photograph.','none seen','IMG_8092',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Blue", "Brown"]}'::jsonb),
(240,'ilan-240','obje','yayinda','Rococo Garden Scene Tapestry in Gilt Frame, Framed','A finely woven tapestry panel after a rococo garden painting. A gentleman in a plumed hat plays to two seated women in silk gowns; a parasol lies across the foreground and a domed pavilion closes the view through the trees. Rose, cream, sage and dusty blue dominate. Mounted in a heavy carved and gilded frame with a rose-red slip. Medium: woven tapestry panel. Condition: weave sound; slight gilt loss at the frame corners.','','','20th century after an 18th century composition','woven tapestry panel','','','','','','katalog B058; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8099, IMG_8100; No weaver mark or edge label visible; height not measured.','none seen','IMG_8097',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["panel", "textile"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Pink", "Beige", "Green", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(241,'ilan-241','tablo','yayinda','Blissful Moments, Itzchak Tarkay Serigraph, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 2007','Itzchak Tarkay. A light, decorative cafe scene. Four women in patterned dress sit around a small round table set with fruit and a vase of blossom; a striped throw and a potted plant fill the right of the sheet. Line is quick and calligraphic, colour is laid in flat washes of rose, saffron and pale blue. Signed in the plate at the lower right. Wide cream mat in a slim dark frame. Medium: serigraph in colour on wove paper. Signed lower right, in the plate, reading "Tarkay". Edition: signed in the plate. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity for Tarkay, Itzchak, Blissful Moments, 2007, serigraph in colour on wove paper, image 16 1/4 x 19 1/2 in, registration no 226984.W647. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: PARK WEST Certificate of Authenticity; Registration No 226984.W647; Tarkay, Itzchak; Blissful Moments. Condition: sheet clean; the certificate and its card mount are worn at the edges.','Itzchak Tarkay','Blissful Moments','2007','serigraph in colour on wove paper','signed in the plate','','Park West Gallery, Delaware','PARK WEST Certificate of Authenticity; Registration No 226984.W647; Tarkay, Itzchak','','katalog B059; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8104, IMG_8105','Certificate of Authenticity for Tarkay, Itzchak, Blissful Moments, 2007, serigraph in colour on wove paper, image 16 1/4 x 19 1/2 in, registration no 226984.W647','IMG_8101',32.0,29.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Pink", "Gold", "Blue", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(242,'ilan-242','tablo','yayinda','Wide Abstract in Black, Ochre and Bone, Signed, Framed','A long horizontal abstraction built from broad black gestures dragged across warm ochre, bone and pale grey. A scratched grid shows through at the lower left and a thin red note flickers near the top. The surface is worked with palette knife and brush and reads as weathered plaster. Signed in black at the lower left. Broad silver-gilt frame. Medium: acrylic and mixed media on canvas. Signed lower left. Condition: no visible damage.','','','late 20th to early 21st century','acrylic and mixed media on canvas','','','','','','katalog B060; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8111, IMG_8112; The signature is a gestural mark and cannot be transcribed.','none seen','IMG_8108',56.0,26.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["canvas"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Black", "Gold", "Beige", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(243,'ilan-243','tablo','yayinda','Half-Timbered Village Canal Oil Painting, Signed, Framed','A still green-grey waterway recedes between steep-roofed half-timbered houses, board fences and clipped shrubs toward a bulb-domed church spire and pale blue hills. The palette is chalky and muted: cream and ochre plaster, terracotta and moss-green roofs, soft blue sky, with the buildings mirrored in the water. Paint is thin and small-brushed with light impasto in the roof tiles and foliage; a fine craquelure runs across the whole surface. A small brown dog stands on the near bank at lower left. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right, painted in red over the water, reading "C.FAU?ET". Condition: Fine age craquelure over the entire canvas, most visible in the sky and water; surface dirt and slight dulling; frame shows minor knocks. No tears, losses or restoration visible in the photographs.','','','mid 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog B061; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8116, IMG_8117; The red signature at lower right is only partly legible - it looks like a ''C.'' initial followed by FAU and ending in ET (e.g. FAUCHET / FAUQUET), but I cannot read it reliably, so no name is asserted. Both tape shots crop off the zero end, so the dimensions are inferred from the reading at the far frame edge.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8114',24.25,30.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "landscape", "architecture", "animal"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Gold", "Beige", "Orange"]}'::jsonb),
(244,'ilan-244','tablo','yayinda','Barbara A. Wood Woman in Black Hat, Signed, Framed','Barbara A. Wood. A young blonde woman is shown in three-quarter view, her face lowered under a wide black hat trimmed with a red band and a small red flower, a scarlet scarf at her throat and a heavy dark wrap pulled around her shoulders. The handling imitates chalk and pastel, with dense scribbled hatching in charcoal grey, mauve and pale blue behind her and thick dark scumbling in the coat. The palette is smoky and cool apart from the two hot reds. Signed in the image in red and again in pencil on the paper margin below. Medium: colour lithograph on paper, pencil signed and numbered. Signed in the image lower right in red, and in pencil on the margin below the image, reading "Barbara A. Wood". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Barbara A. Wood. Condition: Mat and sheet look clean with faint scattered specks on the mat; heavy glare from the glazing in every shot. No tears or waviness visible.','Barbara A. Wood','','late 20th century','colour lithograph on paper, pencil signed and numbered','','','','Barbara A. Wood','','katalog B062; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8122, IMG_8123, IMG_8124; A pencil edition fraction is written at the lower left of the margin (IMG_8121) but it is too soft and out of focus to read - it may be a three digit number over a larger edition. Whether the printing process is offset lithography or true stone lithography cannot be settled from these photographs.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8118',31.25,35.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "charcoal", "paper"], "style": ["old-masters", "contemporary"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gray", "Beige", "Red", "Purple"]}'::jsonb),
(245,'ilan-245','tablo','yayinda','Christian Title Serigraph Red Windows, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 1988','Christian Title. A sunlit garden built from short broken strokes of pistachio green, cadmium yellow, cobalt and white, with a young tree at the centre, a bank of white flowering shrubs in the foreground and a red-roofed house glimpsed through the foliage at right. The sky is a stippled blue and the ground a warm ochre path. The surface is flat printed colour with clean unbroken edges and a wide white paper margin, hand-numbered and signed in pencil below the image. Medium: colour serigraph (screenprint) on paper. Signed pencil, lower right of the paper margin, reading "Christian Title". Edition: XXXIX/C (pencil on the print); certificate states edition of C of which this is the XXXIV. Accompanied by a certificate: Certifies an Original Serigraph by Christian Title titled ''Red Windows'', pulled in a limited edition of C, this copy numbered XXXIV, authorised signature ''Sally K...'' and date issued 5/4/88. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: XXXIX/C; Certificate of Authenticity; Original Serigraph; Pulled in a limited edition of C of which this is the XXXIV. Condition: Bright fresh colour, clean margins, no foxing or toning visible. The certificate is creased and lightly soiled at the edges. Glazing glare in all shots.','Christian Title','Red Windows','1988','colour serigraph (screenprint) on paper','XXXIX/C (pencil on the print); certificate states edition of C of which this is the XXXIV','','Fine Arts Gallery, Inc., Ardmore, PA','XXXIX/C; Certificate of Authenticity; Original Serigraph','','katalog B063; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8129, IMG_8130; The pencil number on the print reads XXXIX/C (39/100) while the certificate is filled in as XXXIV (34) - the two do not agree. The artist''s name is taken from the pencil signature and the certificate; both read as ''Christian Title'' but the handwriting is loose. The authorised signature on the certificate (''Sally'' plus surname) is not legible.','Certifies an Original Serigraph by Christian Title titled ''Red Windows'', pulled in a limited edition of C, this copy numbered XXXIV, authorised signature ''Sally K...'' and date issued 5/4/88.','IMG_8125',35.25,32.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Yellow", "Blue", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(246,'ilan-246','tablo','yayinda','Lady at the Piano Interior Oil Painting, Signed, Framed','A small, highly finished interior: a woman in a long white dress sprigged with green and red flowers and a red bodice sits at a dark upright piano beside a blue upholstered chair, in a room papered in golden ochre with a framed miniature on the wall and an open door to a cool grey passage at left. Light falls from the left across a polished plank floor, thrown back as soft reflections. Handling is fine and tight, with small dragged strokes in the dress and floor and thicker touches of white in the highlights. Medium: oil on canvas. Signed lower right of the canvas, dark paint over the floor. Condition: Paint film looks stable with only slight surface grime; the gilt frame has small rubs and a few chips to the composition ornament. No visible craquelure or losses in the image area.','','','late 19th to early 20th century','oil on canvas','','','','','','katalog B064; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8135, IMG_8136; The signature at lower right is a short cursive of roughly six letters (something like ''V...gan''), too small and abraded to transcribe, so no name is given. Support could be a fine canvas or a canvas-textured board; the frame prevents a definite reading.','no certificate or label photographed','IMG_8132',16.0,19.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": ["old-masters"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Gold", "White", "Brown", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(247,'ilan-247','tablo','yayinda','Gerard Bachelet La Chrysalide Lithograph Nude, Numbered Edition, Framed','Gerard Bachelet. A pale, softly modelled nude kneels folded into an enormous green leaf that wraps around her like a cocoon, her blonde hair swept up and a filmy white veil drifting across her body. Around her lie cowrie shells, small stones and a banded snail on bands of sand-yellow and green, with a hazy pale seascape above. The colour is delicate and chalky - leaf green, flesh, sand, faint blue - printed on heavy white paper with a wide margin, titled and numbered in pencil below. Medium: colour lithograph on wove paper. Signed pencil, lower right of the margin, reading "Gerard Bachelet". Edition: 19/50. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 19/50; "La Chrysalide"; Gerard Bachelet. Condition: The mat is noticeably browned and water-stained, especially along the top and left, and the backing paper is toned; the print itself looks clean. Frame rubbed at the corners.','Gerard Bachelet','La Chrysalide','third quarter 20th century','colour lithograph on wove paper','19/50','','','19/50; "La Chrysalide"; Gerard Bachelet','','katalog B065; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8141, IMG_8142; The edition numerator reads as 19 but could be 13; the denominator 50 is clear. The pencil title and signature are legible, but whether the print is a stone lithograph or a fine offset lithograph cannot be determined behind glass. A brass nameplate reading GERARD BACHELET appears in IMG_8143, which is filed under B066 but whose frame and mat match this listing.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8138',24.75,32.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Black", "Beige", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(248,'ilan-248','tablo','yayinda','Large Abstract Mixed Media on Deckled Paper, Signed, Framed','A tall abstract sheet built from dragged and scraped layers - rust, brick and ochre washes at the base rising into smoky grey, with a black vertical shaft down the right of centre and a torn white streak of dry white pigment beside it. Small flecks of orange and a heavy black blot punctuate the surface, and the paint sits with visible grain and scratched-back texture. The sheet has a soft deckled edge and floats on a white mount, signed in white at the lower right. Medium: mixed media (acrylic and gouache with scraped and dry-brushed passages) on heavy deckle-edged paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, written in white over the dark ground. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: GERARD BACHELET. Condition: Sheet appears clean and unfaded with its deckle intact; glazing glare and reflections throughout. Frame in good order with light dust.','','','late 20th century','mixed media (acrylic and gouache with scraped and dry-brushed passages) on heavy deckle-edged paper','','','','GERARD BACHELET','','katalog B066; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8147, IMG_8148; The white signature at lower right is a fast scrawl and cannot be read, so no artist is named. IMG_8143 - grouped with this listing - shows a brass plaque reading GERARD BACHELET, but the wood frame and browned mat in that photograph match B065, not this black frame, so the plaque probably does not belong to this work. Whether the piece is a unique painting or a heavily worked print could not be resolved through the glass.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8144',33.0,42.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "landscape"], "medium": ["watercolour", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Gold", "Gray", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(249,'ilan-249','tablo','yayinda','Three Hand-Coloured Asia Costume Plates, Framed','Three separate hand-coloured plates, each individually mounted in a slim black frame and grouped behind a taupe mount in one large lacquered surround. Left and right show standing male dancers in plumed helmets and blue cloaks over red and white striped skirts, holding long staffs; the centre plate shows a seated ascetic with a great fan-shaped ochre headdress on a patterned mat. Colouring is light and transparent - carmine, ochre, indigo and flesh - over fine engraved outlines on cream paper, with engraved captions in italic script and the word ASIA beneath two of them. Medium: hand-coloured engraving or lithograph on paper. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: ASIA; ASIA; Bailarina. Condition: Paper is lightly toned with a warm cream tone overall; no tears or foxing visible at this resolution. Two small bright reflections on the glass; the orange frame has minor surface marks.','','','mid 19th century','hand-coloured engraving or lithograph on paper','','','','ASIA; ASIA; Bailarina','','katalog B067; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8151, IMG_8152; The engraved italic captions under the left and centre plates are too faint to transcribe with confidence; only ''ASIA'' and the right-hand ''Bailarina'' are certain. The plate captions are Spanish, which suggests a Spanish-language costume encyclopaedia, but no publisher, plate number or series title is visible. Engraving versus lithography cannot be settled behind glass.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8149',27.5,16.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "19th", "color": ["Beige", "Gold", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(250,'ilan-250','tablo','yayinda','Etching Figure with Spear and Scribbled Beasts, Signed, Framed','A sparse etching on cream paper: a standing figure drawn in tight coils of scribbled line, its head a dark scribbled cap, holds a red-orange spear toward a small striped animal, while a second figure in a red skirt with a yellow bow stands behind. A thin drawn horizon runs across the sheet and the rest is left bare. The only colour is the red of the spear and skirt and a touch of yellow; the impression sits inside a clean plate mark on heavy paper, pencil numbered at the lower left and signed at the lower right. Medium: etching with drypoint and hand colouring on paper. Signed pencil, lower right of the margin. Condition: Paper carries a light overall warm toning and a few faint handling marks; the plate mark is crisp. Strong reflections on the glazing. Frame sound.','','','third quarter 20th century','etching with drypoint and hand colouring on paper','','','','','','katalog B068; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8157, IMG_8158; Both the pencil signature (a single sweeping monogram) and the edition fraction at lower left are illegible - the fraction looks like a three digit number over 150 but cannot be read. Artist unidentified. This sheet is clearly a companion to B069 (same hand, same frame and size).','no certificate photographed','IMG_8154',30.0,35.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Black", "Red", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(251,'ilan-251','tablo','yayinda','Etching Spearman and Seated Thinker, Signed, Framed','An etching in soft brown aquatint tones: at left a stiff, jointed figure like an artist''s lay figure raises one arm in a red sleeve and holds a long yellow spear, while at right a pale seated nude in a folded paper hat rests his chin on his hand on a terracotta block. A narrow band of pale blue sea crosses behind them and a scribbled coil-drawn creature stands on the far shore. Warm sepia ground, cream margins, pencil signed at the lower right. Medium: etching with aquatint and hand colouring on paper. Signed pencil, lower right of the margin. Condition: Light overall toning of the sheet and mount; image clean and strong. Heavy glazing reflections. No tears or foxing visible.','','','third quarter 20th century','etching with aquatint and hand colouring on paper','','','','','','katalog B069; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8163, IMG_8164; The pencil signature is the same illegible sweeping monogram as B068, so no artist is named, and no edition number is visible on this sheet (it may be hidden by the mount). Orientation is mixed: the plate is landscape but the frame and mount are portrait; I recorded the frame''s orientation in the dimensions.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8159',30.0,35.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Brown", "Beige", "Orange", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(252,'ilan-252','tablo','yayinda','Art Deco Zodiac Serigraph Virgo, Signed in the Plate, Framed','A stylised deco design on cream paper: a black night window sprinkled with white stars stands behind a potted plant, a slanting blue plane carries the ultramarine Virgo glyph in flowing line, and a cluster of blue and cobalt spheres drawn with fine white radiating hatching sits at the lower left with a single spotted red-brown accent. Two thin outline hands gesture at either side. Flat, opaque screenprinted colour with crisp edges and generous margins; titled, numbered and signed in pencil below. Medium: colour serigraph (screenprint) on paper. Signed pencil, lower right of the margin. Edition: LXXX/XC. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: LXXX/XC; Virgo. Condition: Sheet and mount are lightly cream-toned; colours strong. No foxing or damage visible, only glazing glare.','','Virgo','late 20th century','colour serigraph (screenprint) on paper','LXXX/XC','','','LXXX/XC; Virgo','','katalog B070; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8168, IMG_8169; The pencil signature at lower right is a rapid flourish and cannot be transcribed, so no artist is asserted; the deco zodiac subject and roman-numeral edition are characteristic of the Erte zodiac serigraphs, but nothing in the photographs confirms that. The edition reads LXXX/XC (80 of 90) - the numerator is slightly smudged.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8165',28.25,35.0,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["art-nouveau"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Black", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(253,'ilan-253','tablo','yayinda','Marcel Mouly Guitare Jaune Colour Lithograph, Mouly, Marcel, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 1991','Mouly, Marcel. A boldly coloured cubist still life: a yellow guitar and a second, ghostly white one are fractured across a grid of flat planes in lemon yellow, vermilion, cobalt, emerald and violet, with a dark bottle, a stemmed bowl of fruit and a chequered table edge locked into the design. Colour is laid in broad opaque blocks with visible lithographic grain and embossed relief in the lighter passages, on heavy Arches paper with a soft edge. Signed within the image at the lower right. Medium: colour lithograph with embossing on Arches paper. Signed lower right within the image, reading "M. Mouly". Edition: from the edition of 300 (30 artist''s proofs also exist), per the label; the pencil number itself was not photographed. Accompanied by a certificate: Printed inventory label taped to the backing board giving artist, title, date 1991, size 32 1/4 x 23 3/4 in, medium, edition of 300 and printer Aloys Litho, Paris. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 191)  56457; Mouly, Marcel; Guitare Jaune; (Yellow Guitar). Condition: Colours fresh and unfaded; sheet clean. Some reflection and a dust film on the glossy black frame. No visible foxing, ripple or damage.','Mouly, Marcel','Guitare Jaune (Yellow Guitar)','1991','colour lithograph with embossing on Arches paper','from the edition of 300 (30 artist''s proofs also exist), per the label; the pencil number itself was not photographed','','Park West Gallery, Southfield, Michigan','191)  56457; Mouly, Marcel; Guitare Jaune','','katalog B071; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8171, IMG_8172, IMG_8173, IMG_8174; The label is the source for medium, edition and size; the pencil signature and edition number on the sheet itself were not photographed, only the signature inside the image. The label''s 32 1/4 x 23 3/4 in is stated height x width but which of the two is meant is not spelled out.','Printed inventory label taped to the backing board giving artist, title, date 1991, size 32 1/4 x 23 3/4 in, medium, edition of 300 and printer Aloys Litho, Paris.','IMG_8170',38.0,46.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Red", "Blue", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(254,'ilan-254','tablo','yayinda','Cubist Seated Woman After Picasso, Marina Collection, Numbered Edition, Framed, 1953','A seated woman is broken into flat angular planes - a white lattice-patterned chair back and skirt, a deep green bodice, grey and black shadow shapes - with her head turned in profile-and-frontal at once, a single staring eye and long black hair. The design is drawn with thick brushy black outlines and washed grey and olive fills, dated in the plate at the upper right ''19.3.53.''. Printed on heavy white deckle-edged paper with a wide margin, an embossed blindstamp and a pencil inscription below. Medium: colour lithograph on deckle-edged paper (limited edition after a Picasso work). Edition: 105/500. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: collection Marina Picasso; 105/500; 19.3.53.; ...work by Pablo Picasso  A lim... (circular embossed blindstamp, partly legible). Condition: Sheet clean and bright with an intact deckle; mat and frame in good order. Heavy reflections in every photograph.','','','late 20th century edition after a 1953 composition','colour lithograph on deckle-edged paper (limited edition after a Picasso work)','105/500','','','collection Marina Picasso; 105/500; 19.3.53.','','katalog B072; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8181, IMG_8182; The pencil inscription reads ''collection Marina Picasso'' and the blindstamp includes ''...work by Pablo Picasso'' and ''A lim...'' but is only partly readable, so I have not asserted an artist attribution. There is no autograph signature - the date 19.3.53. is part of the printed image. Whether the process is lithography or a photomechanical reproduction cannot be settled through the glass.','no paper certificate photographed; authentication is the embossed blindstamp on the sheet','IMG_8176',33.0,42.25,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "White", "Green", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(255,'ilan-255','tablo','yayinda','Salvador Dali Etching Lady Dulcinea Don Quixote, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 1974','Salvador Dali. A slight, dreamlike figure fills the sheet: a pale woman with long yellow hair looks out from beneath a towering black scribbled headdress, her shoulders draped in a pink veil that falls to either side like a tent over a thin blue horizon and mauve hills. Her bodice is drawn in fine looping pen-like line with a scatter of dark curls at the neckline. Colours are soft washes - shell pink, straw yellow, pale blue - over crisp etched outline on white paper, signed in pencil at the lower right below a clean plate mark. Medium: etching with hand colouring on paper. Signed pencil, lower right of the margin. Edition: certificate states pencil signed and numbered; the number itself is not visible in the photographs. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity for Salvador Dali, ''Histoire de Don Quixote de la Mancha Suite #941 Lady Dulchea'', original etching, 1974, pencil signed and numbered, size given as 34" x 37". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Certificate of Authenticity; Salvador Dali; Entitled: "Histoire de Don Quixote de la Mancha Suite #941 Lady Dulchea"; Description: Original Etching. Condition: Print clean and bright with a crisp plate mark; the linen mat is slightly cream-toned. Ornate gilt frame has small chips and rubs to the composition ornament. Glazing glare in all views.','Salvador Dali','Histoire de Don Quixote de la Mancha Suite #941 Lady Dulchea','1974','etching with hand colouring on paper','certificate states pencil signed and numbered; the number itself is not visible in the photographs','','St. Petersburg Gallery','Certificate of Authenticity; Salvador Dali; Entitled: "Histoire de Don Quixote de la Mancha Suite #941 Lady Dulchea"','','katalog B073; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8186, IMG_8187; The attribution and title come entirely from the 2003 gallery certificate, not from anything readable on the sheet; the pencil signature at lower right is an illegible flourish and no edition number is visible. The certificate''s size of 34 x 37 in disagrees with my tape readings of the frame (about 35 x 40 1/2 in). Certificates of this kind are dealer-issued and are not independent authentication.','Certificate of Authenticity for Salvador Dali, ''Histoire de Don Quixote de la Mancha Suite #941 Lady Dulchea'', original etching, 1974, pencil signed and numbered, size given as 34" x 37".','IMG_8183',35.0,40.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Black", "Yellow", "White", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(256,'ilan-256','tablo','yayinda','Joan Miro Ceramiques Photomechanical Graphic, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 1993','Joan Miro. A wide horizontal composition scattered with Miro''s black stick figures, spiky stars and eyed biomorphs, punctuated by discs and crescents of scarlet, cobalt, emerald and cadmium yellow and hazed with fine spray-spattered pink and orange. The white ground is left largely open, with a thin black keyline border, and a facsimile signature appears in the lower right of the sheet. Colour is flat and even with no plate mark or ink relief. Medium: photomechanical colour graphic (offset reproduction) on paper, facsimile signature. Signed lower right of the sheet, facsimile. Edition: 500 piece edition numbered with facsimile signature. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate for ''Ceramiques'' by Joan Miro, photomechanical graphic published 1993 in an edition of 500 numbered impressions with facsimile signature, plate destroyed; the edition number field is left blank. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: CERTIFICATE OF AUTHENTICITY; CERAMIQUES - FACSIMILIE SIGNATURE; By JOAN MIRO; Medium PHOTOMECHANICAL GRAPHIC. Condition: Sheet clean and bright, mat crisp; certificate is stored in a yellowed plastic sleeve behind the frame. Frame gilding lightly rubbed. Glazing glare throughout.','Joan Miro','Ceramiques','published 1993','photomechanical colour graphic (offset reproduction) on paper, facsimile signature','500 piece edition numbered with facsimile signature','','','CERTIFICATE OF AUTHENTICITY; CERAMIQUES - FACSIMILIE SIGNATURE; By JOAN MIRO','','katalog B074; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8192, IMG_8193; This is expressly a reproduction, not a hand-pulled print: the certificate calls it a photomechanical graphic with a facsimile signature, so the signature at lower right is printed, not autograph. The edition number field on the certificate is blank, so this copy''s number is unknown, and the shipping label''s size fields were never filled in.','Certificate for ''Ceramiques'' by Joan Miro, photomechanical graphic published 1993 in an edition of 500 numbered impressions with facsimile signature, plate destroyed; the edition number field is left blank.','IMG_8189',44.0,36.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["White", "Black", "Red", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(257,'ilan-257','tablo','yayinda','LeRoy Neiman Brooklyn Bridge Cityscape Print, Signed, Framed, 1974','LeRoy Neiman. A long panoramic cityscape: the dark blue sweep of the Brooklyn Bridge cuts diagonally across a skyline slashed in cadmium yellow, scarlet, magenta and violet, its towers rising into a turquoise sky. Below, the river is worked in broad palette-knife strokes of purple, teal and yellow with small white sailboats and tugs and their broken reflections. The handling is loose and impasto-like in the original, reproduced flat with dense expressive strokes; signed and dated in the image and again in a large signature on the margin below. Medium: colour offset lithograph on paper. Signed in the image lower right, and a large signature on the paper margin below the image, reading "LeRoy Neiman 74". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: LeRoy Neiman 74; LeRoy Neiman; Copyright(c) LeRoy Neiman, Inc.. Condition: Colours strong, paper clean, mat crisp. Reflections from the glazing across the image. Frame in good condition with light rubbing.','LeRoy Neiman','','image dated 1974, print later','colour offset lithograph on paper','','','','LeRoy Neiman 74; LeRoy Neiman; Copyright(c) LeRoy Neiman, Inc.','','katalog B075; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8199, IMG_8200, IMG_8201; The printed line ''Copyright(c) LeRoy Neiman, Inc.'' next to the large margin signature means this is a published edition; I cannot tell from the photograph whether that margin signature is hand-signed in ink or printed with the sheet, and no edition number is visible.','no certificate photographed','IMG_8197',43.0,28.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["abstract", "seascape", "architecture", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Red", "Purple", "Blue"]}'::jsonb),
(258,'ilan-258','tablo','yayinda','Picasso Bust of a Woman in Hat Print, Signed, Framed','Picasso. A bold graphic head-and-shoulders portrait built from flat, poster-like colour areas with heavy black contour drawing, in the manner of Picasso''s late linocuts. The face is divided vertically, one half yellow and one half red, framed by dark green hair and topped by a wide ochre-yellow hat with red accents. Below, a red and white patterned bodice band closes the composition. The sheet has a generous white margin and is set behind a cream mat with a fine dark line, in a gold moulded frame under glass. Medium: colour offset lithograph after a linocut. Signed lower right, in the sheet margin, reading "Picasso". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Picasso (pencil, lower right margin). Condition: Heavy glass glare across the upper sheet in the photograph; no tears, foxing or losses visible.','Picasso','','late 20th to early 21st century reproduction of a 1960s image','colour offset lithograph after a linocut','','','','Picasso (pencil, lower right margin)','','katalog B076; olcu kareleri galeride degil: yok; A pencil fraction is present in the lower left margin but is too small to read at 900px; the denominator may be 100 or 200. The frames of listing B077 (signature, edition number 49/200 and certificate) appear to show this same image and may in fact be the same physical object photographed a second time. The ''Picasso'' signature is in graphite-grey and may be a facsimile rather than an autograph.','No certificate photographed with this listing; the certificate in listing B077 relates to the same or an identical image.','IMG_8202',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["portrait", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Red", "Yellow", "Green", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(259,'ilan-259','tablo','yayinda','Picasso Woman in Hat Lithograph with Certificate, Pablo Ruiz Picasso, Numbered Edition, Framed, 2010','Pablo Ruiz Picasso. Detail photographs of the lower edge of a large colour print: flat bands of red, green, black and white with heavy black outlines over a warm white wove sheet. Under magnification the colour areas break into a regular halftone dot screen, indicating a photomechanical offset process rather than a hand-pulled relief print. A pencil edition fraction sits in the lower left margin and a pencil signature in the lower right. The accompanying Spanish-issued certificate carries a photograph of the artist. Medium: offset lithograph on Arches paper. Signed lower right margin, reading "Picasso". Edition: 49/200. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate headed ''Pablo Ruiz Picasso'' reading: Author: Pablo Ruiz Picasso / Technique: litografia grafic printed off set / Dimensions: 50 cm x 70 cm / Type of paper: Arches France / License: Foundation Pablo Picasso / Stamps: Pablo Picasso Museum / Lithography in question and '' authentic / Number exemplary: 49/200 / Madrid 03/03/2010 / Grafiart. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 49/200 (pencil, lower left margin); Picasso (pencil, lower right margin). Condition: Paper clean and bright in the details; certificate lightly creased. No foxing or tears visible.','Pablo Ruiz Picasso','','2010 issue after a 1960s image','offset lithograph on Arches paper','49/200','','','49/200 (pencil, lower left margin); Picasso (pencil, lower right margin)','','katalog B077; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8204, IMG_8206, IMG_8207; This listing contains no full view of the work; the detail and certificate photographs appear to belong to the framed print shown in listing B076, and the two codes may describe one object. The pencil ''Picasso'' is grey graphite in tone and may be a printed facsimile. The certificate wording is transcribed exactly as printed, including its non-standard English.','Certificate headed ''Pablo Ruiz Picasso'' reading: Author: Pablo Ruiz Picasso / Technique: litografia grafic printed off set / Dimensions: 50 cm x 70 cm / Type of paper: Arches France / License: Foundation Pablo Picasso / Stamps: Pablo Picasso Museum / Lithography in question and '' authentic / Number exemplary: 49/200 / Madrid 03/03/2010 / Grafiart.','IMG_8205',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "figurative", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "Green", "Black", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(260,'ilan-260','tablo','yayinda','Sunlit Beach Scene with Parasol and Bathers, Signed, Framed','A large, luminous seaside scene handled in loose impressionist strokes: a broad wedge of pale sand runs from the lower left to a bright turquoise sea, with a white and red striped parasol anchoring the left half and figures in white and cream summer dress grouped beneath it. Children in straw hats wade in the shallows at the right, their reflections broken across wet sand. The palette is dominated by cream, sand-ochre, aqua and touches of coral. Presented on a wide cream mat in a substantial gold frame under glass. Medium: colour lithograph or giclee reproduction on paper. Signed lower right of the image. Condition: Strong glass glare and reflections in every photograph; a faint pencil inscription sits in the lower left margin. No tears, foxing or surface damage visible.','','','late 20th century reproduction of an early 20th century image','colour lithograph or giclee reproduction on paper','','','','','','katalog B078; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8213, IMG_8214; The cursive signature in the lower right of the image cannot be resolved at the available resolution and is not transcribed. A pencil inscription (probably an edition fraction) in the lower left margin is likewise illegible. Whether this is a lithograph, a giclee or an original oil on canvas could not be settled from the photographs because of the glazing glare; the presence of glass and a mat argues for a work on paper.','No certificate photographed.','IMG_8210',52.7,38.3,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["impressionist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Gold", "White"]}'::jsonb),
(261,'ilan-261','tablo','yayinda','Native American Hoop Dancer Watercolour, LeRoy Colfax, Signed, Framed','LeRoy Colfax. A single standing figure fills the sheet, shown mid-step with feathered bustle and beaded regalia, arms extended through a set of dance hoops. The handling is transparent watercolour and gouache over fine pen drawing, with warm earth reds, turquoise, ochre and black against an unpainted paper ground that gives the figure a floating, isolated presence. The paper is set close to a plain quarter-sawn oak frame under glass. Medium: watercolour and ink on paper. Signed lower centre right of the sheet, reading "LeRoy Colfax ''95". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: LeRoy Colfax ''95 (signed in ink, the initial letter drawn as a feather). Condition: Glass glare across the upper sheet; no foxing, tears or fading visible.','LeRoy Colfax','','late 20th century, dated in the signature','watercolour and ink on paper','','','','LeRoy Colfax ''95 (signed in ink, the initial letter drawn as a feather)','','katalog B079; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8218, IMG_8219; This photo group contains two different artworks: IMG_8216 (the hoop dancer catalogued here) and IMG_8215, a separate landscape-format oil or acrylic of two stags in a wooded stream, in its own plain oak frame and unglazed. The record describes the hoop dancer because the signature detail and both tape readings belong to it. The signature''s date could be read as ''95 or ''75, and the surname reading ''Colfax'' is legible but not certain.','No certificate photographed.','IMG_8216',20.4,27.7,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["figurative"], "medium": ["watercolour", "ink", "paper"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Orange", "Blue", "Gold", "Black"]}'::jsonb),
(262,'ilan-262','tablo','yayinda','Two Stags in a Wooded Stream, Framed','A landscape-format painting of two stags in a shallow stream running through open woodland, in a plain oak frame and unglazed. Medium: oil or acrylic on canvas. Condition: only one photograph available.','','','','oil or acrylic on canvas','','','','','','katalog B079B; olcu kareleri galeride degil: yok; Photographed once only, inside another listing''s sequence. Needs its own photographs, measurements and a closer look.','','IMG_8215',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape"], "medium": ["oil", "canvas"], "style": [], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "", "color": ["Brown", "Gold", "Green"]}'::jsonb),
(263,'ilan-263','tablo','yayinda','Picasso Nature Morte au Verre Lithograph, Pablo Picasso, Numbered Edition, Framed','Pablo Picasso. A very small, spare image floats at the centre of a large sheet: a pale grey-blue glass or jug drawn in a few decisive contours stands beside a shallow dish holding a yellow and orange fruit, all resting on a black and ochre scumbled table plane. The surrounding paper is left almost entirely bare, and the work is presented on a double French-style mat ruled with fine ink lines, in a slim black frame with a gold inner edge. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Edition: 407/500. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity stating ''This certified museum quality Limited-Edition lithograph/serigraph is individually numbered and hand-signed by the Artist''; Original by: Pablo Picasso (Artist); Title: Nature Morte au Verre; Edition: 407/500; Medium: Lithograph; signed by an officer, President. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 407/500 (pencil, lower left of the sheet); Collection Marina Picasso (pencil, lower right of the sheet). Condition: Certificate is water-stained and toned along the lower edge. The print itself shows no foxing or tears; some glass glare in the photographs.','Pablo Picasso','Nature Morte au Verre','late 20th century posthumous edition','colour lithograph on paper','407/500','','Gallery Art Network, Inc. (logo reads ''Gallery Network'')','407/500 (pencil, lower left of the sheet); Collection Marina Picasso (pencil, lower right of the sheet)','','katalog B080; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8224, IMG_8225; No artist signature is visible on the sheet; the only pencil annotations are the edition fraction and the ''Collection Marina Picasso'' inscription, which contradicts the certificate''s claim that the piece is hand-signed. The cursive ''Collection Marina Picasso'' reading is confident but the writing is small and could contain a further word.','Certificate of Authenticity stating ''This certified museum quality Limited-Edition lithograph/serigraph is individually numbered and hand-signed by the Artist''; Original by: Pablo Picasso (Artist); Title: Nature Morte au Verre; Edition: 407/500; Medium: Lithograph; signed by an officer, President.','IMG_8220',35.9,30.2,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["still-life"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Gray", "Black", "Gold"]}'::jsonb),
(264,'ilan-264','tablo','yayinda','Pressed Leaf and Bamboo Paper Collage, Signed, Framed','A quiet, decorative collage built from torn and cut handmade papers: slender vertical canes in honey, khaki and charcoal rise across a mottled ivory ground, while a bank of broad, veined leaves in sage green and grey-blue spreads across the lower half. The surface is matte and fibrous, with visible deckled paper edges and pressed plant material, and the tonal range stays deliberately soft. It is floated on a pale sage mat with a gold slip, in a moulded gilt frame under glass. Medium: collage of handmade papers and pressed leaves on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, reading "Caso". Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Caso (signed in pencil, lower right; could also read Casa, Casas or Casey). Condition: Glass glare across the upper left; the paper is lightly rippled, which is normal for handmade stock. No tears or staining visible.','','','late 20th century','collage of handmade papers and pressed leaves on paper','','','','Caso (signed in pencil, lower right; could also read Casa, Casas or Casey)','','katalog B081; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8230, IMG_8231; The four-letter pencil signature is small and flourished; ''Caso'' is the best reading but ''Casa'', ''Casas'' and ''Casey'' cannot be excluded, so no artist name is asserted. Whether the leaves are genuine pressed plant material or printed papers cannot be settled behind glass.','No certificate photographed.','IMG_8227',42.4,32.5,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": [], "medium": ["paper"], "style": ["asian", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Green", "Beige", "Gold", "Gray"]}'::jsonb),
(265,'ilan-265','tablo','yayinda','Marc Chagall Blue Bouquet Lithograph, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 2001','Marc Chagall. A dense bouquet of pink, scarlet, orange and lemon blossom erupts from a dark green vase against a smoky grey-blue ground, with a yellow sun burning at the upper right and a pair of embracing lovers dissolved into the flowers at the left. Below the vase a strip of village rooftops and a bird are drawn in washy blues and reds. The lithograph has wide white margins and sits on a cream mat within a black velvet-effect liner and a heavily beaded gilt frame. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right margin, reading "Marc Chagall". Edition: number 112 in an edition of 500. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity from Donnelly Galleries, Bank of America Building, 2000 E. Lamar Blvd, Suite 600, Arlington, Texas 76006, certifying that the lithograph entitled ''Blue Bouquet'' by Marc Chagall is a limited edition lithograph and is number 112 in an edition of 500; dated Oct 10, 2001. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Marc Chagall (signed lower right margin). Condition: The backing paper carries a ''FRAMED BY RUTH'' stamp. Heavy glass glare in the photographs; no foxing, tears or fading visible on the sheet.','Marc Chagall','Blue Bouquet','certified 2001','colour lithograph on paper','number 112 in an edition of 500','','Donnelly Galleries','Marc Chagall (signed lower right margin)','','katalog B082; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8235, IMG_8236; A pencil edition fraction in the lower left margin is illegible at this resolution, so the ''112/500'' comes from the certificate rather than the sheet. The signature is legible as ''Marc Chagall'' but whether it is autograph or a printed facsimile cannot be judged behind glass. The certificate title ''Blue Bouquet'' does not describe the predominantly pink and orange bouquet shown.','Certificate of Authenticity from Donnelly Galleries, Bank of America Building, 2000 E. Lamar Blvd, Suite 600, Arlington, Texas 76006, certifying that the lithograph entitled ''Blue Bouquet'' by Marc Chagall is a limited edition lithograph and is number 112 in an edition of 500; dated Oct 10, 2001.','IMG_8232',29.9,42.3,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life", "animal"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Gray", "Black", "Orange", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(266,'ilan-266','tablo','yayinda','Chagall Exodus Moses Sees His People Suffer, MARC CHAGALL, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 2014','MARC CHAGALL. A crowded biblical scene rendered in washy, luminous colour: the bearded head of Moses looms at the lower left in blue-black, while above and to the right a press of small figures in brown, indigo and violet climbs across a field of hot cadmium yellow and rust red. The drawing is loose and brushy with pooled watercolour-like edges, printed on heavy cream paper with full margins. It is presented on a wide cream mat with a gold fillet, in a broad water-gilt frame under glass. Medium: photomechanical colour graphic (offset lithograph) on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, reading "Marc Chagall". Edition: 500 ARABIC, 500 INTERNATIONAL INTERPRETATIONS OF CHAGALL WITH INTERPRETIVE SIGNATURES; Edition Number left blank. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity for ''EXODUS - MOSES SEES THE SUFFERING OF HIS PEOPLE''; Artist: MARC CHAGALL; Medium: PHOTOMECHANICAL GRAPHIC; Year: 2004; Edition Size: 500 ARABIC, 500 INTERNATIONAL INTERPRETATIONS OF CHAGALL WITH INTERPRETIVE SIGNATURES; Publisher: REA PRODUCTIONS; Atelier: ART LITHO; Fate of The Plate: DESTROYED; Edition Number: (blank); dated OCTOBER 16 2014. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Marc Chagall (signed lower right of the sheet). Condition: Certificate housed in a punched plastic sleeve, lightly creased. Print clean with bright colour; some glass glare.','MARC CHAGALL','EXODUS - MOSES SEES THE SUFFERING OF HIS PEOPLE','published 2004, certified 2014','photomechanical colour graphic (offset lithograph) on paper','500 ARABIC, 500 INTERNATIONAL INTERPRETATIONS OF CHAGALL WITH INTERPRETIVE SIGNATURES; Edition Number left blank','','','Marc Chagall (signed lower right of the sheet)','','katalog B083; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8240, IMG_8241, IMG_8242; The certificate explicitly describes the piece as a photomechanical graphic with an ''interpretive signature'', so the ''Marc Chagall'' on the sheet is very likely printed rather than autograph. The certificate''s Edition Number field was left blank, so no individual number can be given.','Certificate of Authenticity for ''EXODUS - MOSES SEES THE SUFFERING OF HIS PEOPLE''; Artist: MARC CHAGALL; Medium: PHOTOMECHANICAL GRAPHIC; Year: 2004; Edition Size: 500 ARABIC, 500 INTERNATIONAL INTERPRETATIONS OF CHAGALL WITH INTERPRETIVE SIGNATURES; Publisher: REA PRODUCTIONS; Atelier: ART LITHO; Fate of The Plate: DESTROYED; Edition Number: (blank); dated OCTOBER 16 2014.','IMG_8238',30.8,36.4,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["landscape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Yellow", "Orange", "Blue", "Beige"]}'::jsonb),
(267,'ilan-267','tablo','yayinda','Chagall Bouquet of Flowers and Lovers Print, MARC CHAGALL, Signed in the Plate, Framed, 2001','MARC CHAGALL. A tumbling bouquet of white, cream, yellow and blue blossom fills the upper two thirds of the sheet, painted with dense broken impasto-like strokes and set against a burning vermilion ground. A blue horned creature leaps at the upper right above a smouldering village with candles and small figures, while a woman in white reclines along the lower edge beside a blue jug and a dish of fruit. The artist''s name is lettered into the image itself in black block capitals. Presented on a cream mat with a dark inner band, in a gold moulded frame under glass. Medium: photomechanical colour graphic (offset lithograph) on paper. Signed lower right margin, with a printed name also inside the image, reading "Marc Chagall". Edition: 500 ARABIC, 500 ROMAN NUMERAL ALL WITH FACSIMILE SIGNATURE. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity for ''BOUQUET DE FLEURS ET AMANTS'' by MARC CHAGALL; Medium: PHOTOMECHANICAL GRAPHIC; Year Of Publication: 2000; Edition Size: 500 ARABIC, 500 ROMAN NUMERAL ALL WITH FACSIMILE SIGNATURE; Publisher: REA PRODUCTIONS; Atelier: ART WORLD; Fate of the Plate: DESTROYED; Edition No. left blank; Date August 7, 2001. The certificate is photographed as IMG_8250 in listing B085. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: MARC CHAGALL (printed in black block capitals within the image, lower centre); Marc Chagall (lower right margin). Condition: Glass glare in the photographs; sheet clean with no foxing or tears.','MARC CHAGALL','BOUQUET DE FLEURS ET AMANTS','published 2000, certified 2001','photomechanical colour graphic (offset lithograph) on paper','500 ARABIC, 500 ROMAN NUMERAL ALL WITH FACSIMILE SIGNATURE','','','MARC CHAGALL (printed in black block capitals within the image, lower centre); Marc Chagall (lower right margin)','','katalog B084; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8248; The certificate for this work (IMG_8250) and a second tape shot (IMG_8249) were photographed under listing B085 rather than here, so the two listings'' frames are mixed. The certificate states the whole edition carries a facsimile signature, so the margin signature is not autograph. A pencil fraction in the lower left margin is illegible.','Certificate of Authenticity for ''BOUQUET DE FLEURS ET AMANTS'' by MARC CHAGALL; Medium: PHOTOMECHANICAL GRAPHIC; Year Of Publication: 2000; Edition Size: 500 ARABIC, 500 ROMAN NUMERAL ALL WITH FACSIMILE SIGNATURE; Publisher: REA PRODUCTIONS; Atelier: ART WORLD; Fate of the Plate: DESTROYED; Edition No. left blank; Date August 7, 2001. The certificate is photographed as IMG_8250 in listing B085.','IMG_8245',NULL,NULL,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life", "figurative", "document"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "21st", "color": ["Red", "White", "Blue", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(268,'ilan-268','tablo','yayinda','Tarkay Nude with Flowers Signed Lithograph, Numbered Edition, Framed, 1993','TARKAY. A softly drawn nude sits in profile at the left, her body outlined in fine pen and filled with pale flesh and lemon washes, while behind and above her a mass of dove-blue, aubergine and olive blossoms opens across the sheet. The colour is applied in flat translucent shapes with hard edges typical of a lithographic separation, over a warm white deckle-edged paper. It is presented on a wide cream mat with pale blue and navy inner bands, in a mottled silver-white frame with a gold inner lip. Medium: colour lithograph on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet. Edition: 105/400. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity no. 227: TITLE NUDE WITH FLOWERS; ARTIST TARKAY; LITHOGRAPH WITH BOOK; SIGNED AND NUMBERED; AUTHENTICATED BY: CORNELL GABOS; Renaissance Fine Arts, 2184 Warrensville Road, University Hts., Ohio 44118, (216) 371-1230; dated 05/03/93. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 105/400 (pencil, lower left of the sheet). Condition: Glass glare and dust specks in the photographs; sheet clean and bright, certificate sleeved and lightly taped.','TARKAY','NUDE WITH FLOWERS','certified 1993','colour lithograph on paper','105/400','','Renaissance Fine Arts','105/400 (pencil, lower left of the sheet)','','katalog B085; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8249, IMG_8254, IMG_8255; Two frames in this photo group belong to a different work: IMG_8250 is the certificate for the Chagall ''Bouquet de Fleurs et Amants'' of listing B084, and IMG_8249 is a tape shot across that same gold-framed Chagall. The pencil signature at the lower right of the Tarkay sheet is legible only as an initial ''T'' with a trailing flourish, so it is not transcribed; the certificate names the artist as TARKAY.','Certificate of Authenticity no. 227: TITLE NUDE WITH FLOWERS; ARTIST TARKAY; LITHOGRAPH WITH BOOK; SIGNED AND NUMBERED; AUTHENTICATED BY: CORNELL GABOS; Renaissance Fine Arts, 2184 Warrensville Road, University Hts., Ohio 44118, (216) 371-1230; dated 05/03/93.','IMG_8251',21.0,25.2,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["nude", "still-life", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["contemporary", "modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Beige", "Blue", "Purple", "Yellow"]}'::jsonb),
(269,'ilan-269','tablo','yayinda','Chagall Bella Offset Lithograph 50/500, CHAGALL, MARC, Numbered Edition, Framed','CHAGALL, MARC. A pale, dreaming female figure stands centrally holding a great bouquet of cream and gold flowers, her head tilted against a blue-black night window. To the right a flat scarlet animal head and a dark horse shape push into the picture, while at the left a clock face and a candelabra glimmer out of a warm brown ground. Below her, two shallow bowls heaped with gold and russet blossom close the composition. The sheet has full margins on a cream mat with a gold fillet, in a heavily carved and gilded frame under glass. Medium: offset lithograph on paper. Signed lower right of the sheet, reading "Marc Chagall". Edition: 50/500. Accompanied by a certificate: Certificate of Authenticity: Artwork by CHAGALL, MARC; Registration No. 301034; titled BELLA; is an artists OFFSET LITHOGRAPH; is an edition of 50/500; ''This piece is unconditionally guaranteed as to its authenticity.'' Fine Art Wholesalers Inc., 1410 S W 39th Avenue, Pompano Beach, Fl 33069, signed by the President. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: Marc Chagall (lower right of the sheet). Condition: Certificate is creased and lightly toned. Print clean; strong glass glare in the straight-on views.','CHAGALL, MARC','BELLA','late 20th century','offset lithograph on paper','50/500','','Fine Art Wholesalers Inc.','Marc Chagall (lower right of the sheet)','','katalog B086; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8261, IMG_8262; The president''s signature on the certificate is not legible and is not transcribed. Whether the pencil-toned ''Marc Chagall'' on the sheet is autograph or printed cannot be judged behind glass, and an offset edition of 500 would normally carry a plate signature.','Certificate of Authenticity: Artwork by CHAGALL, MARC; Registration No. 301034; titled BELLA; is an artists OFFSET LITHOGRAPH; is an edition of 50/500; ''This piece is unconditionally guaranteed as to its authenticity.'' Fine Art Wholesalers Inc., 1410 S W 39th Avenue, Pompano Beach, Fl 33069, signed by the President.','IMG_8258',33.9,42.3,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["architecture", "still-life", "animal", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["modern"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Blue", "Beige", "Gold", "Red"]}'::jsonb),
(270,'ilan-270','tablo','yayinda','Surrealist Sailboat and Yellow Sun Etching, Numbered Edition, Framed','A spare, elegant surrealist composition: a pale oval like an eggshell or a sail dominates the sheet, holding a small yellow-sailed boat afloat on a scribble of blue water, while a fan of fine ink lines shoots from a scribbled black-and-gold sun at the upper right. Along the lower edge, minute attenuated figures in ink and yellow wash dance and gesture across an empty plain, casting long shadows. The palette is limited to lemon yellow, warm grey and black on cream wove paper. Framed with a pale grey slip on a large butter-yellow mat in a dark walnut moulding under glass. Medium: etching with hand or stencil colour on paper. Edition: 151/200. Inscribed on the reverse or mount: 151/200 (pencil, written as a stacked fraction, lower left of the sheet). Condition: Several strong glass reflections across the sheet; paper appears clean with no foxing or toning.','','','second half of the 20th century','etching with hand or stencil colour on paper','151/200','','','151/200 (pencil, written as a stacked fraction, lower left of the sheet)','','katalog B087; olcu kareleri galeride degil: IMG_8268, IMG_8269; No signature is visible anywhere on the exposed sheet; the pointed mark at the lower right that resembles a monogram is part of the drawn composition. The style strongly suggests Salvador Dali but no attribution is asserted because nothing is inscribed. Whether the technique is etching, lithography or a mixed process cannot be determined behind glass, and the yellow may be stencil (pochoir) rather than hand-applied.','No certificate photographed.','IMG_8264',24.0,32.8,'outside of frame',NULL,'USD',true,'{"subject": ["seascape", "figurative"], "medium": ["print", "paper"], "style": ["surrealist"], "framing": ["framed"], "period": "20th", "color": ["Yellow", "Beige", "Black", "Gray"]}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT (no) DO NOTHING;

